HEY, IT'S HARRY CONNICK JR.

228
00:09:09,333 --> 00:09:10,433
HMM?

229
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:12,000
YOU KNOW YOU WON'T SEE
COSTUMING LIKE THIS

230
00:09:12,067 --> 00:09:13,633
UNTIL MARC SINGER DOES V.

231
00:09:13,700 --> 00:09:16,100
OR THOMAS PYNCHON
DOES V.

232
00:09:16,167 --> 00:09:19,400
♪♪

233
00:09:19,467 --> 00:09:23,133
I WILL PET HIM AND KEEP HIM
AND CALL HIM GEORGE.

234
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:24,600
IT'S VERY SAD, REALLY.

235
00:09:24,667 --> 00:09:26,900
YEAH.

236
00:09:26,967 --> 00:09:29,933
HMM, ARE YOU HUNGRY?

237
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,700
STAY.

238
00:09:31,767 --> 00:09:32,700
[ELECTRONIC BEEPING]

239
00:09:32,767 --> 00:09:34,467
OH, OKAY,
WHOSE BEEPER IS THAT?

240
00:09:34,533 --> 00:09:38,267
[BEEPING]

241
00:09:38,333 --> 00:09:40,700
NOW, I'VE GOT EVERY SHADE
FOR EVERY COMPLEXION.

242
00:09:40,767 --> 00:09:42,000
♪♪

243
00:09:42,067 --> 00:09:45,433
I SEE YOU HAVE A MACHINE
THAT GOES "PING."

244
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:46,900
HUH?

245
00:09:46,967 --> 00:09:47,900
WHAT?

246
00:09:47,967 --> 00:09:49,967
OH.

247
00:09:50,033 --> 00:09:52,333
IT'S A MULTICHANNEL MIXER!

248
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:54,767
IT SAYS SO!

249
00:09:54,833 --> 00:09:56,500
REPORT PRELIMINARY FINDINGS.

250
00:09:56,567 --> 00:09:57,500
THOR REPORTING.

251
00:09:57,567 --> 00:09:58,533
I'VE TAKEN MY PILL, SIR.

252
00:09:58,600 --> 00:10:00,733
42 SATURATION DEGREES
AND 96 VOLUMES.

253
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:01,867
OF BEER ON THE WALL.

254
00:10:01,933 --> 00:10:03,300
INTERMEDIATE FLUCTUATION
IN MARPHON CONTENT.

255
00:10:03,367 --> 00:10:04,300
DEREK REPORTING.

256
00:10:04,367 --> 00:10:05,600
HI, DEREK.

257
00:10:05,667 --> 00:10:08,800
TRIDEX MIXER COMPONENTS RATIO
EXCEEDING 7 TO 1.4.

258
00:10:08,867 --> 00:10:10,600
MOREAL REPORTING.

259
00:10:10,667 --> 00:10:15,667
DIAGONAL ADJUSTMENT READING
RESISTING STRUCTURAL FORMS
BY 2.8.0 VERNAMS.

260
00:10:15,733 --> 00:10:17,100
SAUL REPORTING.

261
00:10:17,167 --> 00:10:18,400
DOG GONE.
[LAUGHS]

262
00:10:18,467 --> 00:10:21,467
UNEVEN CARTOID LEVELS
INTERSECT PLAINS BELOW .03.

263
00:10:21,533 --> 00:10:26,667
♪ SHANNON IS GONE,
THEY SAY SHE DRIFTED
OFF TO... ♪

264
00:10:26,733 --> 00:10:28,767
DRY AS A BONE, HUH?
HEH!

265
00:10:28,833 --> 00:10:31,467
HEY, I THINK I FOUND
THE TOP OF YOUR THERMOS.

266
00:10:31,533 --> 00:10:34,567
SURFACE READINGS REGISTER
ABOVE MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS.

267
00:10:34,633 --> 00:10:36,633
MOREAL!

268
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:39,267
GO BELOW AND BRING UP
THE YOUNG GARGON SPECIMEN.

269
00:10:39,333 --> 00:10:40,433
BUH-BUH.

270
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:42,933
NOW THE DECISION DEPENDS
ON ITS REACTIONS.

271
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,367
WAIT, CAPTAIN.

272
00:10:44,433 --> 00:10:47,200
I HAVE FOUND EVIDENCE OF
INTELLIGENT BEINGS
ON THIS PLANET.

273
00:10:47,267 --> 00:10:49,500
OF WHAT CONCERN
ARE FOREIGN BEINGS?

274
00:10:49,567 --> 00:10:50,667
OF NONE TO YOU, THOR.

275
00:10:50,733 --> 00:10:52,433
CAT FIGHT.
[HISSES]

276
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:55,867
JUST AS YOU WERE SO
UNCONCERNED WHEN YOU
DESTROYED THIS SMALL CREATURE.

277
00:10:55,933 --> 00:10:57,000
WOOF.

278
00:10:57,067 --> 00:10:58,500
SO BRAVELY.

279
00:10:58,567 --> 00:11:00,367
IT WAS NO MORE
THAN AN INSECT.

280
00:11:00,433 --> 00:11:04,033
BUT IT HAD LIFE,
AND THAT LIFE YOU HAD TO TAKE

281
00:11:04,100 --> 00:11:07,000
TO SATISFY YOUR ENDLESS
HUNGER FOR KILLING.

282
00:11:07,067 --> 00:11:08,867
SILENCE, BOTH OF YOU!

283
00:11:08,933 --> 00:11:10,100
HE STARTED IT!

284
00:11:10,167 --> 00:11:12,333
PROCEED.
BRING THE GARGON.

285
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:14,967
THAT WILL NOT BE NECESSARY,
CAPTAIN.

286
00:11:15,033 --> 00:11:18,067
MRS. CARMICHAEL,
PUT THAT LASER DOWN.

287
00:11:18,133 --> 00:11:21,500
CONDITIONS HERE WILL BE
REPORTED AS UNSATISFACTORY,

288
00:11:21,567 --> 00:11:24,133
AS THEY WERE ON THE OTHER
PLANETS WE HAVE CHARTED.

289
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:25,300
BY WHAT AUTHORITY--

290
00:11:25,367 --> 00:11:27,400
YOU WILL PREPARE
FOR TAKEOFF!

291
00:11:27,467 --> 00:11:29,500
THE SHIP WILL LEAVE
THIS PLANET IMMEDIATELY.

292
00:11:29,567 --> 00:11:31,100
ACCORDING TO OUR CODE OF
OPERATIONS--

293
00:11:31,167 --> 00:11:33,033
YOU MAY FORGET THE CODE OF
OPERATIONS, CAPTAIN!

294
00:11:33,100 --> 00:11:34,867
I'M THE CODE
OF OPERATIONS NOW!

295
00:11:34,933 --> 00:11:38,200
ONLY CIVILIZED BEINGS COULD
HAVE MADE THE INSCRIPTION
ON THIS METAL PIECE.

296
00:11:38,267 --> 00:11:42,433
WE SHALL NOT HAVE THE THOUSANDS
OF GARGONS BROUGHT HERE
TO DESTROY THEM.

297
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:45,833
YOU HAVE CONCERN FOR FOREIGN
BEINGS OVER OUR MISSION

298
00:11:45,900 --> 00:11:47,700
TO LOCATE GRAZING LAND
FOR OUR GARGON HERDS?

299
00:11:47,767 --> 00:11:48,700
YEP.

300
00:11:48,767 --> 00:11:50,200
THANK YOU,
CAPTAIN EXPOSITION.

301
00:11:50,267 --> 00:11:53,633
RECALL. IT IS NECESSARY
AS A RESERVE FOOD SUPPLY
FOR OUR PEOPLE.

302
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:56,767
OUR PEOPLE?
WE LIVE LIKE PARTS
OF A MACHINE.

303
00:11:56,833 --> 00:11:59,633
WE DON'T KNOW OUR
FATHERS OR MOTHERS.
WE'RE RAISED IN CUBICLES.

304
00:11:59,700 --> 00:12:01,600
THE SICK AND THE OLD
ARE PUT TO DEATH.

305
00:12:01,667 --> 00:12:07,433
IT IS THE ONE AND ONLY WAY TO
MAINTAIN THE SUPREME RACE.
HAVE YOU FORGOTTEN THAT--

306
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:09,267
OUR PEOPLE HAVE FORGOTTEN.

307
00:12:09,333 --> 00:12:10,467
UH, MAYBE YOU SHOULD HAVE
BROUGHT THIS UP IN GROUP.

308
00:12:10,533 --> 00:12:13,567
THEY HAVE BEEN MADE TO FORGET
FOR CENTURIES.

309
00:12:13,633 --> 00:12:16,533
BUT I HAVE
LEARNED HOW IT ONCE WAS.

310
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:19,733
FAMILIES...
BROTHERS AND SISTERS.

311
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:22,567
THERE WAS HAPPINESS.
THERE WAS LOVE.

312
00:12:22,633 --> 00:12:23,833
OH, BITE ME,
THERE WAS NOT.

313
00:12:23,900 --> 00:12:25,067
OF WHAT DO YOU SPEAK?

314
00:12:25,133 --> 00:12:27,233
FROM WHERE HAVE YOU
LEARNED SUCH THINGS?

315
00:12:27,300 --> 00:12:30,767
I HAVE READ.
I HAVE READ FROM THIS BOOK.

316
00:12:30,833 --> 00:12:31,833
OH, A SEPARATE PEACE.

317
00:12:31,900 --> 00:12:33,233
I DISCOVERED IT
AND KEPT IT HIDDEN.

318
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:34,967
HE'S GOT THE BOOK.

319
00:12:35,033 --> 00:12:36,833
SOMEHOW IT SURVIVED THE FLAMES
OF THE ANNIHILATORS

320
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:41,833
WHEN OUR PEOPLE WERE TURNED
INTO MECHANIZED SLAVES
CENTURIES AGO.

321
00:12:41,900 --> 00:12:46,700
WHEN WE RETURN TO OUR PLANET,
THE HIGH COURT MAY WELL
SENTENCE YOU TO TORTURE...

322
00:12:46,767 --> 00:12:47,733
TORTURE!

323
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:48,733
AND DEATH FOR THIS TREASON.

324
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:49,933
THE HIGH COURT MAY JUDGE ME

325
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,467
AFTER WE HAVE ACCOMPLISHED
OUR MISSION.

326
00:12:51,533 --> 00:12:53,733
BUT THE COURT OF EARTHEN BEAUTY
WILL BACK ME ALL THE WAY!

327
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:57,733
WE WILL FIND AN UNINHIBITED
PLANET TO WHICH THE HERDS
OF GARGONS MAY BE SHIPPED,

328
00:12:57,800 --> 00:13:00,900
WITHOUT ENDANGERING
CIVILIZED BEINGS.

329
00:13:00,967 --> 00:13:02,667
LET ME SEE THAT BOOK.

330
00:13:02,733 --> 00:13:05,867
I THINK WHAT OUR BRIGHT
YOUNG FRIEND IS TRYING
TO TELL US IS...

331
00:13:05,933 --> 00:13:07,867
I AM INTERESTED TO SEE WHAT
SWAYS YOUR MIND SO HEAVILY.

332
00:13:07,933 --> 00:13:09,433
♪♪

333
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:11,233
YOU MAY HAVE IT.

334
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:12,900
IT'S CALLED IRON JOHN.

335
00:13:12,967 --> 00:13:16,600
♪ DAH DAH DAH DAH DAH
DAH DAH DAH DAH ♪

336
00:13:16,667 --> 00:13:18,100
BRING UP THE GARGON.

337
00:13:18,167 --> 00:13:19,400
I'LL NEED AN IPECAC.

338
00:13:19,467 --> 00:13:22,100
YOU ARE A FOOL, DEREK.

339
00:13:22,167 --> 00:13:25,200
THIS BOOK HAS POISONED
YOUR MIND, AND YOU SHALL
SUFFER FOR IT.

340
00:13:25,267 --> 00:13:30,567
CAPTAIN, IF THE GARGONS ARE
SHIPPED HERE, THE INHABITANTS
MAY DESTROY THEM.

341
00:13:30,633 --> 00:13:34,600
THAT POSSIBILITY ALONE
MAKES IT WORTHWHILE TO LOCATE
AN UNINHABITED PLANET.

342
00:13:34,667 --> 00:13:36,833
HE CERTAINLY IS
A WHISPER-THIN LAD, ISN'T HE?

343
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:39,533
THAT BOOK HAS INDEED
MADE YOU FORGET MANY THINGS.

344
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:44,200
WE ARE THE SUPREME RACE.
WE HAVE THE SUPREME WEAPONS.

345
00:13:44,267 --> 00:13:46,067
WE HAVE
THE SUPREME PIZZAS!

346
00:13:46,133 --> 00:13:48,300
KEEP HIM UNDER GUARD, THOR.

347
00:13:48,367 --> 00:13:50,900
I WILL STUDY THE REACTIONS
OF THE YOUNG GARGON.

348
00:13:50,967 --> 00:13:54,133
I HATE HIM, I HATE HIM,
I HATE HIM!

349
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:56,100
♪♪

350
00:13:56,167 --> 00:13:58,700
NOW, I LIKE YOU, TREVOR,
BUT YOU'RE SCREWY,
YOU GOT IT?

351
00:13:58,767 --> 00:14:00,433
I'M THE FELLOW WEARING
THE ROSCOE, SEE?

352
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:02,100
I LIKE DAMES
BUT THEY DON'T LIKE ME.

353
00:14:02,167 --> 00:14:05,533
BEFORE THE HIGH COURT
HAS YOU EXECUTED,

354
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:07,600
YOU SHOULD BE MADE TO
WATCH WHAT HAPPENS

355
00:14:07,667 --> 00:14:10,000
WHEN WE RETURN HERE
WITH THE GARGONS.

356
00:14:10,067 --> 00:14:14,433
BY THE ELEMENTS ALONE,
THEY WILL GROW TO MILLIONS OF
TIMES THEIR ORIGINAL SIZE

357
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:19,133
IN LESS TIME THAN IT TAKES
FOR THE SUN TO RISE AND FALL.

358
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:20,867
YOU MEAN A DAY?

359
00:14:20,933 --> 00:14:21,867
IT THRIVES, CAPTAIN.

360
00:14:21,933 --> 00:14:23,033
♪˯ THRIVE, CAPTAIN,
THRIVE ♪

361
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:24,700
ALREADY, I CAN FEEL
IT HAS GROWN HEAVIER.

362
00:14:24,767 --> 00:14:28,367
WE SHOULD RETURN TO
OUR BASE AND LEAD
THE TRANSPORT SHIPS HERE.

363
00:14:28,433 --> 00:14:32,433
SOON THIS PLANET
WILL BE COVERED WITH
FULL-GROWN GARGONS.

364
00:14:32,500 --> 00:14:33,433
AND I WILL RULE THE WORLD!

365
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:35,467
A SAFE DISTANCE
FROM OUR PLANET,

366
00:14:35,533 --> 00:14:39,100
YET THEIR MEAT WILL BE
AVAILABLE TO US
FOR THE HARVESTING.

367
00:14:39,167 --> 00:14:41,333
REPACK THE INSTRUMENTS.

368
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:44,333
I SHALL RADIO BACK
THE NEWS OF OUR SUCCESS.

369
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:47,067
DEREK,
THE SENSITIVE SPACE MAN.

370
00:14:47,133 --> 00:14:49,267
♪♪

371
00:14:49,333 --> 00:14:50,867
YOU'LL PAY FOR THIS!

372
00:14:50,933 --> 00:14:53,033
CAPTAIN! CAPTAIN,
SOMETHING HAS GONE WRONG.

373
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:54,967
AW, CRIMINY, WHAT NOW?
WHAT?

374
00:14:55,033 --> 00:14:55,967
WHAT HAS HAPPENED?

375
00:14:56,033 --> 00:14:57,800
I DO NOT KNOW.

376
00:14:57,867 --> 00:15:00,933
IT SUDDENLY FELL LIMP
AND NOW DOES NOT MOVE.

377
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,433
PULL MY FINGER!

378
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:03,733
ASSEMBLE THE T-RESSES.
HOOK IN THE GAS GRADING
INSTRUMENTS.

379
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:04,833
BE QUICK!

380
00:15:04,900 --> 00:15:07,433
KWI KWAG?

381
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:10,000
HEY, MAYBE YOU SHOULDN'T HAVE
PUT HIM IN A SNARE DRUM.

382
00:15:10,067 --> 00:15:12,500
MM-MMM.

383
00:15:12,567 --> 00:15:14,300
OH, THEY'RE GONNA
GET HIM CABLE!

384
00:15:14,367 --> 00:15:16,700
OH!

385
00:15:16,767 --> 00:15:19,100
PETER AND ANNETTE
HAD ONE OF THOSE.

386
00:15:19,167 --> 00:15:21,100
♪♪

387
00:15:21,167 --> 00:15:23,867
THE ATMOSPHERE HERE
TESTED ABOVE MINIMUM...

388
00:15:23,933 --> 00:15:25,067
WAGE.

389
00:15:25,133 --> 00:15:27,967
BUT THE GARGON SPECIES
CANNOT LIVE

390
00:15:28,033 --> 00:15:33,267
DUE TO EXCESSIVE NITROGENIC
GAS COMPOUNDS EMITTED IN OUR
PRELIMINARY DIAGNOSIS.

391
00:15:33,333 --> 00:15:34,633
TRY SAYING THAT
THREE TIMES FAST.

392
00:15:34,700 --> 00:15:36,867
THEN THIS PLANET WILL BE
REPORTED AS UNSUITABLE?

393
00:15:36,933 --> 00:15:38,533
OH, YOU'D LIKE THAT,
WOULDN'T YOU?

394
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:41,200
REPACK THE INSTRUMENTS
AND PREPARE FOR TAKEOFF.

395
00:15:41,267 --> 00:15:42,533
THIS BITES!

396
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:45,100
WE WILL CONTINUE OUR SEARCH
IN ANOTHER SOLAR SYSTEM.

397
00:15:45,167 --> 00:15:46,500
YES, YES, YES!

398
00:15:46,567 --> 00:15:48,233
AND WHEN WE RETURN
TO OUR HOME BASE,

399
00:15:48,300 --> 00:15:50,733
YOU WILL BE PRESENTED TO THE
HIGH COURT WITH THE EVIDENCE
AGAINST YOU.

400
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:51,733
TORTURE!

401
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:52,733
THOR, SAUL...

402
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:54,333
MORT SAHL?

403
00:15:54,400 --> 00:15:56,767
BIND THE PRISONER
AND PREPARE HIM FOR
THE ISOLATION CHAMBER.

404
00:15:56,833 --> 00:15:57,833
WHAT'S THE QUESTION?

405
00:15:57,900 --> 00:15:59,000
I WILL MAKE CONTACT
WITH BASE.

406
00:15:59,067 --> 00:16:00,133
OKAY.

407
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:04,667
♪♪

408
00:16:06,733 --> 00:16:07,900
HE IS ESCAPING!

409
00:16:07,967 --> 00:16:09,733
OH, GOTTA GO.
BE BACK.

410
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:10,967
♪♪

411
00:16:11,033 --> 00:16:12,467
NO, THOR!

412
00:16:12,533 --> 00:16:18,067
MOSES? MOSES!

413
00:16:18,133 --> 00:16:19,867
HOW DID HE GET FREE?

414
00:16:19,933 --> 00:16:21,633
HE ESCAPED FROM SAUL.

415
00:16:21,700 --> 00:16:23,400
I COULD HAVE STOPPED HIM.

416
00:16:23,467 --> 00:16:26,433
DEREK IS TO BE
BROUGHT BACK ALIVE.

417
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:28,767
HE'S THE SON OF OUR LEADER.

418
00:16:28,833 --> 00:16:30,000
DEREK?

419
00:16:30,067 --> 00:16:31,400
I REPORTED HIS ACTIONS

420
00:16:31,467 --> 00:16:33,033
AND WAS CONNECTED
WITH THE LEADER HIMSELF.

421
00:16:33,100 --> 00:16:34,167
A REAL NICE GUY.

422
00:16:34,233 --> 00:16:35,467
HE TOLD ME THIS.

423
00:16:35,533 --> 00:16:37,467
HE SAID DEREK DOES NOT KNOW.

424
00:16:37,533 --> 00:16:39,933
AS THE SON OF OUR LEADER,
THE HIGH COURT WILL PARDON HIM.

425
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:40,933
OH, YEAH,
HE'S A KENNEDY.

426
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:41,933
HE WILL BE PARDONED.

427
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,233
OH, YEAH.

428
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:44,967
WHEN THE SKY IS LIGHT,
WE WILL BEGIN TO SEARCH FOR HIM.

429
00:16:45,033 --> 00:16:46,267
WHAT? IT IS LIGHT.

430
00:16:46,333 --> 00:16:50,733
CAPTAIN, LOOK AT THIS.
THE GARGON, IT IS NOT DEAD.

431
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:53,033
I'M NOT DEAD.
I'M GETTING BETTER.

432
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:54,900
IT HAS REVIVED.

433
00:16:54,967 --> 00:16:56,900
IT FLOURISHES.

434
00:16:56,967 --> 00:17:01,433
THE EXCESSIVE NITROGENIC GAS
COMPOUNDS SHOCKED ITS SYSTEM.

435
00:17:01,500 --> 00:17:04,600
NOW IT THRIVES
ON THE VERY SAME COMPOUNDS.

436
00:17:04,667 --> 00:17:06,000
THEN THIS PLANET
IS SUITABLE.

437
00:17:06,067 --> 00:17:07,633
COMPLETELY.

438
00:17:07,700 --> 00:17:09,567
I MUST RESUME
RADIOVISION CONTACT.

439
00:17:09,633 --> 00:17:11,033
PULL MY FINGER,
PULL MY FINGER.

440
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:14,667
MOREAL, SAUL,
SECURE THE GARGON
BY EXPANDABLE LEG BANDS.

441
00:17:14,733 --> 00:17:17,667
EXPANDABLE LEG BANDS?
YES, SIR!

442
00:17:17,733 --> 00:17:20,367
THE SIZE IT ATTAINS
BY THE TIME WE RETURN

443
00:17:20,433 --> 00:17:25,033
WILL GIVE US AN EXACT GROWTH
RATE TO EXPECT OF THE HERDS.

444
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:27,367
HOW MUCH ARE YOU GETTING PAID,
PHIL? MIND MY ASKING?

445
00:17:27,433 --> 00:17:30,267
AT THE RATE THE GARGON
IS EXPECTED TO GROW,
WHAT WILL PREVENT IT

446
00:17:30,333 --> 00:17:33,267
FROM TEARING LOOSE
THE LEG BANDS AND ESCAPING
FROM THE CAVE?

447
00:17:33,333 --> 00:17:34,400
SHUT UP, GOMER.

448
00:17:34,467 --> 00:17:36,167
WE SHALL BE BACK
BEFORE THAT HAPPENS,

449
00:17:36,233 --> 00:17:40,233
UNLESS IT SHOULD RECEIVE
FOOD IN EXCESS OF THE
ATMOSPHERIC ELEMENTS.

450
00:17:40,300 --> 00:17:42,633
WE WILL LEAVE NOTHING ELSE
FOR IT TO CONSUME.

451
00:17:42,700 --> 00:17:44,533
OH, YOU'VE REALLY RELIEVED ME.
THANKS LOADS.

452
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:47,800
IMAGINE...THOUSANDS
OF BEASTS LIKE THAT.

453
00:17:47,867 --> 00:17:50,100
KEEP ME MOIST!
I SHOULD BE IN WATER!

454
00:17:50,167 --> 00:17:51,933
MILLIONS OF TIMES ENLARGED,
ROAMING OVER THIS PLANET.

455
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,100
THEY WILL BE HARVESTED
FROM THE AIR,

456
00:17:54,167 --> 00:17:56,633
SO THERE WILL BE
NO DANGER TO US.

457
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:59,600
LET US BE QUICK.
I DO NOT LIKE TO LOOK UPON IT.

458
00:17:59,667 --> 00:18:01,667
LET US IMPLEMENT
CONTRACTIONS.

459
00:18:01,733 --> 00:18:05,767
♪♪

460
00:18:05,833 --> 00:18:08,133
BOO!

461
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:11,100
NOW THAT YOU REPORT THE PLANET
IS SUITABLE FOR OUR PURPOSES,

462
00:18:11,167 --> 00:18:13,067
YOU ARE TO RETURN HERE
IMMEDIATELY

463
00:18:13,133 --> 00:18:15,200
AND PREPARE TO LEAD THE
TRANSPORT SHIPS THERE.

464
00:18:15,267 --> 00:18:16,833
BUT, SIR,
YOU'RE A HAND PUPPET.

465
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:18,033
DEREK'S ESCAPE
COULD NOW MEAN DIFFICULTY

466
00:18:18,100 --> 00:18:19,467
IN OUR OPERATION,
SHOULD HE COMMUNICATE

467
00:18:19,533 --> 00:18:22,800
IN ANY WAY WITH THE INHABITANTS,
INFERIOR THOUGH THEY MAY BE.

468
00:18:22,867 --> 00:18:26,033
IF WE ARE TO RETURN NOW,
HOW CAN HE BE STOPPED?

469
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:27,067
OVER!

470
00:18:27,133 --> 00:18:28,300
LEAVE YOUR BEST MAN
TO FIND DEREK

471
00:18:28,367 --> 00:18:30,167
AND INFORM HIM HE IS MY SON.

472
00:18:30,233 --> 00:18:32,900
I WILL JOIN YOU ON THE RETURN
TRIP TO MEET HIM THERE.

473
00:18:32,967 --> 00:18:34,367
HE MAY BE STUBBORN.

474
00:18:34,433 --> 00:18:36,333
HE HAS ALREADY
THREATENED OUR LIVES.

475
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:40,867
IF THAT BECOMES THE CASE,
HE-- HE MUST BE DESTROYED.

476
00:18:40,933 --> 00:18:42,500
WHAT ABOUT TORTURE?

477
00:18:42,567 --> 00:18:44,067
AND ANY BEINGS WITH WHOM HE
MIGHT COMMUNICATE,

478
00:18:44,133 --> 00:18:45,800
THEY MUST BE DESTROYED.

479
00:18:45,867 --> 00:18:47,500
YOUR ORDERS ARE COMPLETE.

480
00:18:47,567 --> 00:18:48,600
OH, WOW.

481
00:18:48,667 --> 00:18:51,167
I SHALL SEND MY BEST MAN.

482
00:18:51,233 --> 00:18:52,667
OH, OH.
[CLEARS THROAT]

483
00:18:52,733 --> 00:18:53,867
[WHISTLES A TUNE]
NOTHING, NOTHING.

484
00:18:53,933 --> 00:18:56,467
I HEARD THE ORDERS,
CAPTAIN.

485
00:18:56,533 --> 00:18:57,967
LET ME...

486
00:18:58,033 --> 00:18:58,967
ENTERTAIN YOU!

487
00:18:59,033 --> 00:19:01,033
FIND DEREK.

488
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:03,700
YOU WILL WAIT UNTIL
THE SKY IS LIGHT ENOUGH
TO BEGIN THE SEARCH.

489
00:19:03,767 --> 00:19:05,500
IT IS LIGHT!

490
00:19:05,567 --> 00:19:09,333
WE WILL LEAVE NOW AND RETURN
HERE TO MEET YOU WHEN
WE BRING THE GARGONS.

491
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:10,867
[CROWS SQUAWKING]

492
00:19:10,933 --> 00:19:12,400
HMM?

493
00:19:12,467 --> 00:19:16,200
GO BACK TO YOUR PLANET,
SPACE TEENS!

494
00:19:16,267 --> 00:19:18,667
DO NOT FAIL, THOR.

495
00:19:18,733 --> 00:19:20,533
I SHALL NOT FAIL.

496
00:19:20,600 --> 00:19:21,700
♪♪

497
00:19:21,767 --> 00:19:23,633
YOU'LL FAIL!
YOU CANNOT BEAT US!

498
00:19:23,700 --> 00:19:25,700
WE'RE THE PEOPLE!
WE'LL POOP ON YOU!

499
00:19:25,767 --> 00:19:28,667
RUN YOUR FASTEST!
JUMP YOUR HIGHEST!

500
00:19:28,733 --> 00:19:33,167
LOOK AT THAT STUPID JUMPSUIT,
BELTED AT THE WAIST.

501
00:19:33,233 --> 00:19:34,600
UH, YOURS IS NICE.

502
00:19:34,667 --> 00:19:36,433
THE LONELINESS
OF THE ALIEN RUNNER.

503
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:38,533
♪♪

504
00:19:38,600 --> 00:19:41,367
LIFE IS SIMPLE HERE
IN GROVER'S CORNER.

505
00:19:41,433 --> 00:19:43,333
♪♪

506
00:19:43,400 --> 00:19:45,300
♪ DOO DOO DOO DOO DOO ♪
GEE, DAVEY.

507
00:19:45,367 --> 00:19:46,800
♪ DOO DOO DOO
DOO DOO DOO DOO ♪

508
00:19:46,867 --> 00:19:48,000
♪♪

509
00:19:48,067 --> 00:19:49,233
♪ DOO DOO DOO
DOO DOO DOO DOO ♪

510
00:19:49,300 --> 00:19:50,400
♪ DOO DOO DOO DOO
DOO DOO DOO ♪

511
00:19:50,467 --> 00:19:51,500
♪ DOO DOO DOO
DOO DOO DOO DOO ♪

512
00:19:51,567 --> 00:19:52,600
AAH!

513
00:19:52,667 --> 00:19:53,700
OH, DON'T DO THAT.

514
00:19:53,767 --> 00:19:55,667
ARE YOU MY DADDY?

515
00:19:55,733 --> 00:19:58,000
♪ DOO DOO DOO
DOO DOO DOO DOO ♪

516
00:19:58,067 --> 00:20:00,800
JIM HENSON'S
BERETTA BABIES.

517
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:02,833
♪♪

518
00:20:02,900 --> 00:20:05,067
LET'S WATCH
AS AN ALIEN VISITS

519
00:20:05,133 --> 00:20:06,500
ONE OF OUR FRIENDLY
TEXACO STATIONS.

520
00:20:06,567 --> 00:20:07,700
♪ DOO DOO DOO
DOO DOO DOO DOO ♪

521
00:20:07,767 --> 00:20:08,833
CAN I HELP YOU, SIR?

522
00:20:08,900 --> 00:20:09,867
YES, I...

523
00:20:09,933 --> 00:20:11,267
FILL HER UP, PLEASE.

524
00:20:11,333 --> 00:20:12,767
WOULD--

525
00:20:12,833 --> 00:20:14,600
WOULD YOU TELL ME
THE MEANING

526
00:20:14,667 --> 00:20:17,633
OF THE INSCRIPTION
ON THIS METAL PIECE?

527
00:20:17,700 --> 00:20:19,033
WHAT DO I LOOK LIKE,
THE SHELL ANSWER MAN?

528
00:20:19,100 --> 00:20:20,233
OH, OH, THAT'S RIGHT,
I AM.

529
00:20:20,300 --> 00:20:23,000
"SPARKY,
1243 WILLOWCREST DRIVE."

530
00:20:23,067 --> 00:20:25,500
THAT'S JUST THREE BLOCKS DOWN
THERE AND A FEW DOORS UP.

531
00:20:25,567 --> 00:20:27,633
YOU CAN'T MISS IT.

532
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:28,833
HMM?

533
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:31,333
DAMN ILLEGAL ALIENS.

534
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:33,867
HEY, WATCH WHAT
YOU'RE DOING THERE.

535
00:20:33,933 --> 00:20:36,167
[GASPS]
SORRY, SENATOR HELMS.

536
00:20:36,233 --> 00:20:39,400
I WAS JUST TRYING TO MAKE OUT
WHAT KIND OF CLOTHES THAT GUY
WAS WEARING.

537
00:20:39,467 --> 00:20:41,967
LOOKS LIKE SOME KIND OF
MILITARY UNIFORM.

538
00:20:42,033 --> 00:20:43,533
WONDER WHERE HE'S FROM.

539
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:45,533
COULD BE FROM MARS,
FOR ALL I CARE.

540
00:20:45,600 --> 00:20:48,533
HURRY UP THERE, BOY, WILL YA?
I HAVEN'T GOT ALL DAY.

541
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:49,800
LIGHT A CIGAR, BUDDY.

542
00:20:49,867 --> 00:20:51,233
♪♪

543
00:20:51,300 --> 00:20:54,200
OH, NO, HE FORGOT TO ASK THE
OTHER PERSON WHAT A BLOCK WAS.

544
00:20:54,267 --> 00:20:56,700
♪♪

545
00:20:56,767 --> 00:20:58,433
HMM?

546
00:20:58,500 --> 00:21:00,933
♪♪

547
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:04,767
EXCUSE ME, IS THAT
A ZANDVELD JUMPSUIT?

548
00:21:04,833 --> 00:21:06,467
HOP IN,
I'LL GIVE YOU A LIFT.

549
00:21:06,533 --> 00:21:07,733
LIFT?

550
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:10,233
WELL, IT'S A LONG WAY
INTO TOWN.

551
00:21:10,300 --> 00:21:11,633
TOWN?

552
00:21:11,700 --> 00:21:13,433
OKAY, IT'S ALL RIGHT
WITH ME IF--

553
00:21:13,500 --> 00:21:15,500
WAIT!

554
00:21:15,567 --> 00:21:18,033
IT'S VINCE SUTTON.
IT'S SERGEANT CARTER!

555
00:21:18,100 --> 00:21:19,933
♪♪

556
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:22,767
I'M LOOKING FOR
SARAH CONNOR.

557
00:21:22,833 --> 00:21:24,433
THEY'RE SCOOCHED, RIGHT?

558
00:21:24,500 --> 00:21:28,667
NEVER SAW A UNIFORM
LIKE THAT BEFORE.

559
00:21:28,733 --> 00:21:30,167
WHAT BRINGS YOU HERE?

560
00:21:30,233 --> 00:21:31,633
THE SUGAR BEET FESTIVAL.
AND YOU?

561
00:21:31,700 --> 00:21:32,933
I AM SEARCHING FOR SOMEONE.

562
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,433
MAYBE I CAN HELP YOU.

563
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:37,400
KNOW A LOT OF FOLKS
AROUND THESE PARTS.

564
00:21:37,467 --> 00:21:39,833
I AM SEARCHING FOR SOMEONE
YOU COULD NOT KNOW.

565
00:21:39,900 --> 00:21:41,000
OH, A RIDDLE, HUH?

566
00:21:41,067 --> 00:21:43,433
ONE OF THEM FUNNY
WORD PUZZLE JOKES.

567
00:21:43,500 --> 00:21:45,333
I LIKE THEM.

568
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:49,633
LEVITTOWN,
COMMUNITY OF THE FUTURE.

569
00:21:49,700 --> 00:21:52,867
THIS LOOKS LIKE A NICE PLACE
TO BRING YOUR KIDS UP.

570
00:21:52,933 --> 00:21:55,667
♪♪

571
00:21:55,733 --> 00:21:57,000
♪ DOO DOO DOO
DOO DOO DOO DOO ♪

572
00:21:57,067 --> 00:21:58,567
"ROOM FOR RENT."

573
00:21:58,633 --> 00:22:01,633
I PUT SPARKY'S BREAKFAST OUT
20 MINUTES AGO, GRANDPA,

574
00:22:01,700 --> 00:22:03,000
AND IT'S STILL HERE.

575
00:22:03,067 --> 00:22:05,900
PROBABLY STILL OUT
CHASING GOPHERS.

576
00:22:05,967 --> 00:22:06,900
SWEET WINONA!

577
00:22:06,967 --> 00:22:07,900
HELLO.

578
00:22:07,967 --> 00:22:08,967
[WOLF WHISTLE]

579
00:22:09,033 --> 00:22:11,633
YOU'VE COME TO SEE
OUR ROOM FOR RENT?

580
00:22:11,700 --> 00:22:12,767
[GRANDPA]
WHAT'S THAT?

581
00:22:12,833 --> 00:22:14,767
A FELLOW TO SEE
THE ROOM FOR RENT, GRANDPA.

582
00:22:14,833 --> 00:22:16,500
YOU SHOW IT HIM, WILL YOU?

583
00:22:16,567 --> 00:22:18,167
JOE WILL BE BY FOR ME
IN A MINUTE.

584
00:22:18,233 --> 00:22:20,900
WE'RE GOING SWIMMING
AT ALICE'S, AND I HAVEN'T
EVEN CHANGED YET.

585
00:22:20,967 --> 00:22:22,000
WHOA!

586
00:22:22,067 --> 00:22:24,933
WAIT, I JUST CAME TO SAY
I KILLED YOUR DOG.

587
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:29,167
YOU'RE HARRY CONNICK,
AREN'T YOU?

588
00:22:29,233 --> 00:22:30,467
HEY.

589
00:22:30,533 --> 00:22:32,633
I'M BETTY MORGAN,
AND THIS IS MY GRANDFATHER.

590
00:22:32,700 --> 00:22:33,800
HOW DO YOU DO, SON?

591
00:22:33,867 --> 00:22:35,633
PULL MY FINGER. HA HA!
YOU CAN'T--I'M KIDDING.

592
00:22:35,700 --> 00:22:37,033
JUST ARRIVED IN TOWN?

593
00:22:37,100 --> 00:22:39,700
DON'T BELIEVE I'VE SEEN YOU
AROUND BEFORE.

594
00:22:39,767 --> 00:22:42,100
I JUST ARRIVED.

595
00:22:42,167 --> 00:22:44,667
AND YOUR NAME?

596
00:22:44,733 --> 00:22:47,167
- DEREK.
- DEREK.

597
00:22:47,233 --> 00:22:48,333
MM-HMM.

598
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:50,567
THE EMPTY ROOM BELONGED
TO MY BROTHER BUD.

599
00:22:50,633 --> 00:22:53,267
HE'S MARRIED NOW
AND LIVES UPSTATE.

600
00:22:53,333 --> 00:22:55,300
YOUR BROTHER?

601
00:22:55,367 --> 00:22:57,733
YOU KNEW YOUR BROTHER?

602
00:22:57,800 --> 00:22:59,800
DID I KNOW MY BROTHER?

603
00:22:59,867 --> 00:23:01,667
THAT'S A STRANGE
QUESTION TO ASK.

604
00:23:01,733 --> 00:23:05,200
GRANDPA RAISED US BOTH
SINCE WE WERE KIDS AFTER
MOM AND DAD DIED.

605
00:23:05,267 --> 00:23:07,067
I'M SORRY, I--

606
00:23:07,133 --> 00:23:09,967
IT'S JUST THAT I NEVER
KNEW ANY BROTHERS OR SISTERS.

607
00:23:10,033 --> 00:23:12,867
[CHUCKLES]
YOUR MOTHER AND FATHER
DECIDED TO PLAY IT SMART

608
00:23:12,933 --> 00:23:14,867
AND AVOID A LOT OF SQUABBLES
AROUND THE HOUSE.

609
00:23:14,933 --> 00:23:16,333
OH, GRANDPA.

610
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:19,133
I NEVER KNEW
MY MOTHER OR FATHER.

611
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:20,467
OH, BOO HOO. LOOK,
I'VE GOT PROBLEMS TOO.

612
00:23:20,533 --> 00:23:22,133
WELL, LET'S TAKE
A LOOK AT THE ROOM,

613
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:24,333
AND IF YOU LIKE IT,
YOU'RE WELCOME TO STAY.

614
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:26,267
IT'S THIS WAY--
I'LL SHOW IT TO YOU.

615
00:23:26,333 --> 00:23:29,000
HEY, I THOUGHT YOU WERE GETTING
READY TO GO SWIMMING.

616
00:23:29,067 --> 00:23:30,200
OH, THAT CAN WAIT.

617
00:23:30,267 --> 00:23:32,400
NOW THAT TEEN DREAM'S
HERE.

618
00:23:32,467 --> 00:23:33,467
THERE ARE PLENTY OF WINDOWS.

619
00:23:33,533 --> 00:23:34,500
[CHUCKLES]

620
00:23:34,567 --> 00:23:35,567
KILL THEM.

621
00:23:35,633 --> 00:23:37,767
♪♪

622
00:23:37,833 --> 00:23:38,967
WHAT'S THE MATTER?

623
00:23:39,033 --> 00:23:40,167
YOU ACT LIKE YOU'VE
NEVER SEEN THE INSIDE

624
00:23:40,233 --> 00:23:42,033
OF AN AUTOMOBILE BEFORE.

625
00:23:42,100 --> 00:23:43,567
WHAT IS THIS?

626
00:23:43,633 --> 00:23:44,933
THE GEAR SHIFT.

627
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:46,467
WHERE HAVE YOU BEEN
ALL YOUR LIFE?

628
00:23:46,533 --> 00:23:48,233
WHERE HAVE YOU
BEEN ALL MY LIFE?

629
00:23:48,300 --> 00:23:49,467
TELL ME WHAT IT IS FOR.

630
00:23:49,533 --> 00:23:50,867
NOW, LOOK, MISTER,

631
00:23:50,933 --> 00:23:53,200
I DIDN'T OFFER YOU A RIDE TO
GIVE NO DRIVING LESSON.

632
00:23:53,267 --> 00:23:54,333
TELL ME!

633
00:23:54,400 --> 00:23:55,533
WHY DO YOU LOOK LIKE
HOYT AXTON?

634
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:57,867
SURE.
I DIDN'T MEAN ANYTHING.

635
00:23:57,933 --> 00:23:59,200
HERE'S THE CLUTCH.

636
00:23:59,267 --> 00:24:01,267
WHEN I PUSH IT IN,
I CHANGE GEARS.

637
00:24:01,333 --> 00:24:03,033
LOW, SECOND, AND HIGH.

638
00:24:03,100 --> 00:24:04,433
AND TO HALT THE VEHICLE?

639
00:24:04,500 --> 00:24:06,633
WHEN I WANT TO STOP,
I PRESS THE BRAKE.

640
00:24:06,700 --> 00:24:07,633
RIGHT HERE.

641
00:24:07,700 --> 00:24:08,767
AND THIS?

642
00:24:08,833 --> 00:24:10,600
THE STARTER
AND IGNITION SWITCH.

643
00:24:10,667 --> 00:24:12,067
AND THE FUEL,
WHAT DOES IT USE?

644
00:24:12,133 --> 00:24:13,333
ARE YOU KIDDING?

645
00:24:13,400 --> 00:24:14,333
GASOLINE, OF COURSE.

646
00:24:14,400 --> 00:24:15,333
OF COURSE.

647
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:16,333
HERE'S THE GAS PEDAL
RIGHT HERE.

648
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:17,500
YOU KNOW,
FOR ALL ITS PITFALLS,

649
00:24:17,567 --> 00:24:18,967
THIS MOVIE EDUCATES
AS WELL AS ENTERTAINS.

650
00:24:19,033 --> 00:24:20,033
HMM.

651
00:24:20,100 --> 00:24:22,167
DID YOU EVER THINK
ABOUT THAT?

652
00:24:22,233 --> 00:24:30,167
♪♪

653
00:24:36,367 --> 00:24:40,267
YOU KNOW, JOEL,
THAT OLD GRANDPA GUY
WAS WAY TOO NICE

654
00:24:40,333 --> 00:24:43,200
WHEN HE RENTED THAT ROOM
TO THE TEENAGER
FROM OUTER SPACE.

655
00:24:43,267 --> 00:24:46,700
A REAL-LIFE LANDLORD
WOULD NEVER BE LIKE THAT.

656
00:24:46,767 --> 00:24:49,167
WHY, YES, THINGS THAT
HAPPEN IN THE MOVIES

657
00:24:49,233 --> 00:24:52,533
ARE DIFFERENT FROM THE WAY
THEY HAPPEN IN REAL LIFE.

658
00:24:52,600 --> 00:24:57,200
RIGHT, TOM, SO HERE FROM
OUR LOOK AT THE LIGHTER SIDE
DEPARTMENT,

659
00:24:57,267 --> 00:25:01,800
WE'D LIKE TO INTRODUCE A NEW
SEGMENT CALLED REEL TO REAL.

660
00:25:01,867 --> 00:25:04,467
LET'S CHECK IT OUT.
MOVE ASIDE, YOU GUYS.

661
00:25:04,533 --> 00:25:06,467
YOU SEE--
THERE IT IS.

662
00:25:06,533 --> 00:25:08,300
SEE, IN REEL LIFE...

663
00:25:08,367 --> 00:25:10,533
WELL, YOU'RE OFFERED
FREE ROOM AND BOARD

664
00:25:10,600 --> 00:25:13,200
UNTIL YOU CAN GET A JOB
AND PAY BACK YOUR RENT.

665
00:25:13,267 --> 00:25:15,200
IN REAL LIFE...

666
00:25:15,267 --> 00:25:18,233
IF YOU'RE LATE WITH YOUR RENT,
YOUR ROOM IS PADLOCKED

667
00:25:18,300 --> 00:25:20,433
AND YOU END UP LIVING
IN A REFRIGERATOR BOX.

668
00:25:20,500 --> 00:25:21,467
IN REEL LIFE...

669
00:25:21,533 --> 00:25:23,367
YOUR ROOMMATE IS
A BEAUTIFUL YOUNG WOMAN

670
00:25:23,433 --> 00:25:25,467
WHO FILLS YOUR LIFE
WITH AFTERNOON SWIMS,

671
00:25:25,533 --> 00:25:28,033
MOONLIT DRIVES,
AND THE PROMISE OF ROMANCE.

672
00:25:28,100 --> 00:25:29,433
IN REAL LIFE...

673
00:25:29,500 --> 00:25:32,000
YOUR ROOMMATE IS A STINKY
HIGH SCHOOL DROPOUT

674
00:25:32,067 --> 00:25:33,633
WHO FILLS YOUR LIFE
WITH HEAD LICE,

675
00:25:33,700 --> 00:25:36,233
CRUSTY LAUNDRY, AND FURRY
CANS OF SPAGHETTI-OS.

676
00:25:36,300 --> 00:25:37,467
IN REEL LIFE...

677
00:25:37,533 --> 00:25:39,733
YOUR LANDLORD IS A ROSY-CHEEKED,
CHEERFUL OLD MAN.

678
00:25:39,800 --> 00:25:41,300
IN REAL LIFE...

679
00:25:41,367 --> 00:25:43,567
YOUR LANDLORD'S
A BUTANE ADDICT WHO SNEAKS
INTO YOUR APARTMENT

680
00:25:43,633 --> 00:25:44,633
AND LOOKS THROUGH
YOUR UNDERWEAR DRAWER.

681
00:25:44,700 --> 00:25:45,933
IN REEL LIFE...

682
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:48,433
THERE'S A BIG, FAT, DRUNK GUY
SLEEPING ON YOUR COUCH.

683
00:25:48,500 --> 00:25:49,833
AND IN REAL LIFE...

684
00:25:49,900 --> 00:25:51,833
THERE'S A BIG, FAT, DRUNK GUY
SLEEPING ON YOUR COUCH.

685
00:25:51,900 --> 00:25:52,933
[LAUGHTER]

686
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:54,900
THESE ARE JUST A FEW
OF THE DIFFERENCES

687
00:25:54,967 --> 00:25:57,167
IN REAL LIFE AND REEL LIFE.

688
00:25:57,233 --> 00:26:00,600
STAY WITH US ON OUR LOOK ON
THE LIGHTER SIDE DEPARTMENT

689
00:26:00,667 --> 00:26:03,300
FOR SOME OF THOSE
EVERYDAY BEFUDDLEMENTS

690
00:26:03,367 --> 00:26:05,967
THAT COME AT US IN SUCH
A HUMOROUS WAY.

691
00:26:06,033 --> 00:26:07,333
LIKE DIETING.

692
00:26:07,400 --> 00:26:10,133
I JUST LOOK AT A PIECE OF BREAD
AND I GAIN FIVE POUNDS.

693
00:26:10,200 --> 00:26:13,867
LOOK AT CROW HERE-- HE CAN
EAT TEN BANANA SPLITS
AND NOT GAIN AN OUNCE.

694
00:26:13,933 --> 00:26:15,267
I HATE HIM!

695
00:26:15,333 --> 00:26:17,233
AND MONDAYS--
WHAT ARE YOU GONNA DO?

696
00:26:17,300 --> 00:26:21,067
DON'T EVEN TALK TO ME
TILL I'VE HAD MY COFFEE
IN THE MORNING.

697
00:26:21,133 --> 00:26:23,867
WHAT ABOUT STARTING THE CAR.
HAVE YOU THOUGHT ABOUT IT?

698
00:26:23,933 --> 00:26:25,900
MY HIP HURTS. WHY?

699
00:26:25,967 --> 00:26:28,900
♪♪

700
00:26:32,733 --> 00:26:34,033
IT'S NOT RIGHT.

701
00:26:34,100 --> 00:26:37,533
OH, WHAT'S HE READING?
PROSTRATE WORLD NEWS?

702
00:26:37,600 --> 00:26:38,667
THAT'D BE "PROSTATE."

703
00:26:38,733 --> 00:26:40,733
I ASKED HIM WHERE
HE WAS FROM, GRANDPA,

704
00:26:40,800 --> 00:26:43,733
AND HE JUST SAID
HE WAS FROM VERY FAR AWAY.

705
00:26:43,800 --> 00:26:45,533
A BRITISH VILLAGE, MAYBE.

706
00:26:45,600 --> 00:26:48,900
WELL, MAYBE HE DOESN'T LIKE TO
TALK ABOUT WHERE HE'S FROM.

707
00:26:48,967 --> 00:26:50,533
BY THE LOOKS OF HIS OUTFIT,

708
00:26:50,600 --> 00:26:53,367
I'D SAY HE WAS RAISED IN A
PRIVATE SCHOOL OF SOME SORT.

709
00:26:53,433 --> 00:26:55,800
HE MUST GO TO THAT PAROCHIAL
SCHOOL DOWN THE ROAD.

710
00:26:55,867 --> 00:26:58,733
WELL, GRANDPA,
IF HE JUST GOT INTO TOWN

711
00:26:58,800 --> 00:27:03,100
AND CAN'T PAY THE RENT
UNTIL HE GETS A JOB
OR SOMETHING, WOULD--

712
00:27:03,167 --> 00:27:05,267
WELL, WHAT DO YOU SAY,
YOUNG MAN?

713
00:27:05,333 --> 00:27:06,633
WHAT DO YOU THINK
OF THE ROOM?

714
00:27:06,700 --> 00:27:08,067
TOUGH ROOM, HUH?

715
00:27:08,133 --> 00:27:11,900
YOU WILL LET ME...
LIVE HERE WITH YOU?

716
00:27:11,967 --> 00:27:15,867
WELL, SURE. THAT'S WHY
WE HAVE THE SIGN UP.

717
00:27:15,933 --> 00:27:17,867
THAT'S WHY YOU CAME HERE,
WASN'T IT?

718
00:27:17,933 --> 00:27:19,333
[CLEARS THROAT]

719
00:27:19,400 --> 00:27:20,667
NOT EXACTLY, I--

720
00:27:20,733 --> 00:27:21,767
JEEPERS, THIS DOG TAG'S
A GOLD MINE.

721
00:27:21,833 --> 00:27:24,400
DEREK, I WAS JUST
TALKING TO GRANDPA, AND,

722
00:27:24,467 --> 00:27:27,900
WELL, IF YOU DON'T HAVE
THE RENT MONEY RIGHT AWAY,

723
00:27:27,967 --> 00:27:30,933
THAT COULD WAIT UNTIL
HE GETS A JOB,
COULDN'T IT, GRANDPA?

724
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:33,400
MM, WHY, SURE.
THAT'S ALL RIGHT WITH ME, BETTY.

725
00:27:33,467 --> 00:27:34,400
SUCKER!

726
00:27:34,467 --> 00:27:36,933
BUT THEN, IF HE DOESN'T
LIKE THE ROOM...

727
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:40,100
I LIKE IT HERE.
VERY MUCH.

728
00:27:40,167 --> 00:27:41,167
YES, THANK YOU.

729
00:27:41,233 --> 00:27:42,433
I WOULD LIKE TO STAY.

730
00:27:42,500 --> 00:27:45,367
FINE. I'LL GO OUT AND
TAKE DOWN THE SIGN.

731
00:27:45,433 --> 00:27:47,867
YOU CAN USE THE PHONE TO HAVE
YOUR BAGS BROUGHT OVER.

732
00:27:47,933 --> 00:27:49,600
YOU HAVE A BELLBOY TOO?

733
00:27:49,667 --> 00:27:52,567
MY BAGS?
I HAVE NOTHING ELSE.

734
00:27:52,633 --> 00:27:54,567
NO OTHER CLOTHES
OR ANYTHING?

735
00:27:54,633 --> 00:27:56,133
WE WERE NOT ALLOWED TO--

736
00:27:56,200 --> 00:27:59,567
I MEAN, MY UNIFORM
IS ALL I HAVE.

737
00:27:59,633 --> 00:28:02,533
GOSH, YOU'VE GOTTA
HAVE MORE THAN THAT.

738
00:28:02,600 --> 00:28:05,233
BUD LEFT SOME OF HIS CLOTHES IN
THE CLOSET, GRANDPA.

739
00:28:05,300 --> 00:28:06,967
COULDN'T DEREK
USE SOME OF THEM?

740
00:28:07,033 --> 00:28:09,833
WELL, OF COURSE, MY DEAR.
BUD WOULDN'T MIND
A BIT, I'M SURE.

741
00:28:09,900 --> 00:28:10,833
[CAR HORN HONKS]

742
00:28:10,900 --> 00:28:11,833
OH, GOLLY, THAT'S JOE.

743
00:28:11,900 --> 00:28:13,100
HE'S FROM VENUS.

744
00:28:13,167 --> 00:28:14,633
PUT ON WHATEVER YOU LIKE FROM
THE CLOSET, DEREK.

745
00:28:14,700 --> 00:28:16,500
I'LL BE RIGHT BACK--
MAKE YOURSELF AT HOME.

746
00:28:16,567 --> 00:28:17,500
JUST STAY OUT
OF MY CLOTHES.

747
00:28:17,567 --> 00:28:18,500
HI THERE, JOE.

748
00:28:18,567 --> 00:28:19,733
HI, GRAMPS.

749
00:28:19,800 --> 00:28:22,200
BETTY, I 'M AFRAID I CAN'T MAKE
THE SWIMMING DATE.

750
00:28:22,267 --> 00:28:23,733
NOT TILL LATER, ANYWAY.

751
00:28:23,800 --> 00:28:25,567
GOT A SUDDEN ASSIGNMENT
FOR THE PAPER.

752
00:28:25,633 --> 00:28:27,433
OH, GOSH, WHAT NOW, JOE?

753
00:28:27,500 --> 00:28:29,067
I HAVE A LIST OF FOLKS TO
INTERVIEW.

754
00:28:29,133 --> 00:28:31,167
SAY THEY SAW A NEW
FLYING SAUCER LAST NIGHT.

755
00:28:31,233 --> 00:28:33,300
THAT SOUNDS LIKE IT MIGHT TAKE
YOU ALL DAY.

756
00:28:33,367 --> 00:28:35,733
I HOPE NOT.
I'LL CALL YOU AS SOON
AS I GET THROUGH, OKAY?

757
00:28:35,800 --> 00:28:37,300
OKAY, JOE.

758
00:28:37,367 --> 00:28:40,500
WHY DON'T YOU ASK
THE ALIEN WHO'S STAYING
WITH YOU ABOUT THIS?

759
00:28:40,567 --> 00:28:44,033
AH, I GUESS A REPORTER'S LIFE
CAN BE PRETTY HECTIC.

760
00:28:44,100 --> 00:28:46,233
YOU NEVER KNOW WHEN
A NEWS STORY WILL BREAK.

761
00:28:46,300 --> 00:28:48,633
I WAS JUST THINKING...

762
00:28:48,700 --> 00:28:50,567
MAYBE DEREK WOULD
LIKE TO GO SWIMMING,

763
00:28:50,633 --> 00:28:52,167
IF YOU'D LET US
BORROW THE CAR.

764
00:28:52,233 --> 00:28:53,867
BET HE WOULD AT THAT.

765
00:28:53,933 --> 00:28:56,233
UH, IF YOU DON'T
THINK ALICE WOULD MIND.

766
00:28:56,300 --> 00:28:57,633
[LAUGHS]
YOU DON'T KNOW ALICE.

767
00:28:57,700 --> 00:28:59,333
I WON'T BE ABLE TO
KEEP THEM APART.

768
00:28:59,400 --> 00:29:07,333
[KNOCKING]
HEY, LET ME OUT!
[MUFFLED SHOUTING]

769
00:29:07,400 --> 00:29:08,367
[LAUGHS]

770
00:29:08,433 --> 00:29:09,400
[CRYING]

771
00:29:09,467 --> 00:29:11,433
STAY CALM,
UH, ACT NATURAL.

772
00:29:11,500 --> 00:29:13,667
UH, CAN I INTEREST YOU IN
A TEXACO CHRISTMAS ALBUM?

773
00:29:13,733 --> 00:29:14,700
[LAUGHS]

774
00:29:14,767 --> 00:29:18,633
♪♪

775
00:29:18,700 --> 00:29:19,867
HEY, WHAT'S GOING ON IN TOWN
ANYWAY, MISTER?

776
00:29:19,933 --> 00:29:20,867
CONVENTION OR SOMETHING?

777
00:29:20,933 --> 00:29:21,867
WHAT?

778
00:29:21,933 --> 00:29:23,500
WELL, THOSE CLOTHES
YOU'RE WEARING.

779
00:29:23,567 --> 00:29:26,500
I TALKED TO A GUY THIS
MORNING WHO WAS WEARING
THE SAME KIND OF OUTFIT.

780
00:29:26,567 --> 00:29:28,767
MAY BE THE GUY
YOU'RE LOOKING FOR, HUH?

781
00:29:28,833 --> 00:29:30,533
YOU SPOKE TO HIM?

782
00:29:30,600 --> 00:29:31,667
WHAT DID HE TELL YOU?

783
00:29:31,733 --> 00:29:32,667
WHERE DID HE GO?

784
00:29:32,733 --> 00:29:34,033
HEY, WHAT'S THE MATTER
WITH YOU?

785
00:29:34,100 --> 00:29:35,667
HEY, TAKE YOUR HANDS
OFF ME.

786
00:29:35,733 --> 00:29:36,767
YOU WILL TELL ME
WHAT HE SAID TO YOU!

787
00:29:36,833 --> 00:29:38,000
WHY SHOULD I?

788
00:29:38,067 --> 00:29:39,400
HEY, WHO DO YOU THINK
YOU ARE, ANYWAY?

789
00:29:39,467 --> 00:29:41,467
ANSWER ME,
OR I DESTROY YOU!

790
00:29:41,533 --> 00:29:43,133
HE CAME HERE WITH A DOG TAG.

791
00:29:43,200 --> 00:29:45,733
WANTED TO KNOW ABOUT THE
ADDRESS, AND I TOLD HIM
HOW TO FIND IT.

792
00:29:45,800 --> 00:29:47,400
WHERE...
WHERE DID YOU SEND HIM?

793
00:29:47,467 --> 00:29:49,833
IT WAS AN ADDRESS
ON WILLOWCREST DRIVE.

794
00:29:49,900 --> 00:29:51,800
TELL ME HOW TO GET THERE.

795
00:29:51,867 --> 00:29:53,167
JUST DRIVE DOWN THERE
ABOUT THREE BLOCKS.

796
00:29:53,233 --> 00:29:54,900
THAT'S--
THAT'S WILLOWCREST.

797
00:29:54,967 --> 00:29:57,067
1243,
IT'S ONLY A FEW DOORS UP.

798
00:29:57,133 --> 00:29:58,067
UH-OH.

799
00:29:58,133 --> 00:29:59,600
[DRONING]

800
00:29:59,667 --> 00:30:01,600
WHOA, IT'S LIKE
A JENNY CRAIG RAY.

801
00:30:01,667 --> 00:30:02,867
WOW.

802
00:30:02,933 --> 00:30:04,033
SOMEBODY HELP!

803
00:30:04,100 --> 00:30:06,533
[DRONING]

804
00:30:06,600 --> 00:30:09,533
WELL, GUESS IT'S
A SELF-SERVE NOW, HUH?

805
00:30:09,600 --> 00:30:12,000
COME ON, BABY, OUT, OUT.
I'LL DRIVE NOW.

806
00:30:12,067 --> 00:30:14,267
[BONES RATTLING]

807
00:30:14,333 --> 00:30:15,267
RATTLE THEM BONES.

808
00:30:15,333 --> 00:30:16,500
MM-HMM.

809
00:30:16,567 --> 00:30:17,767
[TIRES SCREECH]

810
00:30:17,833 --> 00:30:20,667
YOU DON'T HAVE TO PUT THE BRAKE
ON SO HARD, DEREK.

811
00:30:20,733 --> 00:30:23,567
THAT IS, UNLESS YOU
WANT US TO GO THROUGH
THE WINDSHIELD EVERY TIME.

812
00:30:23,633 --> 00:30:26,233
I HAVE NEVER PILOTED
A VEHICLE LIKE THIS BEFORE.

813
00:30:26,300 --> 00:30:27,533
I WILL TRY AGAIN.

814
00:30:27,600 --> 00:30:28,800
THIS TIME, PULL IN THERE.

815
00:30:28,867 --> 00:30:30,400
THAT'S ALICE'S HOUSE.

816
00:30:30,467 --> 00:30:33,933
XANADU, STATELY HOME
OF CHARLES FOSTER KANE.

817
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:36,467
COST?
NO ONE CAN SAY.

818
00:30:36,533 --> 00:30:38,600
AH, MUCH BETTER.

819
00:30:38,667 --> 00:30:39,733
WAIT, BETTY.

820
00:30:39,800 --> 00:30:41,467
UH, YOU HAVE TOILET
PAPER ON YOUR SHOE.

821
00:30:41,533 --> 00:30:43,733
YES, DEREK, WHAT IS IT?

822
00:30:43,800 --> 00:30:48,433
WHEN I CAME TO YOUR PLACE,
IT WAS BECAUSE OF...

823
00:30:48,500 --> 00:30:49,767
UH, I'M ALL MIXED UP
INSIDE.

824
00:30:49,833 --> 00:30:50,800
YES?

825
00:30:50,867 --> 00:30:52,633
I HAD JUST ARRIVED HERE.

826
00:30:52,700 --> 00:30:55,300
I-- I DID NOT KNOW
WHERE ELSE TO GO,

827
00:30:55,367 --> 00:30:59,233
BUT EVERYTHING WAS
SO STRANGE TO ME, I...

828
00:30:59,300 --> 00:31:01,267
OH, THAT'S GREAT.
CAN WE JUST GO IN THE HOUSE?

829
00:31:01,333 --> 00:31:04,167
I'M GLAD YOU CAME.

830
00:31:04,233 --> 00:31:06,000
SO'S GRANDPA.

831
00:31:06,067 --> 00:31:07,100
"SGRANDPA"?

832
00:31:07,167 --> 00:31:08,867
WITHOUT ANY FAMILY
OR FRIENDS,

833
00:31:08,933 --> 00:31:13,333
YOU WOULDN'T LIKE IT AT A HOTEL
OR ANY PLACE LIKE THAT.

834
00:31:13,400 --> 00:31:14,600
COME ON.

835
00:31:14,667 --> 00:31:16,567
I HOPE ALICE CAN DIG UP SOME
SWIM TRUNKS FOR YOU.

836
00:31:16,633 --> 00:31:19,467
UH, I HAVE NEVER PILOTED
SWIM TRUNKS BEFORE.

837
00:31:19,533 --> 00:31:21,867
♪♪

838
00:31:21,933 --> 00:31:26,567
OPERATOR, THERE'S A NAKED GIRL
IN MY POOL AND SHE'S NUDE!

839
00:31:26,633 --> 00:31:28,767
[LAUGHS]

840
00:31:28,833 --> 00:31:29,767
HI THERE!

841
00:31:29,833 --> 00:31:30,767
LIKEWISE, I'M SURE.

842
00:31:30,833 --> 00:31:31,767
WHO'S THE STRANGER?

843
00:31:31,833 --> 00:31:32,967
JOE COULDN'T MAKE IT, ALICE.

844
00:31:33,033 --> 00:31:35,200
I TALKED DEREK INTO COMING
ALONG.

845
00:31:35,267 --> 00:31:37,467
DEREK, THIS IS ALICE.

846
00:31:37,533 --> 00:31:41,533
DEREK!
HEY, I LIKE THAT.

847
00:31:41,600 --> 00:31:43,467
COME ON IN,
THE WATER'S FINE.

848
00:31:43,533 --> 00:31:44,800
AND SO AM I.

849
00:31:44,867 --> 00:31:45,833
WELL, WE NEED A PAIR
OF SWIM TRUNKS.

850
00:31:45,900 --> 00:31:47,467
I COULDN'T FIND ANY
AT MY HOUSE.

851
00:31:47,533 --> 00:31:48,667
NO PROBLEM AT ALL.

852
00:31:48,733 --> 00:31:50,267
HE CAN WEAR A PAIR
OF MY FATHER'S.

853
00:31:50,333 --> 00:31:51,533
THEY'VE GOT
THE SUPPORT PANEL.

854
00:31:51,600 --> 00:31:53,233
THE FOLKS ARE GONE TODAY,
AND SO ARE THE SERVANTS.

855
00:31:53,300 --> 00:31:55,267
WE HAVE THE WHOLE PLACE TO
OURSELVES.

856
00:31:55,333 --> 00:31:57,300
MMMMMM...

857
00:31:57,367 --> 00:31:59,100
WHERE ARE THE TRUNKS,
ALICE?

858
00:31:59,167 --> 00:32:00,767
HANGING UP,
RIGHT OVER THERE.

859
00:32:00,833 --> 00:32:02,200
EARTH GIRLS ARE EASY.

860
00:32:02,267 --> 00:32:03,933
THEY LOOK A LITTLE LARGE
FOR YOU, DEREK.

861
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:07,533
MAYBE YOU BETTER PUT THEM ON
WITH SOME CLOTHESPINS,
TOO, JUST IN CASE.

862
00:32:07,600 --> 00:32:09,533
OOH, SHE MAKES EVERYTHING
SOUND SO DIRTY.

863
00:32:09,600 --> 00:32:10,967
I GUESS IT'S SAFE TO
TRY 'EM ON ANYWAY.

864
00:32:11,033 --> 00:32:12,333
OVER THERE,
AT THE BATHHOUSE.

865
00:32:12,400 --> 00:32:13,567
[DOG TAG BOUNCES]

866
00:32:13,633 --> 00:32:14,967
WHAT WAS THAT?

867
00:32:15,033 --> 00:32:16,667
DON'T WORRY, I'LL GET IT.

868
00:32:16,733 --> 00:32:18,133
PROBABLY JUST
A SILLY OLD PLOT POINT.

869
00:32:18,200 --> 00:32:20,667
IT WAS WHAT I WANTED
TO TELL YOU ABOUT,

870
00:32:20,733 --> 00:32:25,267
THE REASON I CAME TO YOUR
PLACE WHEN I DID NOT KNOW
WHERE ELSE TO GO.

871
00:32:25,333 --> 00:32:27,767
HECK, I THOUGHT IT WAS
A 50-CENT PIECE AT LEAST.

872
00:32:27,833 --> 00:32:31,667
[SINGSONG]
DEREK KILLED YOUR DOG,
DEREK KILLED YOUR DOG.

873
00:32:31,733 --> 00:32:34,700
WELL, IT IS.
THAT'S SPARKY'S.

874
00:32:34,767 --> 00:32:37,233
SPARKY'S DOG TAG.

875
00:32:37,300 --> 00:32:39,433
WHERE ON EARTH
DID YOU FIND IT?

876
00:32:39,500 --> 00:32:40,767
WELL, AFTER CAVING IN
HIS HEAD WITH A SHOVEL...

877
00:32:40,833 --> 00:32:43,433
WHEN I FIRST ARRIVED,
I WAS WITH SOME OTHERS.

878
00:32:43,500 --> 00:32:46,000
ONE OF THEM DESTROYED
A SMALL CREATURE.

879
00:32:46,067 --> 00:32:51,000
LATER, I FOUND THAT
AMONG THE REMAINS.

880
00:32:51,067 --> 00:32:53,933
YOU MEAN,
SOMEBODY KILLED SPARKY?

881
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:55,200
MM-HMM.

882
00:32:55,267 --> 00:32:57,433
OH NO, DEREK,
IT CAN'T BE TRUE.

883
00:32:57,500 --> 00:32:59,000
WHY WOULD ANYONE
WANT TO KILL SPARKY?

884
00:32:59,067 --> 00:33:00,900
'CAUSE HE WAS A SCHNAUZER.
I HATE THOSE THINGS.

885
00:33:00,967 --> 00:33:02,033
[ALICE]
BETTY, I'M SORRY.

886
00:33:02,100 --> 00:33:03,833
TELL ME WHO DID IT, DEREK.

887
00:33:03,900 --> 00:33:06,200
THEY...
ARE GONE NOW.

888
00:33:06,267 --> 00:33:08,267
ONLY I REMAIN.

889
00:33:08,333 --> 00:33:11,367
BUT...I DON'T UNDERSTAND.

890
00:33:11,433 --> 00:33:12,800
WHERE IS SPARK--

891
00:33:12,867 --> 00:33:14,367
KY.

892
00:33:14,433 --> 00:33:15,667
SPARKY.

893
00:33:15,733 --> 00:33:17,400
WILL YOU TAKE ME
TO WHERE IT HAPPENED?

894
00:33:17,467 --> 00:33:18,967
I'LL GET DRESSED
AND COME WITH YOU.

895
00:33:19,033 --> 00:33:20,200
NO, ALICE, PLEASE.

896
00:33:20,267 --> 00:33:21,267
DON'T GET DRESSED.

897
00:33:21,333 --> 00:33:23,600
YOU STAY HERE.
WE'LL SEE YOU LATER.

898
00:33:23,667 --> 00:33:24,600
♪♪

899
00:33:24,667 --> 00:33:25,867
HMM.

900
00:33:25,933 --> 00:33:29,867
♪ IT'S THE NEW ZOO REVUE
COMING RIGHT AT YOU ♪

901
00:33:29,933 --> 00:33:30,900
[MUFFLED SHOUTING]
COME ON, MAN!

902
00:33:30,967 --> 00:33:34,633
LET ME OUT!
LET ME OUT!

903
00:33:34,700 --> 00:33:41,133
[MUFFLED SHOUTING]

904
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:44,400
WELL, WELL, SO DEREK
DIDN'T COME INTO TOWN ALONE.

905
00:33:44,467 --> 00:33:46,533
IF YOU'RE LOOKING FOR HIM,
HE ISN'T HERE NOW.

906
00:33:46,600 --> 00:33:48,800
HE AND BETTY-- THAT'S MY
GRANDDAUGHTER--

907
00:33:48,867 --> 00:33:50,600
THEY WENT OVER
TO THE WOODWARDS.

908
00:33:50,667 --> 00:33:52,500
WHY DON'T YOU GO ON
OVER THERE?

909
00:33:52,567 --> 00:33:55,067
NO DOUBT THEY'D BE GLAD TO HAVE
YOU JOIN IN THE FUN.

910
00:33:55,133 --> 00:33:58,600
YES.
HOW DO I GO THERE?

911
00:33:58,667 --> 00:33:59,800
LET ME COUNT THE WAYS.

912
00:33:59,867 --> 00:34:01,300
THE WOODWARDS ARE STRAIGHT
ON DOWN THE STREET

913
00:34:01,367 --> 00:34:04,367
ABOUT THREE MILES, JUST BEFORE
YOU GET TO THE PARK.

914
00:34:04,433 --> 00:34:06,533
GOT THE BIGGEST HOUSE
ON THE BLOCK DOWN THERE.

915
00:34:06,600 --> 00:34:07,567
YOU CAN'T MISS IT.

916
00:34:07,633 --> 00:34:09,600
JUST LIKE YOU
CAN'T MISS ME.

917
00:34:09,667 --> 00:34:11,233
WHERE YOU FELLAS FROM,
ANYWAY?

918
00:34:11,300 --> 00:34:14,600
DON'T BELIEVE I'VE SEEN
UNIFORMS LIKE YOURS BEFORE.

919
00:34:14,667 --> 00:34:16,467
I LIKE YOU, GRAMPS.
THAT'S WHY I KILL YOU LAST.

920
00:34:16,533 --> 00:34:18,400
HMM, MILITARY SECRET, EH?
HEH HEH.

921
00:34:18,467 --> 00:34:20,033
WELL, IT DOESN'T MATTER.

922
00:34:20,100 --> 00:34:22,867
DEREK DIDN'T SAY
WHERE HE'S FROM EITHER.

923
00:34:22,933 --> 00:34:24,000
HAVE YOU MET
MY GRANDDAUGHTER?

924
00:34:24,067 --> 00:34:25,033
DON'T LET ME KEEP YOU.

925
00:34:25,100 --> 00:34:27,167
YOU'RE PROBABLY
ANXIOUS TO SEE HIM.

926
00:34:27,233 --> 00:34:30,667
DON'T LEAVE YOUR DOG
IN THE CAR ON A HOT DAY!

927
00:34:30,733 --> 00:34:33,867
[HUMMING]

928
00:34:33,933 --> 00:34:37,033
[SNIFFING]
WOOF!

929
00:34:37,100 --> 00:34:38,833
SPARKY!
[WHISTLING]

930
00:34:38,900 --> 00:34:40,833
HERE, SPARKY!
SPARKS! SPARKS!

931
00:34:40,900 --> 00:34:43,467
[WHISTLING]
HERE, BOY, HERE, BOY.

932
00:34:43,533 --> 00:34:45,633
HMM, HMM, HMM, HMM.

933
00:34:45,700 --> 00:34:49,000
WHERE IS HE, DEREK?

934
00:34:49,067 --> 00:34:50,000
YECCHH!

935
00:34:50,067 --> 00:34:51,467
YOU DON'T MEAN
THOSE OLD BONES.

936
00:34:51,533 --> 00:34:54,000
YOU CAN SEE THEY'VE BEEN HERE
FOR A VERY LONG TIME.

937
00:34:54,067 --> 00:34:58,833
NO. IT WAS AMONG THESE REMAINS
THAT I FOUND THE METAL
INSCRIPTION.

938
00:34:58,900 --> 00:35:01,767
THIS COULDN'T BE SPARKY.

939
00:35:01,833 --> 00:35:03,200
SPARKY HAD SKIN.

940
00:35:03,267 --> 00:35:05,667
I KNOW-- HE MUST HAVE BEEN HERE,
AND HIS COLLAR TAG FELL OFF.

941
00:35:05,733 --> 00:35:06,700
THAT'S ALL.

942
00:35:06,767 --> 00:35:08,500
HEY, WAKE UP AND SMELL
THE COLLIE.

943
00:35:08,567 --> 00:35:11,967
YOU ARE NOT FAMILIAR
WITH THE FOCUSING
DISINTEGRATOR RAY?

944
00:35:12,033 --> 00:35:13,233
YEAH, MY AUNT HAS ONE.

945
00:35:13,300 --> 00:35:15,600
THE WHAT?

946
00:35:15,667 --> 00:35:17,800
IT PROJECTS AN ISOLATED BEAM

947
00:35:17,867 --> 00:35:21,333
WHICH SEPARATES THE MOLECULES
OF LIVING MATERIAL
IN CHAIN REACTION.

948
00:35:21,400 --> 00:35:22,467
IT SLICES, IT DICES.

949
00:35:22,533 --> 00:35:25,667
ALL BUT THE SOLIDS,
THE SKELETAL BRACES.

950
00:35:25,733 --> 00:35:27,667
HOW HORRIBLE.

951
00:35:27,733 --> 00:35:29,467
YET EFFECTIVE.

952
00:35:29,533 --> 00:35:33,767
AND YOU MEAN SPARKY...

953
00:35:33,833 --> 00:35:35,367
BUT--

954
00:35:35,433 --> 00:35:38,433
OVER THERE IS WHAT HAPPENED
WHEN THE SAME BEAM
WAS AIMED AT ME.

955
00:35:38,500 --> 00:35:39,633
IT MISSED, AND...

956
00:35:39,700 --> 00:35:41,033
BECAME A TREE.

957
00:35:41,100 --> 00:35:43,700
THAT IS WHAT IS LEFT.

958
00:35:43,767 --> 00:35:45,867
GOOD HEAVENS, DEREK.

959
00:35:45,933 --> 00:35:48,033
YOU'VE GOT TO
EXPLAIN IT TO ME.

960
00:35:48,100 --> 00:35:49,800
WHY WERE THEY DOING THIS?

961
00:35:49,867 --> 00:35:50,900
WHERE WERE THEY FROM?

962
00:35:50,967 --> 00:35:51,967
HOW DID YOU--

963
00:35:52,033 --> 00:35:53,967
AND WHO TOOK THE FRAMES
OUT OF THE FILM?

964
00:35:54,033 --> 00:35:57,233
♪♪

965
00:36:00,800 --> 00:36:03,333
[IMITATES DOG PANTING]

966
00:36:03,400 --> 00:36:05,367
HELLO, UHURA.

967
00:36:05,433 --> 00:36:06,567
WELL, HELLO.

968
00:36:06,633 --> 00:36:08,067
AT EASE, SOLDIER.

969
00:36:08,133 --> 00:36:09,267
WHAT CAN I DO FOR YOU?

970
00:36:09,333 --> 00:36:10,467
YOU ARE ALONE?

971
00:36:10,533 --> 00:36:12,033
COULD BE.

972
00:36:12,100 --> 00:36:13,333
WHERE ARE THE OTHERS?

973
00:36:13,400 --> 00:36:14,567
THE ONES WHO WERE WITH YOU.

974
00:36:14,633 --> 00:36:16,633
WHY DO YOU WANT TO KNOW THAT?

975
00:36:16,700 --> 00:36:18,233
TELL ME WHERE THEY ARE.

976
00:36:18,300 --> 00:36:19,500
MISS HATHAWAY,
THE EARLY YEARS.

977
00:36:19,567 --> 00:36:20,733
SAY, WHO ARE YOU ANYWAY?

978
00:36:20,800 --> 00:36:22,333
NEVER MIND!
JUST TELL ME.

979
00:36:22,400 --> 00:36:24,267
THEY LEFT HERE...
THEY'RE GONE.

980
00:36:24,333 --> 00:36:25,733
WHERE DID THEY GO?

981
00:36:25,800 --> 00:36:29,667
I THINK YOU BETTER GET OUT OF
HERE BEFORE I CALL THE POLICE.

982
00:36:29,733 --> 00:36:32,300
YOU WILL CALL NO ONE.
YOU WILL DO AS I SAY.

983
00:36:32,367 --> 00:36:33,867
THAT'S WHAT YOU THINK,
MISTER.

984
00:36:33,933 --> 00:36:35,667
LOOK, PAT BOONE
IS THE STAND-IN HERE.

985
00:36:35,733 --> 00:36:38,300
THIS IS BOGUS!
I'M GOING TO THE DEEP END!

986
00:36:38,367 --> 00:36:41,200
I SAID YOU
WILL CALL NO ONE!

987
00:36:41,267 --> 00:36:43,233
[DRONING]

988
00:36:43,300 --> 00:36:46,300
TOO MUCH CHLORINE!

989
00:36:46,367 --> 00:36:50,233
YES, FOLKS, PROOF YOU CAN
BE TOO RICH AND TOO THIN.

990
00:36:50,300 --> 00:36:52,533
HEY, SHE JUST CHANGED
INTO THE SAME DRESS.

991
00:36:52,600 --> 00:36:54,033
HUH?

992
00:36:54,100 --> 00:36:57,933
WHO DECORATED THIS HOUSE,
WAYLAND FLOWERS?

993
00:36:58,000 --> 00:37:00,833
DARN CORNS.
OOH, OOH.

994
00:37:00,900 --> 00:37:02,333
♪♪

995
00:37:02,400 --> 00:37:04,567
EH, GRAMPS STARTED
EARLY TODAY.

996
00:37:04,633 --> 00:37:07,100
OH, GRANDPA, I BOUGHT
THAT NYQUIL FOR COLDS,

997
00:37:07,167 --> 00:37:09,833
NOT FOR YOU
TO MAKE NYQUILADAS.

998
00:37:09,900 --> 00:37:14,300
"DEAR GRAMPS, I CANNOT
CONTINUE TO LIVE THIS WAY."

999
00:37:14,367 --> 00:37:17,100
AND THE POST-IT NOTE
WAS BORN.

1000
00:37:17,167 --> 00:37:19,500
♪♪

1001
00:37:19,567 --> 00:37:22,467
GRANDPA, I LEFT A NOTE
FOR YOU BY THE PHONE FOR
WHEN YOU WAKE UP.

1002
00:37:22,533 --> 00:37:24,467
GRANDPA!
GRANDPA!

1003
00:37:24,533 --> 00:37:27,567
WHO'S PUTTING SPIDERS
ALL OVER MY... OH.

1004
00:37:27,633 --> 00:37:30,400
IT'S GRAMPS.
HE'S GOT THE FLU AGAIN.

1005
00:37:30,467 --> 00:37:33,300
GRANDPA WAS ASLEEP,
SO I LEFT A NOTE SO HE'LL
KNOW WHERE WE WENT.

1006
00:37:33,367 --> 00:37:36,233
IF I KNOW GRANDPA,
WE'LL BE BACK BEFORE
HE EVEN WAKES UP.

1007
00:37:36,300 --> 00:37:38,633
IF HE EVER WAKES UP.

1008
00:37:38,700 --> 00:37:39,933
[MUFFLED SHOUTING]

1009
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:41,233
[PHONE RINGING]

1010
00:37:41,300 --> 00:37:44,067
STILL GETTING...
[MUMBLING]

1011
00:37:44,133 --> 00:37:45,733
OH, AH, AH!

1012
00:37:45,800 --> 00:37:47,933
♪ IT'S THE NEW ZOO REVUE ♪

1013
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:49,533
♪ COMING BACK AT YOU ♪

1014
00:37:49,600 --> 00:37:51,533
♪ IT'S QUITE
AN AMAZING THING ♪

1015
00:37:51,600 --> 00:37:52,533
♪ WHEN THE ANIMALS... ♪

1016
00:37:52,600 --> 00:37:53,867
[YAWNS] HELLO?

1017
00:37:53,933 --> 00:37:56,167
HELLO, GRAMPS?
THIS IS JOE-- BETTY THERE?

1018
00:37:56,233 --> 00:38:00,100
NO, SHE AND DEREK WENT ON OVER
TO THE WOODWARDS' POOL.

1019
00:38:00,167 --> 00:38:02,533
YOU CAN PROBABLY
REACH HER OVER THERE.

1020
00:38:02,600 --> 00:38:03,933
DEREK-- WHO'S DEREK?

1021
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:06,100
OH, YOU HAVEN'T MET HIM YET,
HAVE YOU?

1022
00:38:06,167 --> 00:38:07,867
HE'S BETTY'S NEW REGULAR
SATURDAY NIGHT THING.

1023
00:38:07,933 --> 00:38:09,333
YEAH, HE RENTED BUD'S
OLD ROOM THIS MORNING.

1024
00:38:09,400 --> 00:38:11,233
SEEMS LIKE A NICE FELLOW.

1025
00:38:11,300 --> 00:38:12,233
OH?

1026
00:38:12,300 --> 00:38:13,500
AT FIRST.

1027
00:38:13,567 --> 00:38:15,033
WELL, THE REASON I CALLED,
I WANTED TO TELL BETTY

1028
00:38:15,100 --> 00:38:16,900
I STUMBLED ONTO
A DOUBLE MURDER STORY

1029
00:38:16,967 --> 00:38:19,167
THAT MAY KEEP ME LONGER,
BUT, WELL,

1030
00:38:19,233 --> 00:38:20,700
AFTER I GET THE STORY
INTO THE PAPER,

1031
00:38:20,767 --> 00:38:22,800
I'LL GO ON OVER TO ALICE'S
AND SEE HER THERE.

1032
00:38:22,867 --> 00:38:25,367
A DOUBLE MURDER, JOE?
WHEN WAS IT, WHERE?

1033
00:38:25,433 --> 00:38:27,367
WE'RE NOT SURE YET, GRAMPS.
THERE'S ONLY A COUPLE OF
SKELETONS.

1034
00:38:27,433 --> 00:38:28,500
AND THEY'RE NOT TALKING.

1035
00:38:28,567 --> 00:38:30,067
WE'LL KNOW MORE
WHEN THE CORONER GETS HERE.

1036
00:38:30,133 --> 00:38:31,800
WELL, GOTTA GET BUSY NOW,
GRAMPS. I'LL TALK TO YOU
LATER-- BYE!

1037
00:38:31,867 --> 00:38:32,900
OH, YOU DON'T NEED
TO SEE THAT, NO.

1038
00:38:32,967 --> 00:38:35,600
JOE! JOE, I JUST
FOUND A NOTE. JOE--

1039
00:38:35,667 --> 00:38:36,667
WHAT DO YOU KNOW?

1040
00:38:36,733 --> 00:38:37,700
HELLO, HELLO!

1041
00:38:37,767 --> 00:38:39,000
HELLO, JOE,
WHAT DO YOU KNOW?

1042
00:38:39,067 --> 00:38:40,433
JUST GOT BACK FROM KOKOMO.

1043
00:38:40,500 --> 00:38:41,633
[MUFFLED SHOUTING]

1044
00:38:41,700 --> 00:38:43,567
I GOT IT-- HE LOOKS LIKE,
UH, ETHEL WATERS.

1045
00:38:43,633 --> 00:38:44,600
YEAH.

1046
00:38:44,667 --> 00:38:46,867
[MUFFLED SHOUTING]

1047
00:38:46,933 --> 00:38:48,833
BY GOLLY, YOU MISSED THEM
AT THE POOL, HUH?

1048
00:38:48,900 --> 00:38:50,300
ON A KILLING SPREE, HUH?

1049
00:38:50,367 --> 00:38:51,333
SURE AM SORRY.

1050
00:38:51,400 --> 00:38:53,500
UH, BETTY LEFT ME A NOTE.

1051
00:38:53,567 --> 00:38:55,133
NOW THEY'VE GONE OVER
TO THE COLLEGE

1052
00:38:55,200 --> 00:38:56,533
TO SEE PROFESSOR SIMPSON.

1053
00:38:56,600 --> 00:38:58,433
GIVE ME THAT.

1054
00:38:58,500 --> 00:39:00,433
HEY, ROOM 222.

1055
00:39:00,500 --> 00:39:01,467
YEAH.

1056
00:39:01,533 --> 00:39:03,833
[WHISTLING A TUNE]

1057
00:39:03,900 --> 00:39:06,933
YOU KNOW, SCHOOL ALWAYS SMELLS
THE SAME WHEN YOU GO BACK.

1058
00:39:07,000 --> 00:39:07,967
MM-HMM.

1059
00:39:08,033 --> 00:39:09,233
YEP.

1060
00:39:09,300 --> 00:39:12,000
IT SMELLS LIKE SHAME,
GUILT, AND HUMILIATION.

1061
00:39:12,067 --> 00:39:13,133
HEY, SYLVIA PLATH!

1062
00:39:13,200 --> 00:39:15,967
HELLO. WHERE CAN WE FIND
PROFESSOR SIMPSON?

1063
00:39:16,033 --> 00:39:17,533
THIS IS HIS OFFICE, BUT HE
HASN'T COME IN YET.

1064
00:39:17,600 --> 00:39:19,067
IT'S BARBIE'S
MALIBU DREAM DESK.

1065
00:39:19,133 --> 00:39:20,733
LET'S WAIT FOR HIM IN THE
FACULTY PARKING LOT.

1066
00:39:20,800 --> 00:39:22,300
IT'S JUST AROUND
THE BUILDING.

1067
00:39:22,367 --> 00:39:23,633
YOU MAY WAIT HERE
IF YOU LIKE.

1068
00:39:23,700 --> 00:39:25,533
NO, THANK YOU.
WE'LL WAIT OUTSIDE.

1069
00:39:25,600 --> 00:39:26,900
YOUR DESK EMBARRASSES US.

1070
00:39:26,967 --> 00:39:28,867
TINY.

1071
00:39:28,933 --> 00:39:30,633
NOW I'LL SHOW YOU
MY OLD LOCKER.

1072
00:39:30,700 --> 00:39:33,867
I WONDER IF I STILL
REMEMBER THE COMBINATION.

1073
00:39:33,933 --> 00:39:35,667
♪ DOO DOO DOO,
COME ON ♪

1074
00:39:35,733 --> 00:39:38,400
♪ IT'S A NICE DAY
FOR A WHITE WEDDING ♪

1075
00:39:38,467 --> 00:39:40,300
♪ DOO DOO DOO,
NICE DAY ♪

1076
00:39:40,367 --> 00:39:41,633
♪ OOH, DOO DOO,
TO START AGAIN ♪

1077
00:39:41,700 --> 00:39:42,700
UH, MISS HATHAWAY, JETHRO
WANTS TO BE A ROCK STAR.

1078
00:39:42,767 --> 00:39:43,967
GOOD MORNING, HILDA.

1079
00:39:44,033 --> 00:39:44,967
OH, GOOD MORNING,
PROFESSOR SIMPSON.

1080
00:39:45,033 --> 00:39:45,967
OOPH!

1081
00:39:46,033 --> 00:39:47,633
UH, CALL
THE BURN WARD PRONTO.

1082
00:39:47,700 --> 00:39:48,967
HAVE THE APTITUDE
QUESTIONNAIRES COME IN?

1083
00:39:49,033 --> 00:39:50,800
THEY'RE PROBABLY STILL IN
MIMEOGRAPHING.

1084
00:39:50,867 --> 00:39:52,700
I'LL GO DOWN AND SEE
IF THEY'RE READY.

1085
00:39:52,767 --> 00:39:54,833
POOR GUY.

1086
00:39:54,900 --> 00:39:57,500
[SINGING]

1087
00:39:57,567 --> 00:39:59,233
THAT'S PROFESSOR SIMPSON'S
OFFICE.

1088
00:39:59,300 --> 00:40:00,767
THE THIRD DOOR DOWN.

1089
00:40:00,833 --> 00:40:02,200
HE'S HEAD OF THE SCIENCE
DEPARTMENT.

1090
00:40:02,267 --> 00:40:04,033
YEAH, IF YOU THROW UP
OR NEED SOME SAWDUST,

1091
00:40:04,100 --> 00:40:05,567
JUST CALL ME.

1092
00:40:05,633 --> 00:40:07,533
[MUFFLED SHOUTING]

1093
00:40:07,600 --> 00:40:10,700
WELL, THAT LOOKS LIKE
PROFESSOR SIMPSON'S CAR
RIGHT THERE.

1094
00:40:10,767 --> 00:40:12,600
HE MUST BE
SOMEWHERE ELSE ON CAMPUS.

1095
00:40:12,667 --> 00:40:14,867
WE'D BETTER GO BACK
TO HIS OFFICE AND WAIT.

1096
00:40:14,933 --> 00:40:17,633
HELLO, THIS IS SIMPSON,
SCIENCE DEPARTMENT.

1097
00:40:17,700 --> 00:40:19,300
PUT THAT DOWN.

1098
00:40:19,367 --> 00:40:20,767
WHAT IS THE MEANING
OF THIS?

1099
00:40:20,833 --> 00:40:21,933
DO AS I SAY.

1100
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:23,133
WHO ARE YOU?

1101
00:40:23,200 --> 00:40:24,367
WHERE IS HE?

1102
00:40:24,433 --> 00:40:26,167
THE ONE WHO CAME WITH
INFORMATION FOR YOU.

1103
00:40:26,233 --> 00:40:28,267
WHO? YOU ARE MAKING
SOME MISTAKE.

1104
00:40:28,333 --> 00:40:30,100
I AM MAKING NO MISTAKE.

1105
00:40:30,167 --> 00:40:32,233
WHERE DID HE GO--
OUT THERE?

1106
00:40:32,300 --> 00:40:34,300
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT YOU'RE TALKING ABOUT!

1107
00:40:34,367 --> 00:40:36,533
YOU WILL SPEAK
TO NO ONE ELSE.

1108
00:40:36,600 --> 00:40:38,033
[DRONING]

1109
00:40:38,100 --> 00:40:39,900
♪♪

1110
00:40:39,967 --> 00:40:42,867
THAT RAYGUN WORKS WELL,
BUT YOU CAN'T GET
THE STINK OUT OF IT.

1111
00:40:42,933 --> 00:40:45,667
OOPH! NEVER TOASTED SOMEBODY
THAT OLD BEFORE.

1112
00:40:45,733 --> 00:40:46,867
AHH!

1113
00:40:46,933 --> 00:40:49,200
OOPH! SMELLS LIKE
THE PRIMATE HOUSE IN HERE.

1114
00:40:49,267 --> 00:40:50,500
JEEPERS!

1115
00:40:50,567 --> 00:40:55,533
[GRUNTING]

1116
00:40:55,600 --> 00:40:57,333
WENT A LITTLE. HUH.

1117
00:40:57,400 --> 00:40:59,567
♪♪

1118
00:40:59,633 --> 00:41:02,867
♪ SHE WAS A FAST MACHINE,
SHE KEPT HER MOTOR CLEAN ♪

1119
00:41:02,933 --> 00:41:04,000
WE FOUND HIS CAR, SO--

1120
00:41:04,067 --> 00:41:05,200
[CHUCKLES]
YES, I KNOW.

1121
00:41:05,267 --> 00:41:07,400
HE CAME IN
RIGHT AFTER YOU LEFT.

1122
00:41:07,467 --> 00:41:11,133
♪♪

1123
00:41:11,200 --> 00:41:13,400
HOLD MY CALLS, WILL YOU?
HA HA!

1124
00:41:13,467 --> 00:41:14,633
[SCREAMS]

1125
00:41:14,700 --> 00:41:16,567
I'LL BE TAKING LUNCH,
HILDA.

1126
00:41:16,633 --> 00:41:18,600
OH, DEREK.

1127
00:41:18,667 --> 00:41:21,600
OH, IT'S SOME KIND
OF FOOLISH JOKE.

1128
00:41:21,667 --> 00:41:25,067
I'M NOT GOING TO KEEP
A JOB WHERE THIS SORT
OF THING GOES ON.

1129
00:41:25,133 --> 00:41:27,000
IS THAT THE STRAW THAT
BROKE THE CAMEL'S BACK?

1130
00:41:27,067 --> 00:41:28,333
YEP.

1131
00:41:28,400 --> 00:41:30,200
I WANT TO BELIEVE WHAT I'M
THINKING ISN'T TRUE, BUT--

1132
00:41:30,267 --> 00:41:32,500
IT WAS
A FOCUSING DISINTEGRATOR.

1133
00:41:32,567 --> 00:41:35,333
THEN WHOEVER KILLED SPARKY...

1134
00:41:35,400 --> 00:41:36,433
USED A FOCUSING
DISINTEGRATOR.

1135
00:41:36,500 --> 00:41:38,100
BUT YOU SAID THEY'D GONE!

1136
00:41:38,167 --> 00:41:40,267
FOR SOME REASON,
THEY WANT TO STOP ME.

1137
00:41:40,333 --> 00:41:42,733
SOMEHOW,
WE WERE TRACED HERE.

1138
00:41:42,800 --> 00:41:44,500
I WANT YOU TO GET IN
YOUR VEHICLE

1139
00:41:44,567 --> 00:41:46,300
AND GO TO A PLACE
WHERE YOU WILL BE SAFE.

1140
00:41:46,367 --> 00:41:47,733
BUT HOW COULD THEY--

1141
00:41:47,800 --> 00:41:49,200
[GASPS]
GRANDPA!

1142
00:41:49,267 --> 00:41:50,300
WHAT?

1143
00:41:50,367 --> 00:41:51,700
I LEFT A NOTE FOR GRANDPA.

1144
00:41:51,767 --> 00:41:53,400
THEY MUST HAVE--
OH, DEREK!

1145
00:41:53,467 --> 00:41:54,400
GRANDPA SQUEALED!

1146
00:41:54,467 --> 00:41:55,867
I WILL GO TO YOUR PLACE.

1147
00:41:55,933 --> 00:41:58,067
NO, THEY MAY BE
WAITING FOR YOU THERE.

1148
00:41:58,133 --> 00:41:59,967
I CAN CALL GRANDPA.

1149
00:42:00,033 --> 00:42:01,633
HERE, GRANDPA!
[WHISTLING]

1150
00:42:01,700 --> 00:42:03,567
HERE, BOY.
HERE, GRANDPA.

1151
00:42:03,633 --> 00:42:06,333
♪♪

1152
00:42:06,400 --> 00:42:08,333
HEY, ROOM FOR ONE, BUDDY.

1153
00:42:08,400 --> 00:42:12,333
♪♪

1154
00:42:12,400 --> 00:42:14,833
[PHONE RINGING]

1155
00:42:14,900 --> 00:42:17,800
OH, GOODY,
SOMEBODY NEEDS A ROOM.

1156
00:42:17,867 --> 00:42:18,933
HELLO?

1157
00:42:19,000 --> 00:42:20,667
OH, GRANDPA, THANK HEAVENS.

1158
00:42:20,733 --> 00:42:22,267
DEREK, HE'S ALL RIGHT.

1159
00:42:22,333 --> 00:42:24,233
BETTY, WHAT IS IT, CHILD?
WHAT'S THE MATTER?

1160
00:42:24,300 --> 00:42:26,100
GRANDPA, WAS SOMEBODY THERE?

1161
00:42:26,167 --> 00:42:28,100
SOMEBODY YOU TOLD
WE WERE AT THE COLLEGE?

1162
00:42:28,167 --> 00:42:29,933
OH, YES.
THE FRIEND OF DEREK'S.

1163
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:31,633
DID HE FIND YOU OKAY?

1164
00:42:31,700 --> 00:42:32,633
HE'S A MURDERER!

1165
00:42:32,700 --> 00:42:34,800
HE KILLED PROFESSOR SIMPSON,
GRANDPA!

1166
00:42:34,867 --> 00:42:38,333
HE'S AFTER DEREK, AND HE'S
PROBABLY ON THE WAY BACK
TO THE HOUSE RIGHT NOW.

1167
00:42:38,400 --> 00:42:39,333
BUT DOES HE NEED A ROOM?

1168
00:42:39,400 --> 00:42:41,100
A MURDERER?
BUT ARE THE POLICE--

1169
00:42:41,167 --> 00:42:42,333
DON'T ARGUE, GRANDPA.
JUST GET OUT OF THERE.

1170
00:42:42,400 --> 00:42:43,900
THIS CALL IS COMING
FROM INSIDE THE HOUSE!

1171
00:42:43,967 --> 00:42:45,633
WE'RE GOING TO THE CITY HALL
POLICE STATION RIGHT NOW.

1172
00:42:45,700 --> 00:42:47,067
MEET US THERE.

1173
00:42:47,133 --> 00:42:49,100
DON'T WORRY ABOUT ME, BETTY.
I'LL LEAVE RIGHT AWAY.

1174
00:42:49,167 --> 00:42:50,433
I'LL PACK A BAG OF TRUSSES
AND BE OUT IN A MINUTE.

1175
00:42:50,500 --> 00:42:51,467
GOOD-BYE, HONEY.

1176
00:42:51,533 --> 00:42:52,500
AAH!

1177
00:42:52,567 --> 00:42:54,333
[MUFFLED SHOUTING]

1178
00:42:54,400 --> 00:42:55,800
I BETTER CALL
THE POLICE AND LET THEM
KNOW WE'RE COMING.

1179
00:42:55,867 --> 00:42:56,867
NICKELS,
CHECK FOR NICKELS!

1180
00:42:56,933 --> 00:42:58,100
WITH WHAT WEAPONS ARE THEY
EQUIPPED?

1181
00:42:58,167 --> 00:42:59,667
WITH GUNS, WHY?

1182
00:42:59,733 --> 00:43:00,800
GUNS THAT EMIT WHAT?

1183
00:43:00,867 --> 00:43:02,033
LOVE! WHY?

1184
00:43:02,100 --> 00:43:03,233
BULLETS.
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

1185
00:43:03,300 --> 00:43:07,367
BULLETS. CENTURIES-OLD
INVENTION AGAINST--

1186
00:43:07,433 --> 00:43:10,967
HELLO, OPERATOR?
GIVE ME THE POLICE
DEPARTMENT, HURRY.

1187
00:43:11,033 --> 00:43:13,800
NOBODY EXPECTS
THE SPANISH INQUISITION!

1188
00:43:13,867 --> 00:43:17,233
MIXED WEAPONRY, UH,
FIGURE IT'S A SURPRISE.

1189
00:43:17,300 --> 00:43:18,767
WOW, THIS IS PRETTY NICE.

1190
00:43:18,833 --> 00:43:21,000
I DON'T THINK I WANT TO
DESTROY THIS HOUSE AFTER ALL.

1191
00:43:21,067 --> 00:43:23,400
BOY, IT SURE
IS A NICE PLACE.

1192
00:43:23,467 --> 00:43:24,933
A GUY COULD REALLY
RENT A ROOM HERE.

1193
00:43:25,000 --> 00:43:26,067
HMM, HMM.

1194
00:43:26,133 --> 00:43:28,100
SURE WOULD LIKE TO RENT
ONE OF THESE ROOMS.

1195
00:43:28,167 --> 00:43:29,567
♪ OOH DOO DOO DOO ♪

1196
00:43:29,633 --> 00:43:32,900
♪♪

1197
00:43:32,967 --> 00:43:34,600
YES, WE'LL BE THERE
RIGHT AWAY.

1198
00:43:34,667 --> 00:43:36,067
THANK YOU.

1199
00:43:36,133 --> 00:43:37,567
BETTY, TELL ME
HOW TO GO THERE.

1200
00:43:37,633 --> 00:43:40,767
I WANT YOU TO GO SOMEWHERE ELSE
WHERE YOU WILL BE SAFE.

1201
00:43:40,833 --> 00:43:42,967
WHERE'S SAFER
THAN THE CITY HALL?

1202
00:43:43,033 --> 00:43:45,000
THE POLICE SAID THEY'RE
GOING TO HAVE ARMED GUARDS

1203
00:43:45,067 --> 00:43:46,833
WAITING FOR US
ON THE FRONT STEPS.

1204
00:43:46,900 --> 00:43:48,400
I TOLD THEM
WE'D BE RIGHT THERE.

1205
00:43:48,467 --> 00:43:49,500
LET'S HURRY.

1206
00:43:49,567 --> 00:43:50,900
THEY'RE SCURRYING!

1207
00:43:50,967 --> 00:43:53,467
♪ I THINKING
IT'S THE NEW ZOO REVUE ♪

1208
00:43:53,533 --> 00:43:55,033
♪ COMING AFTER YOU ♪

1209
00:43:55,100 --> 00:43:56,300
OH, HO HO HO HO!

1210
00:43:56,367 --> 00:44:01,867
♪♪

1211
00:44:06,067 --> 00:44:07,500
ALL RIGHT, YOU GUYS,
THE WASTE RECEPTACLE'S
IN POSITION.

1212
00:44:07,567 --> 00:44:08,500
ARE YOU READY?

1213
00:44:08,567 --> 00:44:09,967
ROGER!

1214
00:44:10,033 --> 00:44:13,100
OKAY, I'M ABOUT TO
JETTISON THE SNACKS
INTO SPACE!

1215
00:44:13,167 --> 00:44:17,033
OH, BOY, HERE THEY GO.
[IMITATES RAPID FIRING]

1216
00:44:17,100 --> 00:44:18,733
♪ DAH DAH DAH DAH
DAH DAH DAH DAH ♪

1217
00:44:18,800 --> 00:44:20,300
♪ DAH DAH DAH
DAH DAH DAH DAH DAH ♪

1218
00:44:20,367 --> 00:44:22,700
♪ DAH DAH DAH DAH DAH
DAH DAH DAH DAH ♪

1219
00:44:22,767 --> 00:44:24,433
♪ DAH DAH DAH DAH
DAH DAH DAH DAH ♪

1220
00:44:24,500 --> 00:44:25,800
♪ DAH DAH DAH
DAH DAH DAH DAH DAH ♪

1221
00:44:25,867 --> 00:44:28,767
♪ DAH DAH DAH DAH
DAH DAH DAH DAH ♪

1222
00:44:28,833 --> 00:44:34,400
♪ DAH DAH DAH DAH DAH DAH
DAHHHHH ♪

1223
00:44:34,467 --> 00:44:35,567
♪ DAH DAH DAH DAH ♪

1224
00:44:35,633 --> 00:44:37,867
THERE IS NO SMOKING
IN THIS AUDITORIUM.

1225
00:44:37,933 --> 00:44:39,800
♪ DAH DAH DAH DAH
DAH DAH DAH DAH ♪

1226
00:44:39,867 --> 00:44:42,100
AND NOW WE INVITE YOU
TO ENJOY OUR FEATURE
PRESENTATION...

1227
00:44:42,167 --> 00:44:43,500
♪ TAH DAH ♪

1228
00:44:43,567 --> 00:44:46,000
♪ DAH ♪

1229
00:44:46,067 --> 00:44:48,733
[OVERLAPPING SHOUTING]

1230
00:44:48,800 --> 00:44:55,733
[MECHANICAL WHIRRING]

1231
00:44:57,900 --> 00:45:00,033
♪ DOO DOO DOO
DOO DOO DOO DOO DOO ♪

1232
00:45:00,100 --> 00:45:01,300
[LAUGHS]

1233
00:45:01,367 --> 00:45:03,200
ALIEN CROSSING.

1234
00:45:03,267 --> 00:45:05,000
♪♪

1235
00:45:05,067 --> 00:45:08,100
WOW, HE'S GONNA TURN
CITY HALL INTO THE MUSEUM
OF NATURAL HISTORY.

1236
00:45:08,167 --> 00:45:09,100
OOH!

1237
00:45:09,167 --> 00:45:10,500
I GUESS YOU CAN FIGHT
CITY HALL.

1238
00:45:10,567 --> 00:45:11,667
THERE YOU GO.

1239
00:45:11,733 --> 00:45:15,867
SNAP, CRACKLE,
POP, RICO, LEE!

1240
00:45:15,933 --> 00:45:18,000
[DRONING]

1241
00:45:18,067 --> 00:45:19,233
♪˯ DOO DOO DOO ♪

1242
00:45:19,300 --> 00:45:21,067
WATCH OUT, OR HE'LL
TURN YOU INTO A DEAD HEAD.

1243
00:45:21,133 --> 00:45:22,300
WHOA, OH!

1244
00:45:22,367 --> 00:45:24,667
UHH!
ONLY A FLESH WOUND.

1245
00:45:24,733 --> 00:45:25,700
TOO LATE.

1246
00:45:25,767 --> 00:45:27,500
[GUNSHOTS]

1247
00:45:27,567 --> 00:45:29,500
[DRONING]

1248
00:45:29,567 --> 00:45:31,833
AH, I'M HIT! I'M HIT,
CHARLIE, I'M HIT!

1249
00:45:31,900 --> 00:45:33,767
WHAT'S THAT THING
ON HIS HEAD?

1250
00:45:33,833 --> 00:45:35,333
[GUNSHOTS]

1251
00:45:35,400 --> 00:45:36,867
DEREK, NO!

1252
00:45:36,933 --> 00:45:37,933
[GUNSHOTS]

1253
00:45:38,000 --> 00:45:39,200
[GROANS]

1254
00:45:39,267 --> 00:45:41,500
OH, THEY'RE USING
REAL BULLETS, THOSE BASTARDS!

1255
00:45:41,567 --> 00:45:44,033
♪♪

1256
00:45:44,100 --> 00:45:45,067
COVER ME.

1257
00:45:45,133 --> 00:45:46,367
[LAUGHS]

1258
00:45:46,433 --> 00:45:48,300
♪♪

1259
00:45:48,367 --> 00:45:49,433
WELL.

1260
00:45:49,500 --> 00:45:51,700
WELL, THAT WAS FUN.
NOW, WHERE WERE WE?

1261
00:45:51,767 --> 00:45:53,300
SHOULD WE CHASE THEM
OR KNOCK OFF FOR COFFEE?

1262
00:45:53,367 --> 00:45:54,533
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

1263
00:45:54,600 --> 00:45:55,600
HE MUST HAVE SLIPPED OFF
THAT WAY-- COME ON.

1264
00:45:55,667 --> 00:45:56,967
GO HANG BOB
IN MY OFFICE.

1265
00:45:57,033 --> 00:45:58,000
STAY UNDER COVER.

1266
00:45:58,067 --> 00:45:59,600
♪ UNDERCOVER ANGEL ♪

1267
00:45:59,667 --> 00:46:01,267
♪ MIDNIGHT... ♪

1268
00:46:01,333 --> 00:46:05,100
♪♪

1269
00:46:05,167 --> 00:46:08,433
HEY, SCOOP!
HI, THEY WENT THAT-A-WAY.

1270
00:46:08,500 --> 00:46:09,933
JIMMY OLSEN HERE.

1271
00:46:10,000 --> 00:46:12,200
BETTY!
THANK THE LORD YOU'RE SAFE.

1272
00:46:12,267 --> 00:46:13,667
I JUST CAME FROM ALICE'S.

1273
00:46:13,733 --> 00:46:14,867
THERE WAS A SKELETON
IN THE POOL, I--

1274
00:46:14,933 --> 00:46:17,933
ALICE?
OH, NO!

1275
00:46:18,000 --> 00:46:19,367
WE CAME TO MEET GRANDPA.

1276
00:46:19,433 --> 00:46:20,500
A LOT OF GRIEF.

1277
00:46:20,567 --> 00:46:21,567
THE MURDERER CAME
IN THE CAR WITH HIM.

1278
00:46:21,633 --> 00:46:22,667
WHAT?

1279
00:46:22,733 --> 00:46:24,967
BUT HOW DID YOU
GET MIXED UP IN THIS?

1280
00:46:25,033 --> 00:46:27,267
WE THINK THEY KILLED
SPARKY OUT BY THE OLD MINE.

1281
00:46:27,333 --> 00:46:28,767
SHE SOUNDS LIKE BETTY BOOP
ALL OF A SUDDEN.

1282
00:46:28,833 --> 00:46:29,833
HE'S AN INSANE KILLER, JOE!

1283
00:46:29,900 --> 00:46:31,367
AND HE FORCED GRAMPS
TO DRIVE HERE?

1284
00:46:31,433 --> 00:46:33,333
WHERE IS GRAMPS--
IS HE OKAY?

1285
00:46:33,400 --> 00:46:36,033
YES, HE'S-- WELL, THERE
HE IS, TRYING TO GET
ACROSS THE STREET.

1286
00:46:36,100 --> 00:46:37,333
STAY, GRANDPA, STAY!

1287
00:46:37,400 --> 00:46:38,467
YOU STAY PUT.

1288
00:46:38,533 --> 00:46:40,467
I'LL GO OVER
AND HELP HIM ACROSS.

1289
00:46:40,533 --> 00:46:42,500
♪♪

1290
00:46:42,567 --> 00:46:44,533
THAT'S THE LAST
BOY SCOUT.

1291
00:46:44,600 --> 00:46:47,033
♪ I HAVE OFTEN WALKED
DOWN THIS STREET BEFORE ♪

1292
00:46:47,100 --> 00:46:49,500
♪ BUT I'VE NEVER DONE IT
PACKING HEAT BEFORE ♪

1293
00:46:49,567 --> 00:46:51,167
[LAUGHS]

1294
00:46:51,233 --> 00:46:52,367
♪♪

1295
00:46:52,433 --> 00:46:53,633
HEY.

1296
00:46:53,700 --> 00:46:56,100
♪♪

1297
00:46:56,167 --> 00:46:57,433
WHAT ARE YOU
DOING DOWN HERE?

1298
00:46:57,500 --> 00:47:01,500
GO INTO THE BUILDING.
THAT IS THE SAFEST PLACE.

1299
00:47:01,567 --> 00:47:06,000
HMM?
LOOK, LOOK.

1300
00:47:06,067 --> 00:47:07,033
LOOK.

1301
00:47:07,100 --> 00:47:08,200
PICK A CUP OF SAUCE.

1302
00:47:08,267 --> 00:47:09,667
HERE ON THE SIDEWALK.

1303
00:47:09,733 --> 00:47:11,567
DROPS OF BLOOD.

1304
00:47:11,633 --> 00:47:14,100
BETTY,
GO INTO THE BUILDING.

1305
00:47:14,167 --> 00:47:16,167
ONE AT A TIME,
DING-DING-DING.

1306
00:47:16,233 --> 00:47:17,767
DEREK...

1307
00:47:17,833 --> 00:47:19,733
SURPRISE!

1308
00:47:19,800 --> 00:47:21,733
GIVE ME THE WEAPON
YOU HAVE, DEREK.

1309
00:47:21,800 --> 00:47:24,267
HEY, IT'S A TUBE OF CREST.
HE MUST BE A CAVITY FIGHTER.

1310
00:47:24,333 --> 00:47:25,867
ONE SUDDEN MOVE,
AND I SLAY YOU BOTH!

1311
00:47:25,933 --> 00:47:27,167
I'LL TRY TO CONTROL YOU!

1312
00:47:27,233 --> 00:47:29,433
DEREK, DO AS HE SAYS.

1313
00:47:29,500 --> 00:47:32,067
WHAT?

1314
00:47:32,133 --> 00:47:33,267
NICE LUGER.

1315
00:47:33,333 --> 00:47:34,933
GET IN!

1316
00:47:35,000 --> 00:47:37,100
OKAY, OKAY,
I'M GETTING IN!

1317
00:47:37,167 --> 00:47:38,833
JEEZ, WHAT A GROUCH.

1318
00:47:38,900 --> 00:47:40,733
YOU WILL TAKE ME
TO A MAN OF SURGERY

1319
00:47:40,800 --> 00:47:42,533
TO REMOVE THE METAL
PELLETS FROM MY FLESH.

1320
00:47:42,600 --> 00:47:43,700
THAT IS NOT POSSIBLE.

1321
00:47:43,767 --> 00:47:45,200
WELL, IT'S 2:30.
THEY'RE PROBABLY ALL GOLFING.

1322
00:47:45,267 --> 00:47:47,100
WE MUST DO AS HE SAYS.

1323
00:47:47,167 --> 00:47:48,800
I KNOW A DOCTOR'S OFFICE.

1324
00:47:48,867 --> 00:47:50,033
WE'LL TAKE HIM THERE.

1325
00:47:50,100 --> 00:47:51,433
SHE IS VERY WISE.

1326
00:47:51,500 --> 00:47:52,433
OH, YOU LIKE HER?

1327
00:47:52,500 --> 00:47:54,000
NOW GO!

1328
00:47:54,067 --> 00:47:57,533
HEY, AND A WANT
A JOLLY RANCHER FIRE STICK
WHEN I'M DONE, TOO.

1329
00:47:57,600 --> 00:48:00,600
♪♪

1330
00:48:00,667 --> 00:48:04,367
WATCH YOUR SPACE CUSHION.
SLOW, SLOW. I DON'T--OH.

1331
00:48:04,433 --> 00:48:05,433
AND THAT'S THE WAY
IT HAPPENED.

1332
00:48:05,500 --> 00:48:06,433
I'M WALTER CRONKITE.

1333
00:48:06,500 --> 00:48:07,867
NEXT THING I KNEW,

1334
00:48:07,933 --> 00:48:09,133
HE WAS TRYING TO FIRE OUT THE
WINDOW AT BETTY AND DEREK.

1335
00:48:09,200 --> 00:48:10,300
HE'S TALKING
TO CLIFFORD IRVING.

1336
00:48:10,367 --> 00:48:12,333
I SWERVED THE CAR AND--

1337
00:48:12,400 --> 00:48:14,667
SAY, WHERE IS BETTY?

1338
00:48:14,733 --> 00:48:16,100
WHERE IS BETTY?

1339
00:48:16,167 --> 00:48:19,433
THAT'S FUNNY. SHE MUST BE
AROUND SOMEPLACE.

1340
00:48:19,500 --> 00:48:21,167
BUT THE CAR IS GONE.

1341
00:48:21,233 --> 00:48:22,567
THEY MUST HAVE LEFT
WITHOUT ME.

1342
00:48:22,633 --> 00:48:23,967
GET THE HINT, GRAMPS?

1343
00:48:24,033 --> 00:48:26,933
WELL, DON'T WORRY, GRAMPS.
YOU'LL GET AN ESCORT HOME.

1344
00:48:27,000 --> 00:48:29,133
I'M GOING TO PHONE
THE STORY IN TO THE PAPER

1345
00:48:29,200 --> 00:48:31,300
AND THEN DRIVE OUT TO THE OLD
MINE BETTY MENTIONED.

1346
00:48:31,367 --> 00:48:33,367
THE OLD MINE?
WHAT'S OUT THERE?

1347
00:48:33,433 --> 00:48:34,700
I DON'T KNOW.

1348
00:48:34,767 --> 00:48:36,867
THAT'S WHERE SHE SAID SPARKY
WAS KILLED BY THE GUY.

1349
00:48:36,933 --> 00:48:38,000
HOW COME I ALWAYS HAVE TO
DO THE EXPOSITIONS?

1350
00:48:38,067 --> 00:48:39,100
SPARKY, OUR DOG?

1351
00:48:39,167 --> 00:48:40,867
SHE DIDN'T TELL ME
ABOUT THAT.

1352
00:48:40,933 --> 00:48:43,067
HEY, MAC, OVER HERE!

1353
00:48:43,133 --> 00:48:44,567
BLOOD SPOTS
ON THE SIDEWALK.

1354
00:48:44,633 --> 00:48:45,767
A CAR HAS BEEN
BLEEDING HERE.

1355
00:48:45,833 --> 00:48:46,933
AND WHERE'S THAT CAR
THAT WAS PARKED HERE?

1356
00:48:47,000 --> 00:48:49,267
THAT'S IT. THAT'S HOW
THE KILLER GOT AWAY.

1357
00:48:49,333 --> 00:48:50,733
IN OUR CAR?

1358
00:48:50,800 --> 00:48:54,433
THEN BETTY AND DEREK,
THEY MUST HAVE BEEN KIDNAPPED!

1359
00:48:54,500 --> 00:48:55,833
YOU'VE GOT TO DO SOMETHING!

1360
00:48:55,900 --> 00:48:57,567
YOU'VE GOT TO FIND THEM.

1361
00:48:57,633 --> 00:48:58,833
D'OH.

1362
00:48:58,900 --> 00:49:02,900
♪ HOT CHILD IN THE CITY ♪

1363
00:49:02,967 --> 00:49:03,933
THIS IS IT, DEREK.

1364
00:49:04,000 --> 00:49:05,333
THAT'S DR. BRANDT THERE.

1365
00:49:05,400 --> 00:49:06,500
HE LOOKS LIKE HE'S LEAVING.

1366
00:49:06,567 --> 00:49:08,067
STOP HIM-- BLOCK HIS PATH!

1367
00:49:08,133 --> 00:49:09,367
♪♪

1368
00:49:09,433 --> 00:49:11,000
♪ LOOKIN' GOOD
AND FEELIN' PRETTY ♪

1369
00:49:11,067 --> 00:49:12,700
[TIRES SCREECH]

1370
00:49:12,767 --> 00:49:15,533
HEY, YOU BLOCKED
MY PATH!

1371
00:49:15,600 --> 00:49:16,967
IS THERE SOME EMERGENCY?

1372
00:49:17,033 --> 00:49:18,533
I HAVE A HOUSE CALL
TO MAKE.

1373
00:49:18,600 --> 00:49:20,300
OFFICE HOURS DON'T
BEGIN FOR ANOTHER HOUR.

1374
00:49:20,367 --> 00:49:21,867
[THOR]
GO INSIDE, ALL OF YOU!

1375
00:49:21,933 --> 00:49:24,133
I SAY, WHAT IS THIS?

1376
00:49:24,200 --> 00:49:25,300
AND YOU SAY IT
RATHER WOODENLY.

1377
00:49:25,367 --> 00:49:26,967
HE'S HOLDING A GUN
ON US, DR. BRANDT.

1378
00:49:27,033 --> 00:49:28,633
WE HAD TO BRING HIM HERE.

1379
00:49:28,700 --> 00:49:30,100
OH, I SEE IT NOW.

1380
00:49:30,167 --> 00:49:32,233
HE WANTS BULLETS REMOVED.

1381
00:49:32,300 --> 00:49:33,667
I SEE.

1382
00:49:33,733 --> 00:49:34,867
WELL, I DON'T SEE, BUT...

1383
00:49:34,933 --> 00:49:36,333
I'M AFRAID
I CANNOT BE OF ANY HELP.

1384
00:49:36,400 --> 00:49:37,633
YOU WILL NEED HOSPITAL
FACILITIES FOR ANYTHING--

1385
00:49:37,700 --> 00:49:39,867
BE SILENT AND GET INSIDE!

1386
00:49:39,933 --> 00:49:42,200
YOU WILL REMOVE THE PELLETS
HERE, NOW.

1387
00:49:42,267 --> 00:49:44,200
LEAVE THESE PEOPLE
ALONE, THOR.

1388
00:49:44,267 --> 00:49:45,333
HE'S SO GENTLE.

1389
00:49:45,400 --> 00:49:47,333
WHERE IS OUR SHIP?
I WILL TAKE YOU THERE.

1390
00:49:47,400 --> 00:49:49,533
NO, IT IS GONE.
DO AS I SAY!

1391
00:49:49,600 --> 00:49:51,533
DEREK, PLEASE.

1392
00:49:51,600 --> 00:49:53,533
DOCTOR, YOU MUST TRY.

1393
00:49:53,600 --> 00:49:57,100
HMM...HMM...
AH, CRIMINY, COME ON, DUMMY.

1394
00:49:57,167 --> 00:50:01,200
I WAS GOING TO A HAT PARTY.
MINE WAS THE GRANDEST
OF ALL, TOO.

1395
00:50:01,267 --> 00:50:03,933
BIG FEATHER BOA
IN THE BACK, TOO.

1396
00:50:04,000 --> 00:50:06,400
♪♪

1397
00:50:06,467 --> 00:50:08,233
NOW, YOU'LL HAVE TO
WAIT AN HOUR.

1398
00:50:08,300 --> 00:50:10,200
IT'S STANDARD PROCEDURE.

1399
00:50:10,267 --> 00:50:11,567
♪♪

1400
00:50:11,633 --> 00:50:13,300
AH, SORRY ABOUT THE MESS.

1401
00:50:13,367 --> 00:50:14,867
THIS KIND OF DOUBLES
AS MY ROOM.

1402
00:50:14,933 --> 00:50:16,400
I'VE JUST GOT TO CLEAN
A FEW THINGS UP HERE.

1403
00:50:16,467 --> 00:50:17,967
YOU WILL HAVE TO
LIE DOWN HERE.

1404
00:50:18,033 --> 00:50:20,967
I WILL PREPARE AN ANESTHETIC.
THE PAIN WILL BE GREAT.

1405
00:50:21,033 --> 00:50:22,467
I WILL NOT BE DRUGGED.

1406
00:50:22,533 --> 00:50:24,400
YOU WILL SIMPLY
REMOVE THE PELLETS.

1407
00:50:24,467 --> 00:50:27,033
WELL, I WON'T BE
USING THIS THEN.

1408
00:50:27,100 --> 00:50:30,000
BOTH OF YOU, SIT THERE.
I SHALL KEEP YOU COVERED.

1409
00:50:30,067 --> 00:50:31,600
I DID NOT SAY,
"SIMON SAYS."

1410
00:50:31,667 --> 00:50:35,300
TAKE HEED. ONE TREACHEROUS
MOVE, AND THEY PAY WITH
THEIR LIVES.

1411
00:50:35,367 --> 00:50:36,867
NOW PROCEED.

1412
00:50:36,933 --> 00:50:38,867
IN IAMBIC PENTAMETER.

1413
00:50:38,933 --> 00:50:42,333
SHALL I COMPARE THEE
TO A FLESHY WOUND?

1414
00:50:42,400 --> 00:50:44,800
HEY, WHAT'S A TURKEY ROASTING
PAN DOING IN THE OFFICE?

1415
00:50:44,867 --> 00:50:46,100
I DON'T KNOW.

1416
00:50:46,167 --> 00:50:51,333
IF HE DIES,
THEY CAN MAKE SOUP.

1417
00:50:51,400 --> 00:50:54,167
HEY, YOU'RE PUT TOGETHER
ALL DIFFERENTLY.

1418
00:50:54,233 --> 00:50:56,133
YOU'RE A WILLOWY YOUNG THING,
AREN'T YOU?

1419
00:50:56,200 --> 00:50:57,133
♪♪

1420
00:50:57,200 --> 00:50:58,767
HE LIKES THAT.

1421
00:50:58,833 --> 00:51:02,433
OH, LOOKS LIKE YOUR
POPPER'S COME UP. OH,
THAT'S YOUR NIPPLE.

1422
00:51:02,500 --> 00:51:03,467
THOR...

1423
00:51:03,533 --> 00:51:04,867
YETH, IT IS VERY THOR.

1424
00:51:04,933 --> 00:51:07,367
TELL ME WHY YOU HAVE BEEN
SEARCHING FOR ME.

1425
00:51:07,433 --> 00:51:09,633
IT MUST HAVE BEEN IMPORTANT
FOR YOU TO HAVE--

1426
00:51:09,700 --> 00:51:11,367
THE GARGON
HAD TO BE RAISED HERE.

1427
00:51:11,433 --> 00:51:13,600
OH, YEAH, THE LOBSTERS.
I FORGOT.

1428
00:51:13,667 --> 00:51:15,633
YOU COULD NOT BE
ALLOWED TO RUN FREE.

1429
00:51:15,700 --> 00:51:19,267
BUT THE SPECIMEN
REACTION WAS NEGATIVE.

1430
00:51:19,333 --> 00:51:23,033
IT WAS VERIFIED POSITIVE
AFTER YOU ESCAPED.

1431
00:51:23,100 --> 00:51:25,000
THE CAPTAIN SHOULD HAVE
LET ME KILL YOU

1432
00:51:25,067 --> 00:51:26,600
WHEN I HAD THE CHANCE!

1433
00:51:26,667 --> 00:51:28,633
AND WHY DIDN'T HE?

1434
00:51:28,700 --> 00:51:30,767
I SAW HIM STOP YOU WHEN YOU
FIRED AT ME.

1435
00:51:30,833 --> 00:51:31,800
BECAUSE--

1436
00:51:31,867 --> 00:51:33,033
HE LIKES THE CUT
OF YOUR JIB.

1437
00:51:33,100 --> 00:51:35,167
BECAUSE HE JUST LEARNED
THAT--

1438
00:51:35,233 --> 00:51:37,600
THAT YOU ARE
THE SON OF OUR LEADER.

1439
00:51:37,667 --> 00:51:39,767
I'M DAVID EISENHOWER.

1440
00:51:39,833 --> 00:51:42,567
THAT MAKES YOU
JULIE NIXON!

1441
00:51:42,633 --> 00:51:44,967
♪♪

1442
00:51:45,033 --> 00:51:49,000
HUH, A CIGARETTE BUTT.
WHAT THE HELL IS THAT
DOING IN THERE?

1443
00:51:49,067 --> 00:51:52,367
♪♪

1444
00:51:52,433 --> 00:51:54,833
SUDDENLY IT'S
CARNIVAL OF SOULS.

1445
00:51:54,900 --> 00:51:57,833
♪♪

1446
00:51:57,900 --> 00:51:59,100
[GASPS]
LOOK!

1447
00:51:59,167 --> 00:52:01,067
OH, OH, COME ON,
COME ON.

1448
00:52:01,133 --> 00:52:04,367
YES, YES, YES, COME ON,
BABY, COME ON.

1449
00:52:04,433 --> 00:52:09,533
COME ON, OH, OH, OH, UH,
AW.

1450
00:52:09,600 --> 00:52:11,667
THEN IF I AM
NOT TO BE KILLED,

1451
00:52:11,733 --> 00:52:13,733
WHY DID YOU FIRE AT ME
IN THE CITY?

1452
00:52:13,800 --> 00:52:16,700
YOUR LIFE OR DEATH
WAS PUT IN MY HANDS.

1453
00:52:16,767 --> 00:52:19,833
A TRAITOR DOES NOT DESERVE
TO BE OUR NEXT LEADER!

1454
00:52:19,900 --> 00:52:22,133
THE ONLY REASON
YOU DO NOT FIRE NOW

1455
00:52:22,200 --> 00:52:24,833
IS TO FORCE ATTENTION
TO YOUR WOUNDS.

1456
00:52:24,900 --> 00:52:28,067
WHEN THAT IS DONE...

1457
00:52:28,133 --> 00:52:29,767
PROCEED!

1458
00:52:29,833 --> 00:52:33,400
OH, OKAY,
LET'S SEE HERE.
REMOVE FUNNY BONE.

1459
00:52:33,467 --> 00:52:36,167
HA HA HA.

1460
00:52:36,233 --> 00:52:39,733
WELL, HERE'S THE LITTLE
BUGGER THAT WAS CAUSING
ALL THE TROUBLE.

1461
00:52:39,800 --> 00:52:41,767
♪♪

1462
00:52:41,833 --> 00:52:43,600
OKAY, HOP DOWN.
PUT YOUR CLOTHES ON.

1463
00:52:43,667 --> 00:52:45,067
ANTISEPTIC MUST BE
APPLIED TO YOUR WOUNDS,

1464
00:52:45,133 --> 00:52:46,533
AND YOU WILL NEED BANDAGES.

1465
00:52:46,600 --> 00:52:49,100
I RECOMMEND SEA BREEZE
ASTRINGENT.

1466
00:52:49,167 --> 00:52:50,500
♪♪

1467
00:52:50,567 --> 00:52:52,800
HMM, NO INSURANCE.
SAD, REALLY.

1468
00:52:52,867 --> 00:52:56,267
♪ HOT BLOODED,
CHECK IT AND SEE ♪

1469
00:52:56,333 --> 00:52:58,133
♪♪

1470
00:52:58,200 --> 00:53:00,267
[GROANING]

1471
00:53:00,333 --> 00:53:02,667
AUNTIE EM, UNCLE HENRY,
YOU WERE THERE

1472
00:53:02,733 --> 00:53:04,433
AND YOU AND YOU AND YOU...

1473
00:53:04,500 --> 00:53:05,600
♪♪

1474
00:53:05,667 --> 00:53:09,167
YEAH, ALL RIGHT.

1475
00:53:09,233 --> 00:53:10,200
YES!

1476
00:53:10,267 --> 00:53:11,233
OH!

1477
00:53:11,300 --> 00:53:13,800
WHERE WAS I ON THE NIGHT
OF THE 14TH?

1478
00:53:13,867 --> 00:53:16,100
♪♪

1479
00:53:16,167 --> 00:53:18,767
COME BACK!
I--I'LL FIND YOU.

1480
00:53:20,833 --> 00:53:23,800
IT'S BRYAN FERRY!
LOVE IS THE DRUG FOR HIM!

1481
00:53:23,867 --> 00:53:26,067
[GRUNTING]

1482
00:53:26,133 --> 00:53:28,000
[WEAKLY]
YOU'RE IN HERE.

1483
00:53:28,067 --> 00:53:29,300
I KNOW YOU ARE.

1484
00:53:29,367 --> 00:53:30,967
BUT WHAT AM I?

1485
00:53:31,033 --> 00:53:32,300
I'LL FIND YOU!

1486
00:53:32,367 --> 00:53:33,467
AND THEN YOU'LL BE IT!

1487
00:53:33,533 --> 00:53:35,233
HMM.

1488
00:53:35,300 --> 00:53:36,900
[BRAKES SCREECH]

1489
00:53:36,967 --> 00:53:38,767
ALL RIGHT, THIS IS
YOUR STOP, GRANDPA.

1490
00:53:38,833 --> 00:53:41,333
OUT, BABY--
OUT, OUT, OUT!

1491
00:53:41,400 --> 00:53:43,967
♪♪

1492
00:53:44,033 --> 00:53:45,500
MY NURSE, MISS MORSE!

1493
00:53:45,567 --> 00:53:47,467
SHE'LL BE ARRIVING
FOR OFFICE HOURS.

1494
00:53:47,533 --> 00:53:49,767
BOY, THE OLD GUY MOVES
WHEN HE WANTS TO.

1495
00:53:49,833 --> 00:53:51,767
YEAH, GOOD TRUSS ON HIM.

1496
00:53:51,833 --> 00:53:53,167
[PANTING]

1497
00:53:53,233 --> 00:53:56,400
UHH!
GOT TO SOLVE THE JUMBLE!

1498
00:53:56,467 --> 00:53:57,900
I CAN HEAR YOU!

1499
00:53:57,967 --> 00:54:01,367
TOMMY, I CAN HEAR YOU.
I CAN FEEL YOU NEAR ME.

1500
00:54:01,433 --> 00:54:04,167
YOU--YOU CANNOT ESCAPE ME!

1501
00:54:04,233 --> 00:54:07,500
I'M CHARLES FOSTER KANE!

1502
00:54:07,567 --> 00:54:09,800
I'LL FIND YOU,
I'LL FIND YOU,
I'LL FIND YOU!

1503
00:54:09,867 --> 00:54:14,167
THERE YOU ARE--YOU'RE
IN A SAILBOAT OVER THE--
UHH!

1504
00:54:14,233 --> 00:54:16,933
OH, HERE COMES
THE S.S. NURSE.

1505
00:54:17,000 --> 00:54:19,767
♪˯ GA-DING-A-DING A-DING-DING,
DING-A-DING A-DING ♪

1506
00:54:19,833 --> 00:54:21,600
♪˯ DING-A-DING A-DING
DING DING ♪

1507
00:54:21,667 --> 00:54:23,267
HERE WE GO, FOLKS.

1508
00:54:23,333 --> 00:54:24,667
♪♪

1509
00:54:24,733 --> 00:54:27,000
♪ YES, I'M A SEX SHOOTER ♪

1510
00:54:27,067 --> 00:54:29,267
♪ SHOOTING LOVE
IN YOUR DIRECTION ♪

1511
00:54:29,333 --> 00:54:30,267
[HUMMING]

1512
00:54:30,333 --> 00:54:31,267
HMM?

1513
00:54:31,333 --> 00:54:32,433
WHAT?

1514
00:54:32,500 --> 00:54:34,167
OH, THE DOCTOR LEFT
ANOTHER YOUNG ONE

1515
00:54:34,233 --> 00:54:35,633
BLEEDING ON THE STOOP
AGAIN.

1516
00:54:35,700 --> 00:54:37,433
AH!

1517
00:54:37,500 --> 00:54:40,800
HAVE YOU BEEN
WAITING LONG, HMM?

1518
00:54:40,867 --> 00:54:43,500
DR. BRANDT!
DR. BRANDT!

1519
00:54:43,567 --> 00:54:45,667
THERE'S A DEAD SPACEMAN
TO SEE YOU, SIR.

1520
00:54:45,733 --> 00:54:48,333
♪♪

1521
00:54:48,400 --> 00:54:50,533
♪ DOO DOO DOO DOO DOO ♪

1522
00:54:50,600 --> 00:54:51,867
♪ SNOT IS RUNNING DOWN
YOUR... ♪

1523
00:54:51,933 --> 00:54:54,167
SHE'S ALREADY LEFT?

1524
00:54:54,233 --> 00:54:55,767
OKAY, GOOD-BYE, THEN.

1525
00:54:55,833 --> 00:54:56,800
UHH!

1526
00:54:56,867 --> 00:54:58,467
NOT VERY COURTEOUS.

1527
00:54:58,533 --> 00:55:01,233
HMM, WESSON OIL
ON A WOUND?

1528
00:55:01,300 --> 00:55:03,233
YEAH, SHE'S NOT
FLORENCE NIGHTINGALE,
SHE'S FLORENCE HENDERSON.

1529
00:55:03,300 --> 00:55:04,733
OH!

1530
00:55:04,800 --> 00:55:06,767
[PHONE RINGING]

1531
00:55:06,833 --> 00:55:10,433
OH, EVERY TIME
I'M ABOUT TO SWAB.

1532
00:55:10,500 --> 00:55:12,567
[RINGING CONTINUES]

1533
00:55:12,633 --> 00:55:17,867
♪ PICTURE YOURSELF
ON A TRAIN IN THE STATION ♪

1534
00:55:17,933 --> 00:55:20,300
♪ MMMM MMMM MMM ♪

1535
00:55:20,367 --> 00:55:23,233
♪ AND MARSHMALLOWS
AND MMMM ♪

1536
00:55:23,300 --> 00:55:27,067
♪˯ I DON'T GIVE A DAMN,
THE NEXT STEP IS VIETNAM ♪

1537
00:55:27,133 --> 00:55:29,300
HMM?

1538
00:55:29,367 --> 00:55:32,433
[RINGING CONTINUES]

1539
00:55:32,500 --> 00:55:33,467
HMM.

1540
00:55:33,533 --> 00:55:35,200
IT MUST BE THAT NICE
ADAM RICH BOY

1541
00:55:35,267 --> 00:55:36,967
CALLING FOR HIS
PRESCRIPTION AGAIN.

1542
00:55:37,033 --> 00:55:38,133
[RINGING]

1543
00:55:38,200 --> 00:55:39,733
♪ HEY DOO DOO DOO OH ♪

1544
00:55:39,800 --> 00:55:41,500
DR. BRANDT'S OFFICE.

1545
00:55:41,567 --> 00:55:43,967
MISS MORSE, THANK HEAVENS
I'VE REACHED YOU.

1546
00:55:44,033 --> 00:55:45,000
THIS IS DR. BRANDT.

1547
00:55:45,067 --> 00:55:46,667
WHERE ARE YOU, DOCTOR?

1548
00:55:46,733 --> 00:55:48,167
THERE'S AN EMERGENCY
PATIENT HERE.

1549
00:55:48,233 --> 00:55:49,333
I'VE DONE ALL I CAN--

1550
00:55:49,400 --> 00:55:51,733
LISTEN, MISS MORSE,
HE'S A MURDERER.

1551
00:55:51,800 --> 00:55:53,133
'CAUSE PEPPERIDGE FARM
REMEMBERS.

1552
00:55:53,200 --> 00:55:54,833
HE HELD HOSTAGES AT GUNPOINT TO
FORCE ME TO REMOVE BULLETS.

1553
00:55:54,900 --> 00:55:57,800
WE WERE FORTUNATE IN ESCAPING.
YOU MUST GET OUT OF THERE.

1554
00:55:57,867 --> 00:55:59,200
A "MORDEWER"?

1555
00:55:59,267 --> 00:56:01,100
NO, I SAID MURDERER!

1556
00:56:01,167 --> 00:56:02,667
IF YOU'VE TREATED HIM,
HE COULD REVIVE AT ANY MOMENT.

1557
00:56:02,733 --> 00:56:05,667
Y-YES, DOCTOR.
I'LL LEAVE IMMEDIATELY.

1558
00:56:05,733 --> 00:56:08,567
YOU WILL COME WITH ME.
PUT THAT DOWN!

1559
00:56:08,633 --> 00:56:10,200
MISS MORSE, MISS MORSE,
WHAT IS IT?

1560
00:56:10,267 --> 00:56:11,633
HE DOESN'T HAVE
ANY INSURANCE!

1561
00:56:11,700 --> 00:56:13,433
AND DON'T LIFT A FINGER!

1562
00:56:13,500 --> 00:56:14,667
WHAT DO YOU WANT?

1563
00:56:14,733 --> 00:56:16,533
YOU WILL HELP ME TO ESCAPE.

1564
00:56:16,600 --> 00:56:17,800
GO OUT!

1565
00:56:17,867 --> 00:56:19,200
WAIT A MINUTE!
MISS MORSE!

1566
00:56:19,267 --> 00:56:21,500
JUST LEAVE YOUR BONES
BY THE DOOR!

1567
00:56:21,567 --> 00:56:24,167
MISS MORSE!
MISS MORSE!

1568
00:56:24,233 --> 00:56:26,167
♪♪

1569
00:56:26,233 --> 00:56:29,567
NOBODY ELSE PULL A RAYGUN.
YOU PUT THAT RIGHT AWAY.

1570
00:56:29,633 --> 00:56:32,900
THAT VEHICLE.
IS THAT HOW YOU ARRIVED?

1571
00:56:32,967 --> 00:56:33,933
YES, THAT'S MY CAR.

1572
00:56:34,000 --> 00:56:34,933
IN STYLE.

1573
00:56:35,000 --> 00:56:37,533
GET IN. YOU WILL TAKE ME
WHERE I SAY.

1574
00:56:37,600 --> 00:56:39,800
IF YOU DISOBEY,
YOU WILL BE KILLED!

1575
00:56:39,867 --> 00:56:44,067
I HOPE YOUR BANDAGES
STICK TO YOUR SCABS,
YOU SON OF A...

1576
00:56:44,133 --> 00:56:47,333
THE POLICE ARE ON THE WAY,
DR. BRANDT. THEY--

1577
00:56:47,400 --> 00:56:49,033
IT'S NO USE.

1578
00:56:49,100 --> 00:56:50,367
I WAS TOO LATE.

1579
00:56:50,433 --> 00:56:51,667
THEY'RE GONE.

1580
00:56:51,733 --> 00:56:52,833
I WASN'T
THE FIFTH CALLER.

1581
00:56:52,900 --> 00:56:54,100
THOR HAS ESCAPED?

1582
00:56:54,167 --> 00:56:55,433
BUT HOW COULD HE?

1583
00:56:55,500 --> 00:56:57,100
YOU SAID HE WOULD BE
HELPLESS, THAT--

1584
00:56:57,167 --> 00:57:00,467
WITHOUT AID, BUT MY NURSE,
SHE DIDN'T KNOW.

1585
00:57:00,533 --> 00:57:04,100
SHE BANDAGED HIM,
GAVE HIM AN INJECTION.

1586
00:57:04,167 --> 00:57:05,767
HE REVIVED.

1587
00:57:05,833 --> 00:57:06,800
OH, NO.

1588
00:57:06,867 --> 00:57:08,033
THEN THEY PLAYED
JIMI HENDRIX.

1589
00:57:08,100 --> 00:57:09,800
ALL DAY AT BLACK ROCK,
EH?

1590
00:57:09,867 --> 00:57:11,867
WELL, WE'VE GOT TO TELL
THE POLICE. THEY MIGHT BE
ABLE TO DO SOMETHING.

1591
00:57:11,933 --> 00:57:12,933
I'LL TELL THEM.

1592
00:57:13,000 --> 00:57:14,033
NO, NO,
THAT WOULD BE TELLING.

1593
00:57:14,100 --> 00:57:15,533
I'LL TELL THEM
WHAT HAPPENED.

1594
00:57:15,600 --> 00:57:18,800
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,
CHARLES SCHULTZ
PREMIERING PEANUTS.

1595
00:57:18,867 --> 00:57:19,833
♪♪

1596
00:57:19,900 --> 00:57:21,033
WHO ARE YOU AGAIN?

1597
00:57:21,100 --> 00:57:23,767
OH, MY GIRLFRIEND.
OKAY.

1598
00:57:23,833 --> 00:57:26,933
OH, HAVE I GOT
A NERVOUS TUMMY.

1599
00:57:27,000 --> 00:57:29,500
THE THINKER.

1600
00:57:29,567 --> 00:57:32,800
DON'T WORRY, DEREK.
THOR WILL BE CAUGHT.

1601
00:57:32,867 --> 00:57:35,133
THEY'RE SURE TO FIND HIM
EVENTUALLY.

1602
00:57:35,200 --> 00:57:37,133
IT IS WHAT I KNOW
IS COMING HERE.

1603
00:57:37,200 --> 00:57:38,133
LEND ME A TENNER?

1604
00:57:38,200 --> 00:57:39,600
THE GARGON.

1605
00:57:39,667 --> 00:57:41,000
THEY ARE SMALL
WHEN YOUNG...

1606
00:57:41,067 --> 00:57:42,367
BUT THEY'LL CLAW YA.

1607
00:57:42,433 --> 00:57:44,667
BUT THEY CAN ATTAIN THE--
THE SIZE OF THIS BUILDING

1608
00:57:44,733 --> 00:57:46,700
IN NO MORE THAN A DAY.

1609
00:57:46,767 --> 00:57:48,867
BUT CAN'T YOU STOP THEM?

1610
00:57:48,933 --> 00:57:50,433
ONLY IF THEY'RE WILLING
TO STOP THEMSELVES.

1611
00:57:50,500 --> 00:57:52,400
THE ONLY CHANCE
IS TO DUPLICATE

1612
00:57:52,467 --> 00:57:54,133
THE OPERATION
OF THE DISINTEGRATOR.

1613
00:57:54,200 --> 00:57:56,000
WE'LL NEED A SHOESTRING
AND A PICTURE OF EVE ARDEN.

1614
00:57:56,067 --> 00:57:57,267
HOW CAN THAT BE DONE?

1615
00:57:57,333 --> 00:57:58,500
THE MEN OF SCIENCE HERE
MIGHT BE ABLE TO DO IT

1616
00:57:58,567 --> 00:58:00,700
IF THEY COULD GET
THOR'S AS A MODEL.

1617
00:58:00,767 --> 00:58:03,667
IF ONLY THERE IS
ENOUGH TIME.

1618
00:58:03,733 --> 00:58:06,367
YOU KNOW,
THIS LITTLE DOG HAS BECOME

1619
00:58:06,433 --> 00:58:07,433
QUITE A TOURIST ATTRACTION
AROUND HERE.

1620
00:58:07,500 --> 00:58:08,633
AH, YUP.

1621
00:58:08,700 --> 00:58:09,633
ARF.

1622
00:58:09,700 --> 00:58:10,733
YOU KNOW,
I DON'T GET THIS GUY.

1623
00:58:10,800 --> 00:58:12,100
IT'S NOT A GUY,
IT'S A DOG.

1624
00:58:12,167 --> 00:58:15,000
ANIMALS OR HUMANS,
HE JUST SEEMS TO LIKE KILLING.

1625
00:58:15,067 --> 00:58:17,167
THERE'S MORE TO IT
THAN THAT, JOE.

1626
00:58:17,233 --> 00:58:19,067
THERE'S SOMETHING
BEHIND THIS.

1627
00:58:19,133 --> 00:58:20,500
SOMETHING
WE DON'T UNDERSTAND.

1628
00:58:20,567 --> 00:58:21,533
LIKE THE NEW MATH.

1629
00:58:21,600 --> 00:58:23,400
THE WEAPON HE USES,
IT'S UNHEARD OF.

1630
00:58:23,467 --> 00:58:25,667
BLASTING FLESH
RIGHT OFF THE BONES.

1631
00:58:25,733 --> 00:58:26,767
REALLY A WASTE.

1632
00:58:26,833 --> 00:58:29,000
LOOK AT THAT TREE
OVER THERE.

1633
00:58:29,067 --> 00:58:30,067
USED IT FOR TARGET PRACTICE,
BY THE LOOKS OF IT.

1634
00:58:30,133 --> 00:58:31,400
AH, THAT'S PRETTY
FAR-FETCHED, BOB.

1635
00:58:31,467 --> 00:58:34,033
I DON'T KNOW.
LET'S TAKE A LOOK
IN THE OLD CAVE.

1636
00:58:34,100 --> 00:58:36,867
♪♪

1637
00:58:36,933 --> 00:58:38,867
♪ ROW, ROW, ROW ♪
COME ON, SING!

1638
00:58:38,933 --> 00:58:39,867
♪ ROW, ROW,
ROW YOUR BOAT ♪

1639
00:58:39,933 --> 00:58:42,333
WHERE ARE WE GOING?

1640
00:58:42,400 --> 00:58:44,067
YOU'VE GOT TO TELL ME.

1641
00:58:44,133 --> 00:58:45,367
SO I KNOW
WHERE TO TURN.

1642
00:58:45,433 --> 00:58:48,033
IT IS NOT FAR NOW.

1643
00:58:48,100 --> 00:58:50,133
YOU CAN'T ESCAPE.

1644
00:58:50,200 --> 00:58:51,733
THE POLICE WILL FIND YOU.

1645
00:58:51,800 --> 00:58:53,267
POSSIBLY THEY WILL,

1646
00:58:53,333 --> 00:58:55,633
BUT BARRICADED
IN THE MOUTH OF A CAVE

1647
00:58:55,700 --> 00:58:57,367
WITH YOU AS HOSTAGE
AND ME WITH THIS--

1648
00:58:57,433 --> 00:58:59,600
HOW LONG DO YOU THINK YOU CAN
HOLD OUT THAT WAY?

1649
00:58:59,667 --> 00:59:01,567
LONG ENOUGH.

1650
00:59:01,633 --> 00:59:05,000
THERE WILL NOT BE
TOO LONG TO WAIT.

1651
00:59:05,067 --> 00:59:08,233
SUSPICION, NORTH BY--
AH, YOU KNOW.

1652
00:59:08,300 --> 00:59:10,433
WHY DO YOU SEEK THE LIVING
AMONG THE DEAD?

1653
00:59:10,500 --> 00:59:13,033
HEY, BRING YOUR
FLASHBULBS UP HERE.

1654
00:59:13,100 --> 00:59:14,900
THIS TUNNEL
IS BLACK AS PITCH.

1655
00:59:14,967 --> 00:59:16,333
OKAY, I'LL BE RIGHT UP.

1656
00:59:16,400 --> 00:59:18,300
AND IT'S FILLED
WITH CHILI.

1657
00:59:18,367 --> 00:59:20,800
IT'S A TUNNEL OF CHILI,
LIKE A HORMEL HOT DOG.
GET IT?

1658
00:59:20,867 --> 00:59:24,067
[MAC SCREAMING,
GARGON WAILING]

1659
00:59:24,133 --> 00:59:25,067
[BONES CRUNCHING]

1660
00:59:25,133 --> 00:59:26,833
SHOULD I BRING
MORE FLASHBULBS?

1661
00:59:26,900 --> 00:59:27,833
MAC!

1662
00:59:27,900 --> 00:59:29,433
♪♪

1663
00:59:29,500 --> 00:59:30,667
UH-OH.

1664
00:59:30,733 --> 00:59:32,200
AN INTRUDER ALREADY!

1665
00:59:32,267 --> 00:59:36,433
NO!

1666
00:59:36,500 --> 00:59:38,333
I WON'T LET YOU
KILL ANYONE.

1667
00:59:38,400 --> 00:59:39,767
YOU'LL KILL SOMEONE
OVER MY DEAD BODY!

1668
00:59:39,833 --> 00:59:41,567
I SEE YOU DO NOT
VALUE YOUR LIFE!

1669
00:59:41,633 --> 00:59:43,367
MUCH!

1670
00:59:43,433 --> 00:59:44,433
HE'S GETTING AWAY!
FOLLOW HIM!

1671
00:59:44,500 --> 00:59:45,433
NO!

1672
00:59:45,500 --> 00:59:47,600
YOU DARE REFUSE?

1673
00:59:47,667 --> 00:59:50,333
HEY, HEY, THAT'S WHERE
I DRAW THE LINE!

1674
00:59:50,400 --> 00:59:51,667
PISTOL WHIPPING.

1675
00:59:51,733 --> 00:59:56,100
♪♪

1676
00:59:56,167 --> 00:59:58,500
DAMN, THE TREE.
I HATE THAT!

1677
00:59:58,567 --> 01:00:00,200
♪♪

1678
01:00:00,267 --> 01:00:01,933
AFTER HIM, SCOOB!

1679
01:00:02,000 --> 01:00:04,433
THAT REPORTER'S RUNNING
AWAY FROM THE STORY.

1680
01:00:04,500 --> 01:00:05,867
♪♪

1681
01:00:05,933 --> 01:00:09,633
KIND OF LIKE THE YEAR OF
LIVING SENSIBLY, YOU KNOW?

1682
01:00:09,700 --> 01:00:10,967
♪♪

1683
01:00:11,033 --> 01:00:13,233
YOU DON'T SEE THIS SHOT IN
MOVIES VERY OFTEN, DO YOU?

1684
01:00:13,300 --> 01:00:14,967
NO, UH-- MM-HMM.

1685
01:00:15,033 --> 01:00:17,333
NO, THIS IS
JUST LIKE MISERY.

1686
01:00:17,400 --> 01:00:18,967
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?
THIS IS MISERY.

1687
01:00:19,033 --> 01:00:20,700
I'LL SAY.

1688
01:00:20,767 --> 01:00:24,833
SAN DIEGO FREEWAY,
THE EARLY YEARS.

1689
01:00:24,900 --> 01:00:27,567
MENOPAUSE CAN FEEL LIKE
A SPEEDING CAR CHASE.

1690
01:00:27,633 --> 01:00:29,333
[MOANING]

1691
01:00:29,400 --> 01:00:34,600
I'VE GOT A HEADACHE THIS BIG,
AND IT'S GOT THIS MOVIE
WRITTEN ALL OVER IT.

1692
01:00:34,667 --> 01:00:37,900
WHOA, HE SHOULDN'T BE DRIVING
WITHOUT CORRECTIVE LENSES.

1693
01:00:37,967 --> 01:00:39,700
AAH!

1694
01:00:39,767 --> 01:00:40,833
OH!

1695
01:00:40,900 --> 01:00:45,233
IT'S MAE "THE SUPER NURSE"
OSBORNE.

1696
01:00:45,300 --> 01:00:46,267
OOH.

1697
01:00:46,333 --> 01:00:47,833
♪♪

1698
01:00:47,900 --> 01:00:50,167
♪ DOO DOO DOO DOO
DOO DOO ♪

1699
01:00:50,233 --> 01:00:51,767
♪ DOO DOO
DOO DOO DOO DOO ♪

1700
01:00:51,833 --> 01:00:54,467
AH, WHAT DO YOU KNOW?
"VALLEY" PARKING.

1701
01:00:54,533 --> 01:00:56,500
♪♪

1702
01:00:56,567 --> 01:00:59,300
HOW'D I DO THAT?

1703
01:00:59,367 --> 01:01:00,633
OOPH!

1704
01:01:00,700 --> 01:01:03,833
THOSE EASY SPIRIT PUMPS
SAVED HER HASH.

1705
01:01:03,900 --> 01:01:05,233
♪♪

1706
01:01:05,300 --> 01:01:08,633
WELL, SHE'S FINE, BUT THESE
STAINS WILL NEVER COME OUT.

1707
01:01:08,700 --> 01:01:10,133
ARE YOU HURT BADLY?

1708
01:01:10,200 --> 01:01:12,467
WELL, I--
I DON'T THINK SO.

1709
01:01:12,533 --> 01:01:13,667
WELL, THEN,
DOWN HILL WITH YOU!

1710
01:01:13,733 --> 01:01:17,467
JUST BRUISED.
OH, THANK HEAVENS IT'S OVER.

1711
01:01:17,533 --> 01:01:19,267
IT WAS LIKE A NIGHTMARE.

1712
01:01:19,333 --> 01:01:20,633
ONLY I WASN'T ABOARD
THAT PIRATE SHIP WITH MY--

1713
01:01:20,700 --> 01:01:21,900
I-- I WISH IT WAS OVER.

1714
01:01:21,967 --> 01:01:23,167
WELL, WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

1715
01:01:23,233 --> 01:01:25,533
BACK IN THE CAVE,
WHERE HE SHOT AT ME.

1716
01:01:25,600 --> 01:01:27,500
SOME KIND OF
MAN-EATING MONSTER.

1717
01:01:27,567 --> 01:01:29,567
POOR MAC,
THE GUY I WAS WITH.

1718
01:01:29,633 --> 01:01:31,467
I COULD HEAR THE THING
TEARING HIM APART.

1719
01:01:31,533 --> 01:01:32,700
IT SOUNDED DELICIOUS.

1720
01:01:32,767 --> 01:01:33,767
HE WAS DEAD
IN A FEW SECONDS.

1721
01:01:33,833 --> 01:01:35,133
OH, HOW HORRIBLE.

1722
01:01:35,200 --> 01:01:36,767
WHAT COULD IT HAVE BEEN?

1723
01:01:36,833 --> 01:01:38,567
I DON'T KNOW.

1724
01:01:38,633 --> 01:01:39,700
BUT WHATEVER IT IS,

1725
01:01:39,767 --> 01:01:41,267
I'M AFRAID THE NIGHTMARE
HAS JUST BEGUN.

1726
01:01:41,333 --> 01:01:42,267
♪ DA DAH DAH DUNNN ♪

1727
01:01:42,333 --> 01:01:45,267
♪♪

1728
01:01:48,767 --> 01:01:49,833
THOR CRASHED
JUST BELOW HERE.

1729
01:01:49,900 --> 01:01:51,800
IF THAT DISINTEGRATOR
IS DOWN THERE,

1730
01:01:51,867 --> 01:01:53,433
I'M GOING TO FIND IT.

1731
01:01:53,500 --> 01:01:54,633
DEREK, I JUST THOUGHT...

1732
01:01:54,700 --> 01:01:55,767
WELL, STOP THAT.

1733
01:01:55,833 --> 01:01:58,667
THE MONSTER THAT ESCAPED
FROM THE CAVE,

1734
01:01:58,733 --> 01:02:01,000
IT MUST HAVE BEEN THERE
AT THE SAME TIME WE WERE.

1735
01:02:01,067 --> 01:02:04,900
WHAT I CAN'T FIGURE OUT IS WHY
DID IT ESCAPE WHEN IT DID?

1736
01:02:04,967 --> 01:02:06,167
WHY NOT SOONER?

1737
01:02:06,233 --> 01:02:07,300
WHY DO I LOVE IT
LIKE I DO?

1738
01:02:07,367 --> 01:02:08,633
IT WOULD NOT HAVE BEEN
LARGE ENOUGH.

1739
01:02:08,700 --> 01:02:12,600
BUT THE MAN IT CONSUMED
INCREASED ITS GROWTH RATE.

1740
01:02:12,667 --> 01:02:14,400
STUPID OLD MAN.

1741
01:02:14,467 --> 01:02:17,333
THEN HOW BIG
WOULD IT BE NOW?

1742
01:02:17,400 --> 01:02:18,900
THERE IS NO TELLING.

1743
01:02:18,967 --> 01:02:20,333
HAVE YOU SEEN
LISTOMANIA?

1744
01:02:20,400 --> 01:02:22,800
YOU STAY HERE,
KEEP THE DOOR CLOSED.

1745
01:02:22,867 --> 01:02:26,733
OH, AND IF A STRANGE LOOKING
LOBSTER COMES KNOCKING,
IGNORE IT.

1746
01:02:26,800 --> 01:02:29,867
♪♪

1747
01:02:29,933 --> 01:02:31,167
[HUMMING]

1748
01:02:31,233 --> 01:02:32,433
♪♪

1749
01:02:32,500 --> 01:02:34,600
WELL,
THERE'S THE ROCKFORD CAR,

1750
01:02:34,667 --> 01:02:37,800
THERE'S THE STARSKY
AND HUTCH CAR, AND--OH.

1751
01:02:37,867 --> 01:02:39,067
♪♪

1752
01:02:39,133 --> 01:02:41,800
CLOTHES BY
CHARLIE MCCARTHY.

1753
01:02:41,867 --> 01:02:42,833
♪♪

1754
01:02:42,900 --> 01:02:45,667
YEP, NO.
NO EASTER EGGS HERE.

1755
01:02:45,733 --> 01:02:48,067
THE HILLS HAVE CRABS.

1756
01:02:48,133 --> 01:02:49,967
♪♪

1757
01:02:50,033 --> 01:02:52,267
WAIT.

1758
01:02:52,333 --> 01:02:55,433
I'M GETTING HOT.
WHY DIDN'T HE CRACK A WINDOW?

1759
01:02:55,500 --> 01:02:56,667
♪♪

1760
01:02:56,733 --> 01:02:58,367
DEREK?

1761
01:02:58,433 --> 01:02:59,700
DEREK,
CAN I HAVE THE KEYS

1762
01:02:59,767 --> 01:03:02,000
SO I CAN LISTEN
TO THE RADIO AT LEAST?

1763
01:03:02,067 --> 01:03:05,333
♪♪

1764
01:03:05,400 --> 01:03:09,433
AH, QUEEN ANNE'S LACE,
MORNING GLORIES, BUTTERCUPS.

1765
01:03:09,500 --> 01:03:10,467
HMM.

1766
01:03:10,533 --> 01:03:11,500
♪♪

1767
01:03:11,567 --> 01:03:13,800
IT'S ANDREW WYETH'S VALLEY.

1768
01:03:13,867 --> 01:03:18,067
♪♪

1769
01:03:18,133 --> 01:03:20,400
NO, BETTY, GO BACK, IT'S TOO
DANGEROUS FOR YOU--

1770
01:03:20,467 --> 01:03:23,200
WE CAN FIND THAT THING
TWICE AS FAST IF WE BOTH LOOK.

1771
01:03:23,267 --> 01:03:25,400
OH!
OH!

1772
01:03:25,467 --> 01:03:27,467
WELL, AS LONG
AS WE'RE DOWN HERE...

1773
01:03:27,533 --> 01:03:31,067
YOU MAKE ME ANGRY,

1774
01:03:31,133 --> 01:03:35,767
BUT I LIKE YOU VERY MUCH.

1775
01:03:35,833 --> 01:03:39,200
IN A MOMENT, THE MOON WILL COME
FROM BEHIND A CLOUD.

1776
01:03:39,267 --> 01:03:40,767
WHAT IS THIS, A BERGMAN FILM
ALL OF A SUDDEN?

1777
01:03:40,833 --> 01:03:43,067
IT'LL BE EASIER TO SEE WHAT
WE'RE LOOKING FOR.

1778
01:03:43,133 --> 01:03:44,900
YES.

1779
01:03:44,967 --> 01:03:47,233
THE LIGHT FROM YOUR MOON,
IT WILL HELP.

1780
01:03:47,300 --> 01:03:49,367
MY MOON?

1781
01:03:49,433 --> 01:03:51,667
[MAKING UP WORDS
THAT SOUND SWEDISH]

1782
01:03:51,733 --> 01:03:53,667
WHERE ARE YOU FROM, DEREK?

1783
01:03:53,733 --> 01:03:56,200
A PLACE CALLED STUDSVILLE.

1784
01:03:56,267 --> 01:03:57,200
POPULATION: ME.

1785
01:03:57,267 --> 01:03:59,933
I THINK I KNOW.

1786
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:03,100
I THINK I'VE KNOWN
FOR SOME TIME.

1787
01:04:03,167 --> 01:04:05,767
YOU ARE ONE WEIRD
MAMMA JAMMA.

1788
01:04:05,833 --> 01:04:09,300
YOU'RE NOT FROM
THIS WORLD, ARE YOU?

1789
01:04:09,367 --> 01:04:10,967
YOU'RE FROM THE VALLEY,
AREN'T YOU?

1790
01:04:11,033 --> 01:04:13,000
I DID NOT KNOW
HOW TO TELL YOU.

1791
01:04:13,067 --> 01:04:14,667
I'M FROM JERSEY.

1792
01:04:14,733 --> 01:04:18,233
IT SEEMS IMPOSSIBLE
TO BELIEVE.

1793
01:04:18,300 --> 01:04:19,833
BELIEVE IT OR NOT.

1794
01:04:19,900 --> 01:04:22,167
YOU'RE SO MUCH LIKE US.

1795
01:04:22,233 --> 01:04:23,567
WAIT UNTIL
YOU SEE MY TONGUES.

1796
01:04:23,633 --> 01:04:26,367
LIKE MY BROTHER, OR GRANDPA,
WHEN HE WAS YOUNG.

1797
01:04:26,433 --> 01:04:27,733
AND HAD A LIVER.

1798
01:04:27,800 --> 01:04:30,800
AND TO THINK...

1799
01:04:30,867 --> 01:04:32,233
WE WERE MADE THE SAME.

1800
01:04:32,300 --> 01:04:33,833
HOW INCONVENIENT.

1801
01:04:33,900 --> 01:04:38,800
THE ONLY DIFFERENCE IS
THAT WE WERE PUT ON PLACES
FAR, FAR APART.

1802
01:04:38,867 --> 01:04:40,800
OH, NOW HE'S GONNA
SING EBONY AND IVORY.

1803
01:04:40,867 --> 01:04:44,600
WHAT IS IT LIKE...
WHERE YOU'RE FROM?

1804
01:04:44,667 --> 01:04:48,200
BABIES ARE BRED
AND RAISED LIKE LIVESTOCK,

1805
01:04:48,267 --> 01:04:51,567
PARENTED BY THE MOST PERFECT
SPECIMENS OF OUR RACE.

1806
01:04:51,633 --> 01:04:53,000
HMM, SOUNDS NICE.

1807
01:04:53,067 --> 01:04:55,300
IF YOU BECOME ILL,
YOU ARE PUT TO DEATH...

1808
01:04:55,367 --> 01:04:57,167
HMM, MASSACHUSETTS,
RHODE ISLAND.

1809
01:04:57,233 --> 01:04:58,467
AS ARE THE OLD.

1810
01:04:58,533 --> 01:05:00,367
SO THEY'RE STRICT?
IS THAT WHAT YOU'RE SAYING?

1811
01:05:00,433 --> 01:05:05,667
YOU WON'T BE GOING BACK EVER,
WILL YOU?

1812
01:05:05,733 --> 01:05:09,533
I SHALL MAKE
THE EARTH MY HOME,

1813
01:05:09,600 --> 01:05:14,667
AND I SHALL NEVER,
NEVER LEAVE IT.

1814
01:05:14,733 --> 01:05:18,200
AND HE'LL REALIZE THAT THERE
ARE CUTER GIRLS AT SCHOOL.

1815
01:05:18,267 --> 01:05:19,433
♪♪

1816
01:05:19,500 --> 01:05:23,233
HMM, EVER TASTE
GARGON FLESH?

1817
01:05:23,300 --> 01:05:26,133
EVER TASTE
DR. PEPPER LIP-SMACKER?

1818
01:05:26,200 --> 01:05:27,167
♪♪

1819
01:05:27,233 --> 01:05:30,333
LOVE IS COOLING
IN THE SAGEBRUSH.

1820
01:05:30,400 --> 01:05:32,967
WOCKA-WOW!

1821
01:05:33,033 --> 01:05:35,933
OOH.

1822
01:05:36,000 --> 01:05:38,200
YOU THOUGHT THAT NURSE
HAD GRASS STAINS. OOPH!

1823
01:05:38,267 --> 01:05:40,033
THE MOON HAS COME
FROM BEHIND THE CLOUD.

1824
01:05:40,100 --> 01:05:41,267
DONE.

1825
01:05:41,333 --> 01:05:42,300
♪♪

1826
01:05:42,367 --> 01:05:43,333
HMM.

1827
01:05:43,400 --> 01:05:44,433
COLD.

1828
01:05:44,500 --> 01:05:46,033
GETTING WARMER.

1829
01:05:46,100 --> 01:05:48,300
DEREK.

1830
01:05:48,367 --> 01:05:49,467
THE CRICKETS...

1831
01:05:49,533 --> 01:05:51,500
WE'LL NAME THE BAND
"THE CRICKETS."

1832
01:05:51,567 --> 01:05:53,067
IT'S SO QUIET.

1833
01:05:53,133 --> 01:05:54,067
TOO QUIET.

1834
01:05:54,133 --> 01:05:55,067
[SCREAMS]

1835
01:05:55,133 --> 01:05:56,067
OH, MY GOD,
IT'S MY MOM!

1836
01:05:56,133 --> 01:05:57,867
THE GARGON-- GET BACK!

1837
01:05:57,933 --> 01:05:58,867
THERE IT IS, DEREK!

1838
01:05:58,933 --> 01:06:00,667
IT WAS
UNDER THE ROCK-- QUICK!

1839
01:06:00,733 --> 01:06:01,733
[GARGON WAILING]

1840
01:06:01,800 --> 01:06:02,733
UH, SHRIMP IN THE GAME.

1841
01:06:02,800 --> 01:06:04,000
SHOOT IT, DEREK, SHOOT IT!

1842
01:06:04,067 --> 01:06:05,933
IT WON'T WORK-- RUN!
GO START THE MOTOR, HURRY!

1843
01:06:06,000 --> 01:06:07,033
HURRY!

1844
01:06:07,100 --> 01:06:08,433
[GARGON WAILING]

1845
01:06:08,500 --> 01:06:10,467
FOR THE SEAFOOD KILLER
IN YOU.

1846
01:06:10,533 --> 01:06:11,500
TONIGHT...

1847
01:06:11,567 --> 01:06:13,633
IT'S A ROCKED LOBSTER!

1848
01:06:13,700 --> 01:06:16,600
WHOA, WHOA, TURN DOWN
THE FIREBIRD, SWEETS.

1849
01:06:16,667 --> 01:06:17,867
♪♪

1850
01:06:17,933 --> 01:06:19,867
BYE, DEREK!

1851
01:06:19,933 --> 01:06:25,700
♪♪

1852
01:06:25,767 --> 01:06:27,533
[ENGINE STARTS]

1853
01:06:27,600 --> 01:06:30,500
OOPS, WRONG WAY.
THERE YOU GO.

1854
01:06:30,567 --> 01:06:32,300
SEE YOU, KIDS.

1855
01:06:32,367 --> 01:06:34,533
THAT'S THE MOST TERRIFYING
THING I'VE EVER SEEN.

1856
01:06:34,600 --> 01:06:35,533
AND THE LOBSTER
WAS BAD TOO.

1857
01:06:35,600 --> 01:06:37,233
WHY WOULDN'T THE GUN WORK?

1858
01:06:37,300 --> 01:06:40,733
MUST HAVE BEEN DAMAGED
SOMEHOW WHEN THOR WAS
"FLOWN" IN THE CRASH.

1859
01:06:40,800 --> 01:06:42,100
"FLOWN" IN THE CRASH?

1860
01:06:42,167 --> 01:06:43,933
YOU SAID THAT--THAT THING
WOULD KEEP GROWING.

1861
01:06:44,000 --> 01:06:45,333
AND THE LOBSTER TOO!

1862
01:06:45,400 --> 01:06:47,900
IF IT DOES, WHAT CAN STOP IT
FROM WRECKING THE CITY AND--

1863
01:06:47,967 --> 01:06:50,900
I MAY BE ABLE TO REPAIR
THE DAMAGED PART OF THE
DISINTEGRATOR.

1864
01:06:50,967 --> 01:06:53,133
IF I CAN,
WE WILL STOP THE GARGON

1865
01:06:53,200 --> 01:06:56,300
AND GIVE THE EARTH A WEAPON
AGAINST INVASION AS WELL.

1866
01:06:56,367 --> 01:06:59,000
IF ONLY
I CAN GET IT TO WORK.

1867
01:06:59,067 --> 01:07:00,367
WILL DEREK
GET IT TO WORK?

1868
01:07:00,433 --> 01:07:01,767
TUNE IN NEXT TIME!

1869
01:07:01,833 --> 01:07:04,633
HEY, WHAT DOES SNAPPER
LOOK LIKE, ANYWAY?

1870
01:07:04,700 --> 01:07:06,200
I'M CURT GOWDY.

1871
01:07:06,267 --> 01:07:09,533
JOIN ME AND PHIL HARRIS
AS WE GO AFTER BIG
TEXAS LOBSTER.

1872
01:07:09,600 --> 01:07:10,800
♪♪

1873
01:07:10,867 --> 01:07:12,800
SHOOT FIRST, SEEK TO
UNDERSTAND LATER, MY FRIEND.

1874
01:07:12,867 --> 01:07:13,833
[DISTANT HOWL]

1875
01:07:13,900 --> 01:07:15,200
WHAT WAS THAT?

1876
01:07:15,267 --> 01:07:17,533
ONLY A COYOTE.

1877
01:07:17,600 --> 01:07:20,033
SLAMMIN' SAM SNEAD.

1878
01:07:20,100 --> 01:07:21,033
THERE IT IS!

1879
01:07:21,100 --> 01:07:22,033
[GARGON WAILING]

1880
01:07:22,100 --> 01:07:23,033
[GUNSHOTS]

1881
01:07:23,100 --> 01:07:24,633
OH, THAT'LL HAPPEN.

1882
01:07:24,700 --> 01:07:26,533
YOU'RE BOUND TO LOSE
A FEW OF YOUR HUNTING PARTY
RIGHT AWAY.

1883
01:07:26,600 --> 01:07:28,000
[GARGON WAILING]

1884
01:07:28,067 --> 01:07:30,700
OH, NO!
HE READS TOO! AAH!

1885
01:07:30,767 --> 01:07:32,300
♪♪

1886
01:07:32,367 --> 01:07:33,833
GRANDPA WAS SO EXHAUSTED,

1887
01:07:33,900 --> 01:07:36,067
HE FELL SOUND ASLEEP
WITH ALL HIS CLOTHES ON.

1888
01:07:36,133 --> 01:07:37,200
AND THEN HE SOILED
HIMSELF.

1889
01:07:37,267 --> 01:07:38,933
DO YOU THINK
YOU CAN FIX IT, DEREK?

1890
01:07:39,000 --> 01:07:40,667
I HAVE FOUND
THE DAMAGED PART.

1891
01:07:40,733 --> 01:07:42,867
IT'S GONNA COST YOU.

1892
01:07:42,933 --> 01:07:44,767
SUCH A LITTLE THING.

1893
01:07:44,833 --> 01:07:46,100
IT'S A COPPER 7.

1894
01:07:46,167 --> 01:07:49,000
AND YET IT HAS THE POWER TO
DESTROY US, IT DOES.

1895
01:07:49,067 --> 01:07:50,700
IT IS WORTHLESS...

1896
01:07:50,767 --> 01:07:51,900
OH, IT IS A COPPER 7.

1897
01:07:51,967 --> 01:07:54,667
UNLESS I CAN FIGURE OUT
AN ENERGY SUBSTITUTE.

1898
01:07:54,733 --> 01:07:57,167
MAYBE IT WON'T
COME INTO THE CITY, DEREK.

1899
01:07:57,233 --> 01:07:59,367
IT WILL COME TO THE CITY...

1900
01:07:59,433 --> 01:08:00,633
YEAH, IT NEEDS
TO CASH A CHECK.

1901
01:08:00,700 --> 01:08:03,067
FOR MORE FOOD,
IF NOTHING ELSE.

1902
01:08:03,133 --> 01:08:05,300
WELL, THEN I SHOULD
SET OUT SOME SNACKS.

1903
01:08:05,367 --> 01:08:08,067
MEANWHILE, AT THE OUTHOUSE
ON THE HILL...

1904
01:08:08,133 --> 01:08:11,000
IT'S MEL BROOKS
IN LIFE STINKS...

1905
01:08:11,067 --> 01:08:12,533
♪♪

1906
01:08:12,600 --> 01:08:14,800
KNOW WHEN TO SAY WHEN--
THAT'S MY MOTTO.

1907
01:08:14,867 --> 01:08:17,267
HMM?

1908
01:08:17,333 --> 01:08:18,833
THIS IS JOHNSON
AT STATION 86.

1909
01:08:18,900 --> 01:08:20,500
OUT BY THE HILLS,
DUE NORTHEAST,

1910
01:08:20,567 --> 01:08:21,800
THERE'S SOME KIND
OF A MONSTER!

1911
01:08:21,867 --> 01:08:23,767
IT SUDDENLY POPPED UP
AND SEEMED TO TOUCH THE SKY!

1912
01:08:23,833 --> 01:08:24,767
EHH!

1913
01:08:24,833 --> 01:08:25,800
I HAVE NOT BEEN DRINKING!

1914
01:08:25,867 --> 01:08:26,900
HICCUPPING

1915
01:08:26,967 --> 01:08:28,167
NO, I CAN'T SEE IT NOW.

1916
01:08:28,233 --> 01:08:29,433
IT MUST BE BEHIND THE HILLS.

1917
01:08:29,500 --> 01:08:30,733
BUT I'M GETTING OUT OF HERE!

1918
01:08:30,800 --> 01:08:31,933
GAH-AGG.

1919
01:08:32,000 --> 01:08:33,000
♪♪

1920
01:08:33,067 --> 01:08:34,833
COME ON, OLD FRIEND.

1921
01:08:34,900 --> 01:08:37,533
THE FEW REMAINING SURVIVORS
OF THE SEARCH PARTY THAT
WAS ATTACKED

1922
01:08:37,600 --> 01:08:39,133
REPORT THAT THE BEAST THEY
ENCOUNTERED

1923
01:08:39,200 --> 01:08:41,200
WAS MANY TIMES
THE SIZE THEY EXPECTED,

1924
01:08:41,267 --> 01:08:45,467
INDICATING THAT THE MONSTER
HAS SOME STRANGE POWER
OF RAPID GROWTH.

1925
01:08:45,533 --> 01:08:46,667
AN EXACT DESCRIPTION WAS--

1926
01:08:46,733 --> 01:08:47,767
TAKE THIS.
COME ON, TAKE IT.

1927
01:08:47,833 --> 01:08:49,000
WE HAVE A BULLETIN,
JUST RECEIVED.

1928
01:08:49,067 --> 01:08:50,167
THERE'S A PIECE OF GREEN
SOMETHING BETWEEN YOUR--

1929
01:08:50,233 --> 01:08:51,567
ACCORDING TO A REPORT
NOT YET CONFIRMED,

1930
01:08:51,633 --> 01:08:53,800
A BEAST OF SEEMINGLY
GIGANTIC PROPORTIONS

1931
01:08:53,867 --> 01:08:56,267
HAS BEEN SIGHTED LURKING
IN THE HILLS DUE
NORTHEAST OF TOWN.

1932
01:08:56,333 --> 01:08:57,700
I DON'T HAVE
ANY PANTS ON.

1933
01:08:57,767 --> 01:08:59,500
CITY OFFICIALS HAVE
CALLED FOR MILITARY HELP.

1934
01:08:59,567 --> 01:09:02,233
PLANES AND TROOPS ARE
EXPECTED TO ARRIVE
WITHIN THE NEXT TWO HOURS.

1935
01:09:02,300 --> 01:09:03,300
WE GOTTA ROLL.

1936
01:09:03,367 --> 01:09:04,400
AND ON THE LIGHTER SIDE...

1937
01:09:04,467 --> 01:09:05,633
MEANWHILE, CITIZENS
SHOULD TAKE REFUGE

1938
01:09:05,700 --> 01:09:07,967
IN PLACES OF SAFETY--
CELLARS, BOMB SHELTERS--

1939
01:09:08,033 --> 01:09:10,067
AS DIRECTED BY CIVIL DEFENSE
ADMINISTRATORS.

1940
01:09:10,133 --> 01:09:11,100
I REPEAT...

1941
01:09:11,167 --> 01:09:18,000
[MECHANICAL WHIRRING]

1942
01:09:18,067 --> 01:09:19,567
IS THIS YOUR CARD?

1943
01:09:19,633 --> 01:09:21,067
HEY, CROW, WHAT'S UP?

1944
01:09:21,133 --> 01:09:24,267
OH, JUST THINKING,
WATCHING THE SNACK FOOD
DRIFT BY.

1945
01:09:24,333 --> 01:09:25,433
AH.

1946
01:09:25,500 --> 01:09:26,933
NOTHING MUCH EVER
HAPPENS AROUND HERE.

1947
01:09:27,000 --> 01:09:28,033
BLACK.

1948
01:09:28,100 --> 01:09:29,300
IT MAKES ME REALIZE
HOW ALONE WE ARE.

1949
01:09:29,367 --> 01:09:30,333
KNOW WHAT I MEAN?

1950
01:09:30,400 --> 01:09:31,567
- BLACK.
- MM-HMM.

1951
01:09:31,633 --> 01:09:33,067
HANGING IN SPACE LIKE
A GIANT SPECK OF FOOD,

1952
01:09:33,133 --> 01:09:34,767
FLOATING IN THE OCEAN,

1953
01:09:34,833 --> 01:09:36,267
SOONER OR LATER TO BE
SWALLOWED UP

1954
01:09:36,333 --> 01:09:38,333
BY SOME CREATURE
FLOATING BY.

1955
01:09:38,400 --> 01:09:41,300
ANOTHER DAY IN PARADISE.
YEP, YEP, YEP.

1956
01:09:41,367 --> 01:09:43,667
THIS IS A LOADED DECK,
ISN'T IT? BLACK.

1957
01:09:43,733 --> 01:09:45,867
I MEAN, UH, COME ON,
WHAT IF THERE IS NO
SUPREME BEING?

1958
01:09:45,933 --> 01:09:47,400
WOULDN'T THAT BE A FINE
"HOW DO YOU DO"?

1959
01:09:47,467 --> 01:09:49,467
OH, THERE'S
A SUPREME BEING, ALL RIGHT.

1960
01:09:49,533 --> 01:09:51,000
WELL, OKAY.

1961
01:09:51,067 --> 01:09:52,100
BLACK.

1962
01:09:52,167 --> 01:09:54,133
HEY, TOM, WHAT HAVE YOU
BEEN UP TO LATELY?

1963
01:09:54,200 --> 01:09:55,800
RED.
WELL, YOU KNOW ME.

1964
01:09:55,867 --> 01:09:57,700
I TRY TO WARD OFF MY
VELD SCHWARTZ WITH MY HOBBIES.

1965
01:09:57,767 --> 01:09:59,267
- UH, RED.
- WRONG.

1966
01:09:59,333 --> 01:10:01,667
WELL, I FINALLY FINISHED OFF
THAT TRISTAR PEGASUS LOGO

1967
01:10:01,733 --> 01:10:02,867
WE'RE GONNA USE
IN OUR NEXT MOVIE PAGEANT.

1968
01:10:02,933 --> 01:10:04,133
OH, REALLY?
THAT'S GREAT.

1969
01:10:04,200 --> 01:10:06,033
YEAH, BOY, TRYING TO GET
THOSE LITTLE WINGS TO STICK.

1970
01:10:06,100 --> 01:10:08,100
WOW, I'D REALLY LIKE TO
SEE THAT SOMETIME,
YOU KNOW?

1971
01:10:08,167 --> 01:10:09,900
WELL, SURE, YOU KNOW,
I'VE GOT IT RIGHT DOWN HERE.

1972
01:10:09,967 --> 01:10:12,167
HEY, GUYS, THERE'S A SHIP
COMING INTO VIEW!

1973
01:10:12,233 --> 01:10:13,600
AW, CROW,
YOU'RE PLUMB LOCO.

1974
01:10:13,667 --> 01:10:15,500
IT'S PROBABLY JUST SOME BIG
GUMMI BEAR FROM BEFORE.

1975
01:10:15,567 --> 01:10:18,000
NO, NO, NO,
IT'S A SKULL CRUISER!

1976
01:10:18,067 --> 01:10:21,867
IT-- IT-- IT'S BLACK
AND DEMONIC, AND IT SPREADS
DARKNESS AND DEATH.

1977
01:10:21,933 --> 01:10:23,133
COOL!

1978
01:10:23,200 --> 01:10:24,900
YOU'RE SO HIGH.
RED.

1979
01:10:24,967 --> 01:10:28,200
GUMMI BEARS-- UH,
GUMMI BEARS DON'T SPREAD
DARKNESS AND DEATH.

1980
01:10:28,267 --> 01:10:29,533
UH, DO THEY?

1981
01:10:29,600 --> 01:10:31,667
AND IT'S PILOTED
BY A GHOSTLY FIGURE

1982
01:10:31,733 --> 01:10:33,600
WITH A DARK COUNTENANCE
AND DEADLY INTENT!

1983
01:10:33,667 --> 01:10:34,967
YEAH, YOU GUYS HAVE
GOTTA SEE THIS!

1984
01:10:35,033 --> 01:10:36,567
NO, I THINK
YOU'RE JUST SEEING

1985
01:10:36,633 --> 01:10:38,967
ONE OF THOSE PACKS
OF JORDAN ALMONDS
WE SHOT OUT THERE.

1986
01:10:39,033 --> 01:10:40,000
WHOA!

1987
01:10:40,067 --> 01:10:41,033
OH!

1988
01:10:41,100 --> 01:10:42,633
GET TO ROCKET NUMBER 9
QUICK!

1989
01:10:42,700 --> 01:10:45,633
[ROCK MUSIC]

1990
01:10:45,700 --> 01:10:47,400
♪♪

1991
01:10:47,467 --> 01:10:49,233
BOSS!

1992
01:10:49,300 --> 01:10:54,000
♪♪

1993
01:10:54,067 --> 01:10:56,867
HOOKER HEADERS
AND THRUSH PIPES,

1994
01:10:56,933 --> 01:10:58,733
WOOFERS AND TWEETERS
AND BEARS...

1995
01:10:58,800 --> 01:11:00,133
OH, MY!

1996
01:11:00,200 --> 01:11:04,967
♪♪

1997
01:11:05,033 --> 01:11:09,300
HEY, GUYS, CHECK OUT
THE HEX FIELD VIEW SCREEN.

1998
01:11:09,367 --> 01:11:10,733
WOW.

1999
01:11:10,800 --> 01:11:13,033
OH, COOL.

2000
01:11:13,100 --> 01:11:14,767
UHH! UHH! AAH!

2001
01:11:14,833 --> 01:11:16,533
HUH? WHAT?

2002
01:11:16,600 --> 01:11:19,633
I THINK HE'S TRYING
TO TELL US SOMETHING.

2003
01:11:19,700 --> 01:11:21,600
[BONES CLATTERING]

2004
01:11:21,667 --> 01:11:23,533
UH...

2005
01:11:23,600 --> 01:11:25,300
OH, MAN, WAS THAT LAME!

2006
01:11:25,367 --> 01:11:27,333
BOO! DO OVER!

2007
01:11:27,400 --> 01:11:30,367
IT SEEMS LIKE
KIND OF A GYP. MAN!

2008
01:11:30,433 --> 01:11:32,767
THAT WASN'T COOL.
THAT WAS THE DUMBEST
VISITOR EVER.

2009
01:11:32,833 --> 01:11:34,233
WELL, THAT JANITOR
WAS PRETTY DUMB.

2010
01:11:34,300 --> 01:11:35,700
WELL, THAT'S TRUE.

2011
01:11:35,767 --> 01:11:37,200
WELL, YOU KNOW, AND THE GUY
WITH THE THICK GLASSES,
HE WAS--

2012
01:11:37,267 --> 01:11:38,600
OH, YEAH, YEAH--

2013
01:11:38,667 --> 01:11:41,233
HEY, UH, TOM, YOU KNOW THAT
PEGASUS YOU WERE WORKING ON?

2014
01:11:41,300 --> 01:11:43,533
THIS HORSE IS A COW.

2015
01:11:43,600 --> 01:11:46,533
UH, DOES IT REALLY
MAKE A DIFFERENCE?

2016
01:11:46,600 --> 01:11:47,600
I DON'T THINK SO.

2017
01:11:47,667 --> 01:11:48,667
OH.

2018
01:11:48,733 --> 01:11:50,433
WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

2019
01:11:50,500 --> 01:11:53,433
♪♪

2020
01:11:57,333 --> 01:11:58,600
I CAN HELP, DEREK--
I'M GOING WITH YOU.

2021
01:11:58,667 --> 01:12:01,167
[YAWNING]
WHAT'S GOING ON?

2022
01:12:01,233 --> 01:12:02,500
WHAT'S ALL
THE COMMOTION ABOUT?

2023
01:12:02,567 --> 01:12:04,133
GRANDPA, DEREK AND I ARE GOING
OUT TO THE EDGE OF TOWN.

2024
01:12:04,200 --> 01:12:06,000
WAIT FOR US HERE.

2025
01:12:06,067 --> 01:12:09,500
FIRST I MUST PUT THE
DISINTEGRATOR BACK TOGETHER
AND THEN FIND PROPER TOOLS.

2026
01:12:09,567 --> 01:12:11,933
I CAN LOAD THE CAR WITH EVERY
TOOL WE HAVE IN THE GARAGE.

2027
01:12:12,000 --> 01:12:13,067
I CAN LOAD MY PANTS.

2028
01:12:13,133 --> 01:12:14,067
ALL RIGHT THEN, LET US GO.

2029
01:12:14,133 --> 01:12:16,100
GOOD.

2030
01:12:16,167 --> 01:12:20,000
THE STREETS OF SAN FRANCISCO--
A QUINN MARTIN PRODUCTION.

2031
01:12:20,067 --> 01:12:21,033
EPILOGUE.

2032
01:12:21,100 --> 01:12:23,767
♪♪

2033
01:12:23,833 --> 01:12:25,267
WHAT THE HECK?

2034
01:12:25,333 --> 01:12:28,200
BEFORE, IT WAS A LITTLE TOWN.
NOW IT'S THE HOLLYWOOD HILLS.

2035
01:12:28,267 --> 01:12:30,967
♪♪

2036
01:12:31,033 --> 01:12:32,733
I'M NOT GOING
IN THE TUNNEL.

2037
01:12:32,800 --> 01:12:35,700
♪♪

2038
01:12:35,767 --> 01:12:37,100
IT'S SUNDAY MORNING
IN HOLLYWOOD.

2039
01:12:37,167 --> 01:12:39,133
COME ON DOWN
TO BARGAIN CLOWN!

2040
01:12:39,200 --> 01:12:44,367
♪♪

2041
01:12:44,433 --> 01:12:45,733
HEY, WHERE'D SHE GO?

2042
01:12:45,800 --> 01:12:47,600
HMM?

2043
01:12:47,667 --> 01:12:49,567
♪ DOO DOO DOO DOO ♪

2044
01:12:49,633 --> 01:12:51,867
WOULD YOU LIKE TO GO
SWIMMING?

2045
01:12:51,933 --> 01:12:54,367
WHY AREN'T YOU IN THE CELLAR,
GRAMPS, WITH BETTY?

2046
01:12:54,433 --> 01:12:56,067
WHAT MAKES YOU THINK
BETTY'S IN THE CELLAR?

2047
01:12:56,133 --> 01:12:57,700
SHE'S OUT SOMEWHERE
WITH DEREK AGAIN.

2048
01:12:57,767 --> 01:12:59,533
EVERYBODY
IS SUPPOSED TO TAKE SHELTER.

2049
01:12:59,600 --> 01:13:02,033
THE MONSTER FROM THE CAVE,
IT'S APPROACHING THE TOWN!

2050
01:13:02,100 --> 01:13:04,433
HUH? THEN THAT'S WHERE
THEY MUST HAVE GONE.

2051
01:13:04,500 --> 01:13:06,033
THOSE CRAZY KIDS.

2052
01:13:06,100 --> 01:13:08,267
JOE, WE'VE GOT TO TRY
AND FIND THEM.

2053
01:13:08,333 --> 01:13:09,333
YOU MEAN THEY--

2054
01:13:09,400 --> 01:13:10,333
YES!

2055
01:13:10,400 --> 01:13:11,700
COME ON, THEN, LET'S GO!

2056
01:13:11,767 --> 01:13:14,333
COME ON, JOE,
WE GOTTA GO, ME OH MY OH.

2057
01:13:14,400 --> 01:13:16,333
♪♪

2058
01:13:16,400 --> 01:13:18,500
WHAT IS PARKING?
TEACH ME OF PARKING.

2059
01:13:18,567 --> 01:13:19,867
[GASPS]
DEREK, LOOK!

2060
01:13:19,933 --> 01:13:20,867
[GARGON WAILING]

2061
01:13:20,933 --> 01:13:22,133
WHAT, BEHIND
THE FLYING LOBSTER?

2062
01:13:22,200 --> 01:13:23,767
♪♪

2063
01:13:23,833 --> 01:13:25,467
YOU DRIVE AWAY.

2064
01:13:25,533 --> 01:13:27,367
YOU CAN'T CUT LIVE WIRES.

2065
01:13:27,433 --> 01:13:30,367
DEREK, MY DOOR.
DER--I'LL DO IT.

2066
01:13:30,433 --> 01:13:38,367
♪♪

2067
01:13:38,433 --> 01:13:42,900
OH, WHAT'S THIS--AAH!

2068
01:13:42,967 --> 01:13:45,267
OPERATOR,
THIS IS AN EMERGENCY.

2069
01:13:45,333 --> 01:13:47,900
YOU MUST CONNECT ME
WITH THE CITY ELECTRICAL
GENERATING PLANT.

2070
01:13:47,967 --> 01:13:49,067
HURRY!

2071
01:13:49,133 --> 01:13:51,667
HE THINKS HE'S
THE WICHITA LINEMAN! QUICK!

2072
01:13:51,733 --> 01:13:52,800
[PHONE RINGING]

2073
01:13:52,867 --> 01:13:53,833
GENERATING PLANT.

2074
01:13:53,900 --> 01:13:54,833
SIMPSON HERE.

2075
01:13:54,900 --> 01:13:56,467
HELLO?
PLEASE LISTEN TO ME.

2076
01:13:56,533 --> 01:13:58,133
YOU MUST DO AS I SAY.

2077
01:13:58,200 --> 01:14:00,333
THE MONSTER IS COMING TOWARDS
THE TOWN.

2078
01:14:00,400 --> 01:14:01,667
IF YOU'D LIKE TO SPEAK
TO AN OPERATOR, PRESS ONE.

2079
01:14:01,733 --> 01:14:02,900
I'M AT NORTH RIDGE ROAD.

2080
01:14:02,967 --> 01:14:04,800
WE HAVE A WEAPON HERE THAT MIGHT
BE ABLE TO STOP IT

2081
01:14:04,867 --> 01:14:06,967
IF WE CAN CONNECT IT TO THE
POWER LINES.

2082
01:14:07,033 --> 01:14:08,033
WHO IS THIS?
I'LL HAVE TO CHECK WITH--

2083
01:14:08,100 --> 01:14:09,033
WAIT, IS THIS BOB?

2084
01:14:09,100 --> 01:14:10,200
YOU HAVE TO BELIEVE ME.

2085
01:14:10,267 --> 01:14:12,067
THERE'S NO TIME
TO CHECK WITH ANYBODY!

2086
01:14:12,133 --> 01:14:13,200
♪♪

2087
01:14:13,267 --> 01:14:15,233
WHOA, TIME FOR MY BREAK.

2088
01:14:15,300 --> 01:14:22,267
♪♪

2089
01:14:22,333 --> 01:14:24,000
OUT THERE--
THAT LOOKS LIKE THEM.

2090
01:14:24,067 --> 01:14:25,700
DEREK IS
CLIMBING DOWN A POLE.

2091
01:14:25,767 --> 01:14:27,167
AND LOOK WHAT'S COMING.

2092
01:14:27,233 --> 01:14:29,000
WE'RE NOT GOING TO
MAKE IT DOWN IN TIME.

2093
01:14:29,067 --> 01:14:30,067
OH!

2094
01:14:30,133 --> 01:14:31,333
♪♪

2095
01:14:31,400 --> 01:14:33,067
[GARGON WAILING]

2096
01:14:33,133 --> 01:14:35,033
YOU HAVE GOT TO BE
KIDDING ME.

2097
01:14:35,100 --> 01:14:37,667
♪♪

2098
01:14:37,733 --> 01:14:39,200
RESTORE THE POWER--
IT IS READY!

2099
01:14:39,267 --> 01:14:41,467
HELLO?
TURN THE POWER BACK ON.

2100
01:14:41,533 --> 01:14:42,500
OKAY!

2101
01:14:42,567 --> 01:14:43,667
GEEZ, CAN I GET YOU
ANYTHING ELSE?

2102
01:14:43,733 --> 01:14:45,267
HOW ARE YOU FIXED FOR
SOCKS AND UNDERWEAR?

2103
01:14:45,333 --> 01:14:47,300
♪♪

2104
01:14:47,367 --> 01:14:50,167
IT IS NOT ENOUGH.
IT IS NOT ENOUGH POWER!

2105
01:14:50,233 --> 01:14:53,433
CAN YOU BOOST THE POWER ANY?
PLEASE, IT'S NOT ENOUGH!

2106
01:14:53,500 --> 01:14:54,767
I'LL TRY TO SPEED UP
THE GENERATORS.

2107
01:14:54,833 --> 01:14:56,167
I'M DOING EVERYTHING I CAN,
CAPTAIN!

2108
01:14:56,233 --> 01:14:57,633
DEREK SEEMS TO HAVE
SOME KIND OF WEAPON,

2109
01:14:57,700 --> 01:14:59,267
BUT IT'S NOT DOING ANYTHING!

2110
01:14:59,333 --> 01:15:00,900
[GARGON WAILING]

2111
01:15:00,967 --> 01:15:01,900
[IMITATING GARGON'S WAIL]

2112
01:15:01,967 --> 01:15:02,900
[LAUGHTER]

2113
01:15:02,967 --> 01:15:04,533
[ELECTRICITY SIZZLING]

2114
01:15:04,600 --> 01:15:06,467
OOPS.

2115
01:15:06,533 --> 01:15:07,533
VAPOR ACTION.

2116
01:15:07,600 --> 01:15:09,500
IF ONLY THERE WERE
MORE POWER, BETTY.

2117
01:15:09,567 --> 01:15:11,733
IS THERE ANY WAY
TO GENERATE MORE POWER?

2118
01:15:11,800 --> 01:15:13,367
WE'VE GOT TO HAVE MORE!

2119
01:15:13,433 --> 01:15:15,133
I COULD JOIN IN MORE CIRCUITS,
BUT IT MAY BLOW OUT THE LINE.

2120
01:15:15,200 --> 01:15:16,200
WAIT--HE SOUNDS
LIKE DEREK.

2121
01:15:16,267 --> 01:15:18,600
TRY ANYTHING!
IT'S OUR ONLY CHANCE!

2122
01:15:18,667 --> 01:15:20,967
WELL, I COULD PULL THIS
OTHER POWER HANDLE.

2123
01:15:21,033 --> 01:15:22,067
OH, YEAH.

2124
01:15:22,133 --> 01:15:23,433
THAT OUGHT TO DO IT.

2125
01:15:23,500 --> 01:15:24,533
OH!

2126
01:15:24,600 --> 01:15:26,167
[GARGON WAILING]

2127
01:15:26,233 --> 01:15:27,167
[DRONING]

2128
01:15:27,233 --> 01:15:28,167
THERE WE GO.

2129
01:15:28,233 --> 01:15:31,400
♪♪

2130
01:15:31,467 --> 01:15:32,867
ROSEBUD.

2131
01:15:32,933 --> 01:15:36,200
♪♪

2132
01:15:36,267 --> 01:15:38,500
GOOD NIGHT,
SWEET CRUSTACEAN.

2133
01:15:38,567 --> 01:15:39,733
♪♪

2134
01:15:39,800 --> 01:15:42,667
GEE, YOUR HAIR
SMELLS TERRIFIC.

2135
01:15:42,733 --> 01:15:43,933
♪♪

2136
01:15:44,000 --> 01:15:46,167
YOU CAN TURN THE WEAPON OVER TO
THE SCIENTISTS NOW.

2137
01:15:46,233 --> 01:15:47,233
[HIGH PITCHED TONE]

2138
01:15:47,300 --> 01:15:48,633
HERE'S SOMEONE
WHO CAN HELP YOU.

2139
01:15:48,700 --> 01:15:49,900
[DEREK]
IT IS TOO LATE.

2140
01:15:49,967 --> 01:15:51,033
YOU MEAN THEY'RE COMING?

2141
01:15:51,100 --> 01:15:52,133
TO TAKE ME AWAY?

2142
01:15:52,200 --> 01:15:54,100
ALREADY?

2143
01:15:54,167 --> 01:15:55,900
YOUR PEOPLE ARE HERE FOR YOU.

2144
01:15:55,967 --> 01:15:57,100
I MUST LEAVE.

2145
01:15:57,167 --> 01:15:58,300
MY PEOPLE
WILL CALL YOUR PEOPLE.

2146
01:15:58,367 --> 01:15:59,367
THEY WILL TAKE CARE OF YOU.

2147
01:15:59,433 --> 01:16:01,600
BUT, DEREK, YOU PROMISED.
YOU SAID--

2148
01:16:01,667 --> 01:16:02,933
I KNOW WHAT I MUST DO.

2149
01:16:03,000 --> 01:16:04,100
I HAVE TO TAKE A MEETING.

2150
01:16:04,167 --> 01:16:07,100
YOU MUST NOT INTERFERE.

2151
01:16:07,167 --> 01:16:09,267
BYE.

2152
01:16:09,333 --> 01:16:11,500
♪♪

2153
01:16:11,567 --> 01:16:14,267
BETTY, THANK HEAVENS
YOU'RE ALL RIGHT.

2154
01:16:14,333 --> 01:16:18,667
AND THANK GOODNESS FOR
THE NEW, GENEROUS CUT
OF MY DEPENDS.

2155
01:16:18,733 --> 01:16:20,833
[MUFFLED SHOUTING]

2156
01:16:20,900 --> 01:16:24,167
[CAPTAIN]
THAT BOOK HAS INDEED
MADE YOU FORGET MANY THINGS.

2157
01:16:24,233 --> 01:16:26,367
WE ARE THE SUPREME RACE.

2158
01:16:26,433 --> 01:16:27,600
WE HAVE THE SUPREME WEAPONS.

2159
01:16:27,667 --> 01:16:29,433
AH, TURN RUSH LIMBAUGH OFF.

2160
01:16:29,500 --> 01:16:30,733
YEAH.

2161
01:16:30,800 --> 01:16:32,833
♪♪

2162
01:16:32,900 --> 01:16:36,633
[BETTY]
SOMEHOW, I FEEL THAT
I'VE ALWAYS KNOWN YOU,

2163
01:16:36,700 --> 01:16:38,267
THAT WE'VE NEVER BEEN APART.

2164
01:16:38,333 --> 01:16:40,233
BOY, THIS GUY CAN DO
A LOT OF GREAT VOICES.

2165
01:16:40,300 --> 01:16:43,167
MM-HMM.

2166
01:16:43,233 --> 01:16:44,967
[THOR]
YOU ARE THE SON OF OUR LEADER.

2167
01:16:45,033 --> 01:16:46,767
YOU REMEMBER
HOW TO COOK 'EM.

2168
01:16:46,833 --> 01:16:49,300
WHENEVER THERE'S A COP
BEATING UP A GUY,
I'LL BE THERE.

2169
01:16:49,367 --> 01:16:52,067
[BETTY]
YOU WON'T BE GOING BACK EVER,
WILL YOU?

2170
01:16:52,133 --> 01:16:54,233
TOMORROW IS ANOTHER DAY.

2171
01:16:54,300 --> 01:16:56,500
ASK NOT WHAT YOUR COUNTRY
CAN DO FOR YOU.

2172
01:16:56,567 --> 01:16:58,167
HOW DID HE GET
A WEAPON LIKE THAT?

2173
01:16:58,233 --> 01:17:00,367
MAKES ME THINK OF
WHAT THE KILLER USED.

2174
01:17:00,433 --> 01:17:01,667
GRANDPA, COULDN'T YOU
SIT IN BACK?

2175
01:17:01,733 --> 01:17:04,333
IT IS.
THE SAME THING.

2176
01:17:04,400 --> 01:17:08,000
BUT WHO IS HE? WHERE DID
HE COME FROM, ANYWAY?

2177
01:17:08,067 --> 01:17:11,667
FROM SOMEPLACE NONE OF US HAS
EVER HEARD OF BEFORE, JOE.

2178
01:17:11,733 --> 01:17:13,067
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

2179
01:17:13,133 --> 01:17:14,367
[SPEAKING MADE-UP CHINESE]

2180
01:17:14,433 --> 01:17:15,867
"CLAIRE"
FROM ANOTHER PLANET...

2181
01:17:15,933 --> 01:17:17,200
OH, SHE CAME FROM
PLANET CLAIRE.

2182
01:17:17,267 --> 01:17:18,733
FAR OUT IN SPACE.

2183
01:17:18,800 --> 01:17:20,033
HEY, WAIT A MINUTE.

2184
01:17:20,100 --> 01:17:21,867
BETTY, THIS IS
NO TIME TO BE JOKING.

2185
01:17:21,933 --> 01:17:23,133
I'M NOT JOKING.

2186
01:17:23,200 --> 01:17:24,267
I'M DOING IMPROV.

2187
01:17:24,333 --> 01:17:26,367
WHERE DO YOU THINK
THE MONSTER CAME FROM?

2188
01:17:26,433 --> 01:17:28,067
AND THE MAN WHO WAS
DOING ALL THE KILLING

2189
01:17:28,133 --> 01:17:29,800
AND THE UNHEARD-OF
WEAPON HE USED.

2190
01:17:29,867 --> 01:17:31,333
A BIG CRAB, SURE,
BUT A MAN FROM SPACE?

2191
01:17:31,400 --> 01:17:33,900
THEY CAME IN A SPACESHIP
OF SOME SORT,

2192
01:17:33,967 --> 01:17:36,533
WHATEVER THOSE PEOPLE TOLD YOU
THEY SAW LAST NIGHT.

2193
01:17:36,600 --> 01:17:38,667
THE FLYING SAUCER?

2194
01:17:38,733 --> 01:17:40,867
AND I THOUGHT THOSE PEOPLE WERE
SEEING THINGS.

2195
01:17:40,933 --> 01:17:43,133
YEAH, GOOD REPORTER.
REALLY LISTENS TO PEOPLE.

2196
01:17:43,200 --> 01:17:46,000
DEREK LOOKED INTO THE SKY
JUST BEFORE HE LEFT HERE.

2197
01:17:46,067 --> 01:17:47,700
LOOK TO THE SKY.

2198
01:17:47,767 --> 01:17:52,533
SOMEHOW, HE COULD TELL
THAT MORE ARE ON THE WAY.

2199
01:17:52,600 --> 01:17:54,233
WHAT A FRUITCAKE.

2200
01:17:54,300 --> 01:17:56,467
[HIGH-PITCHED PINGING]

2201
01:17:56,533 --> 01:17:59,467
[SINGING TO THE TUNE
OF LEAVE IT TO BEAVER]

2202
01:17:59,533 --> 01:18:01,867
WHOA, IT LOOKS LIKE IT
TOOK 'EM ALL NIGHT TO GET HOME.

2203
01:18:01,933 --> 01:18:03,000
♪♪

2204
01:18:03,067 --> 01:18:05,200
AH, CRIPES, I NEED A NAP.

2205
01:18:05,267 --> 01:18:06,433
I HAVEN'T HAD ONE
IN 45 MINUTES.

2206
01:18:06,500 --> 01:18:09,333
HE MUST BE IN THE HOUSE.
THERE'S OUR CAR.

2207
01:18:09,400 --> 01:18:12,000
♪♪

2208
01:18:12,067 --> 01:18:13,200
[GASPS]

2209
01:18:13,267 --> 01:18:14,600
♪♪

2210
01:18:14,667 --> 01:18:15,967
DEREK!

2211
01:18:16,033 --> 01:18:18,533
YOU TURNED INTO
BOBBY GOLDSBORO.

2212
01:18:18,600 --> 01:18:21,000
YOU KNOW, EVERYTHING
WORKS BUT THE SHOES

2213
01:18:21,067 --> 01:18:23,200
AND MAYBE THOSE GLOVES.

2214
01:18:23,267 --> 01:18:25,100
♪♪

2215
01:18:25,167 --> 01:18:26,533
GOOD-BYE, BETTY.

2216
01:18:26,600 --> 01:18:28,533
NO, DEREK, NO.

2217
01:18:28,600 --> 01:18:30,133
YOU ARE JOE?

2218
01:18:30,200 --> 01:18:31,400
I AM NOT.

2219
01:18:31,467 --> 01:18:33,667
I WANT YOU TO TAKE ME
SOMEWHERE IN YOUR VEHICLE.

2220
01:18:33,733 --> 01:18:34,900
DISNEYLAND.

2221
01:18:34,967 --> 01:18:35,900
WHAT MAKES YOU THINK I WILL?

2222
01:18:35,967 --> 01:18:37,133
YOU REFUSE TO TAKE ME?

2223
01:18:37,200 --> 01:18:39,833
THAT'S RIGHT.
I'M STAYING RIGHT HERE.

2224
01:18:39,900 --> 01:18:41,367
YOU WILL DO AS I SAY.

2225
01:18:41,433 --> 01:18:43,133
NO, DEREK,
THIS ISN'T YOU.

2226
01:18:43,200 --> 01:18:46,367
DO NOT INTERFERE, BETTY,
I BEG YOU. GET IN.

2227
01:18:46,433 --> 01:18:49,000
NO, WE CAN'T HAVE A PLOT TWIST
THIS LATE IN THE MOVIE.

2228
01:18:49,067 --> 01:18:51,267
[GROANS]

2229
01:18:51,333 --> 01:18:54,067
NOW, LISTEN, IF I
DON'T GET IN THAT CAR,
I'M GONNA REGRET IT,

2230
01:18:54,133 --> 01:18:56,400
MAYBE NOT TODAY, MAYBE
NOT TOMORROW, BUT SOON.

2231
01:18:56,467 --> 01:18:58,500
TAKE ME TO WHERE THEY ARE
KEEPING THE PRISONER.

2232
01:18:58,567 --> 01:18:59,500
THE KILLER?

2233
01:18:59,567 --> 01:19:00,500
NO, THE PRISONER.

2234
01:19:00,567 --> 01:19:01,567
HE'S AT GENERAL HOSPITAL,
BUT--

2235
01:19:01,633 --> 01:19:02,800
THEN TAKE ME THERE.

2236
01:19:02,867 --> 01:19:05,967
I WANT TO MEET LUKE
AND LAURA WHILE I'M THERE.

2237
01:19:06,033 --> 01:19:07,767
JOE, DON'T--THE DISINTEGRATOR,
IT WON'T--

2238
01:19:07,833 --> 01:19:08,800
BETTY!

2239
01:19:08,867 --> 01:19:10,233
NO RUN-ON SENTENCES.

2240
01:19:10,300 --> 01:19:14,133
TRUST ME, BETTY.
TRUST ME.

2241
01:19:14,200 --> 01:19:17,667
♪♪

2242
01:19:21,267 --> 01:19:22,500
OH, I LIKE THAT.

2243
01:19:22,567 --> 01:19:24,300
THEY RACE TO THE SCENE
BUT THEY PARK CAREFULLY.

2244
01:19:24,367 --> 01:19:25,833
THE PRISONER IS
IN THIS BUILDING?

2245
01:19:25,900 --> 01:19:28,567
LOOKS LIKE THEY HAVEN'T
TRANSFERRED HIM
TO CITY JAIL YET.

2246
01:19:28,633 --> 01:19:30,633
- WHAT ARE YOU PLANNING TO DO?
- NEVER MIND.

2247
01:19:30,700 --> 01:19:32,200
I'M GONNA TRY TO CATCH OSWALD
IN THE PARKING RAMP, BUT--

2248
01:19:32,267 --> 01:19:34,667
JUST GET OUT OF THE CAR
AND WALK IN FRONT OF ME.

2249
01:19:34,733 --> 01:19:38,767
♪♪

2250
01:19:38,833 --> 01:19:41,433
OKAY, NOW WET YOUR LIPS
AND WORK THAT BOOTY.

2251
01:19:41,500 --> 01:19:43,433
♪♪

2252
01:19:43,500 --> 01:19:46,300
I HAVE GOOD POSTURE,
I KNOW I DO.

2253
01:19:46,367 --> 01:19:49,333
♪♪

2254
01:19:49,400 --> 01:19:51,167
HEY, DO YOU MIND?

2255
01:19:51,233 --> 01:19:53,600
♪ DOO DOO DOO DOO DOO
DOO DOO DOO DOO ♪

2256
01:19:53,667 --> 01:19:58,900
DO NOT MOVE.
I WILL TAKE THE PRISONER.
GET THEIR GUNS.

2257
01:19:58,967 --> 01:20:02,867
THIS IS THE MOST INCOMPETENT
PRISONER TRANSFER
SINCE DALLAS '63.

2258
01:20:02,933 --> 01:20:06,433
HAND THEM TO ME.

2259
01:20:06,500 --> 01:20:08,700
NOW GET IN.

2260
01:20:08,767 --> 01:20:11,433
NOW DANCE! DANCE!
DO THE TWO-STEP!

2261
01:20:11,500 --> 01:20:13,567
[WHISTLING]

2262
01:20:13,633 --> 01:20:15,733
♪♪

2263
01:20:15,800 --> 01:20:17,500
JACK LALANNE, EVERYBODY,
JACK LALANNE.

2264
01:20:17,567 --> 01:20:18,500
[WHISTLING AND APPLAUDING]

2265
01:20:18,567 --> 01:20:19,500
WHERE'S ELAINE?

2266
01:20:19,567 --> 01:20:20,500
- ELAINE?
- ELAINE LALANNE.

2267
01:20:20,567 --> 01:20:21,967
SCOOCH OVER,
I'LL RIDE RAYGUN.

2268
01:20:22,033 --> 01:20:24,333
YOU FACE THE WALL.
KEEP YOUR HANDS ABOVE
YOUR HEADS.

2269
01:20:24,400 --> 01:20:27,467
OKAY, NOW, SHAKE 'EM!

2270
01:20:27,533 --> 01:20:30,667
I WAS STUPID, THOR.
VERY STUPID.

2271
01:20:30,733 --> 01:20:32,567
BUT THAT IS OVER.

2272
01:20:32,633 --> 01:20:35,733
WE ARE RETURNING TO
MEET THE SHIPS, TOGETHER.

2273
01:20:35,800 --> 01:20:38,000
WHY DO YOU LET THEM LIVE?
KILL THEM!

2274
01:20:38,067 --> 01:20:39,767
THERE IS NO NEED.

2275
01:20:39,833 --> 01:20:42,033
THEY WILL BE
DEAD SOON ENOUGH,

2276
01:20:42,100 --> 01:20:44,767
ALONG WITH EVERYTHING ELSE
ON THIS PLANET.

2277
01:20:44,833 --> 01:20:45,800
GO!

2278
01:20:45,867 --> 01:20:47,900
LIKE YOU'VE NEVER
"GOED" BEFORE.

2279
01:20:47,967 --> 01:20:48,900
♪♪

2280
01:20:48,967 --> 01:20:50,400
WHAT'S YOUR DREAM, GRAMPS?

2281
01:20:50,467 --> 01:20:51,433
[AIR RAID SIREN BLARES]

2282
01:20:51,500 --> 01:20:53,700
UH, FIRST WEDNESDAY
OF THE MONTH.

2283
01:20:53,767 --> 01:20:56,400
SHIPS OF AN ALIEN SOURCE ARE
APPROACHING FROM THE SKY.

2284
01:20:56,467 --> 01:20:59,267
RADIO CONTACT HAS BEEN ATTEMPTED
BUT CANNOT BE ESTABLISHED.

2285
01:20:59,333 --> 01:21:03,400
INSTRUCTIONS ARE TO PREPARE
FOR AN ATTACK BY AN UNKNOWN
ENEMY.

2286
01:21:03,467 --> 01:21:05,867
[AIR RAID SIREN CONTINUES]

2287
01:21:05,933 --> 01:21:09,167
CHILDREN LOSE THE ABILITY
TO WALK.

2288
01:21:09,233 --> 01:21:10,567
OH, CRIPES, LOOK AT THAT.

2289
01:21:10,633 --> 01:21:13,233
I'LL NEVER GET MY BULBS IN.

2290
01:21:13,300 --> 01:21:15,267
HOLD ME.

2291
01:21:15,333 --> 01:21:19,000
♪♪

2292
01:21:19,067 --> 01:21:22,167
SURE IS PRETTY
UP HERE, EH? HEH HEH.

2293
01:21:22,233 --> 01:21:24,400
WHAT MADE YOU THINK HE WAS
COMING HERE?

2294
01:21:24,467 --> 01:21:26,333
[ALL YAWN]

2295
01:21:26,400 --> 01:21:27,533
BECAUSE THEY'RE COMING.

2296
01:21:27,600 --> 01:21:28,733
TO TAKE ME AWAY, HA HA.

2297
01:21:28,800 --> 01:21:31,167
HE TOLD ME THEY'D BE COMING.

2298
01:21:31,233 --> 01:21:34,200
HE TOLD ME HE WOULDN'T GO BACK
WITH THEM, THAT HE'D STAY.

2299
01:21:34,267 --> 01:21:36,533
IT LOOKS LIKE GRANDPA'S GOT
AN ELABORATE NETWORK OF
TRUSSES UNDER THAT SWEATER.

2300
01:21:36,600 --> 01:21:38,100
THAT HE WANTED TO STAY.

2301
01:21:38,167 --> 01:21:40,600
BETTY, LET ME
TAKE YOU BACK HOME.

2302
01:21:40,667 --> 01:21:43,767
NO, GRANDPA, LOOK.
HERE COMES JOE'S CAR!

2303
01:21:43,833 --> 01:21:47,167
AND AS ALWAYS, THERE'S PLENTY OF
FREE PARKING AT THE QUARRY.

2304
01:21:47,233 --> 01:21:48,600
MM-HMM.

2305
01:21:48,667 --> 01:21:52,367
♪♪

2306
01:21:52,433 --> 01:21:54,867
THE MOVIE REALLY PICKS UP
FROM HERE, DOESN'T IT?

2307
01:21:54,933 --> 01:21:57,433
EVERYBODY GETS TO BE
A HOSTAGE IN THIS MOVIE.

2308
01:21:57,500 --> 01:22:01,567
♪♪

2309
01:22:01,633 --> 01:22:04,600
BETTY, GRAMPS,
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

2310
01:22:04,667 --> 01:22:06,167
WHY DO YOU CONCERN
YOURSELF WITH THEM?

2311
01:22:06,233 --> 01:22:07,367
DESTROY THEM!

2312
01:22:07,433 --> 01:22:08,967
WHY, THOR?

2313
01:22:09,033 --> 01:22:10,967
THEY CANNOT CHANGE
WHAT IS GOING TO HAPPEN.

2314
01:22:11,033 --> 01:22:12,967
WHAT IS GOING
TO HAPPEN, DEREK?

2315
01:22:13,033 --> 01:22:14,667
SUBDIVISIONS--
INEVITABLE.

2316
01:22:14,733 --> 01:22:16,300
WALMARTS, MEGA-MALL--
LOTS OF THEM.

2317
01:22:16,367 --> 01:22:17,367
YOU MUST UNDERSTAND.

2318
01:22:17,433 --> 01:22:18,633
I'M A MAGIC MAN.

2319
01:22:18,700 --> 01:22:24,033
DEATH...MUST COME TO ALL.
SOONER TO SOME.

2320
01:22:24,100 --> 01:22:25,800
LATER TO OTHERS.

2321
01:22:25,867 --> 01:22:27,333
SCARECROW, I'LL MISS YOU
LEAST OF ALL.

2322
01:22:27,400 --> 01:22:28,600
[HIGH-PITCHED PINGING]

2323
01:22:28,667 --> 01:22:29,933
THE GUIDE SHIP
IS ABOUT TO LAND.

2324
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:31,033
WE MUST GO TO MEET IT.

2325
01:22:31,100 --> 01:22:32,400
YOU PROMISED, DEREK!

2326
01:22:32,467 --> 01:22:34,333
DON'T YOU REMEMBER
YOUR PROMISE?

2327
01:22:34,400 --> 01:22:36,067
HERE'S YOUR STUPID RING BACK.

2328
01:22:36,133 --> 01:22:37,900
I HAVE NOT FORGOTTEN IT.

2329
01:22:37,967 --> 01:22:40,900
I HAD MY FEELERS CROSSED.

2330
01:22:40,967 --> 01:22:44,967
BUT, UH-- I, UH--
WHAT? OH. OOH.

2331
01:22:45,033 --> 01:22:48,400
[HIGH-PITCHED PINGING]

2332
01:22:48,467 --> 01:22:50,600
HE CALLED THAT
THE GUIDE SHIP.

2333
01:22:50,667 --> 01:22:52,033
YEAH, AND THEY CALL
THE WIND MARIAH.

2334
01:22:52,100 --> 01:22:54,433
AND IT LOOKS LIKE THERE ARE
100 MORE STILL IN THE SKY.

2335
01:22:54,500 --> 01:22:56,733
- WHAT ARE THEY GOING TO DO?
- DEREK TOLD ME.

2336
01:22:56,800 --> 01:22:58,433
I WISH WE COULD PAN
OVER THERE, BUT, YOU KNOW...

2337
01:22:58,500 --> 01:23:02,267
THE OTHER SHIPS ARE LOADED
WITH THOUSANDS OF THOSE
HORRIBLE CREATURES,

2338
01:23:02,333 --> 01:23:04,867
LIKE THE ONE
DEREK KILLED TODAY.

2339
01:23:04,933 --> 01:23:06,333
WHY ARE THEY
BRINGING THEM HERE?

2340
01:23:06,400 --> 01:23:08,367
FOR A MR. STEAK
SUMMERTIME BAKE AND CLAMBAKE.

2341
01:23:08,433 --> 01:23:11,867
TO RAISE, FOR FOOD
A SAFE DISTANCE FROM
THEIR OWN PEOPLE.

2342
01:23:11,933 --> 01:23:14,333
AND THEY DON'T CARE
WHAT HAPPENS TO US?

2343
01:23:14,400 --> 01:23:16,700
DEREK CARED.

2344
01:23:16,767 --> 01:23:20,633
HE WANTED TO MAKE
THE EARTH HIS HOME.

2345
01:23:20,700 --> 01:23:22,933
HE PROMISED
HE WOULD NEVER LEAVE.

2346
01:23:23,000 --> 01:23:25,567
OH, YOUR PROBLEMS ARE THE MOST
IMPORTANT, AREN'T THEY?

2347
01:23:25,633 --> 01:23:28,800
[CRYING]
OH, JOE!

2348
01:23:28,867 --> 01:23:31,167
OH, HEY, JOE.

2349
01:23:31,233 --> 01:23:33,700
I WOULD HAVE USED THE
DISINTEGRATOR ON THEM,

2350
01:23:33,767 --> 01:23:36,167
BUT IT WILL NOT FUNCTION
WITHOUT ENERGY SUPPLY.

2351
01:23:36,233 --> 01:23:37,333
YOU COULDA.
DIDN'T WANNA.

2352
01:23:37,400 --> 01:23:39,567
IT WAS DAMAGED
WHEN YOU CRASHED.

2353
01:23:39,633 --> 01:23:41,133
I HAD TO BLUFF WITH IT.

2354
01:23:41,200 --> 01:23:42,800
IT IS JUST AS WELL.

2355
01:23:42,867 --> 01:23:44,100
I SOUND LIKE
GILBERT GOTTFRIED.

2356
01:23:44,167 --> 01:23:46,767
THEY WILL BE THE FIRST VICTIMS
OF THE GARGON HERDS.

2357
01:23:46,833 --> 01:23:47,833
[ELECTRONIC HUMMING]

2358
01:23:47,900 --> 01:23:51,033
OH, YOUR HAIR'S DONE,
MRS. ANDERSON.

2359
01:23:51,100 --> 01:23:54,667
OH, GREAT,
IT'S MR. TORTURE AGAIN.

2360
01:23:54,733 --> 01:23:56,900
SO YOU WERE ABLE TO
BRING HIM BACK, THOR.

2361
01:23:56,967 --> 01:23:57,900
[ALL]
TORTURE!

2362
01:23:57,967 --> 01:23:59,533
HE...BROUGHT ME.

2363
01:23:59,600 --> 01:24:02,933
I AM SORRY I...
ACTED THE WAY I DID.

2364
01:24:03,000 --> 01:24:04,933
I AM READY TO TAKE MY
PUNISHMENT.

2365
01:24:05,000 --> 01:24:07,833
THERE WILL BE
NO PUNISHMENT, MY SON.

2366
01:24:07,900 --> 01:24:09,667
[WHISTLES]

2367
01:24:09,733 --> 01:24:12,767
OH, WELL, THERE'S GOT TO
BE AT LEAST TWO MORE RUSSIAN
AVIATORS IN THAT THING.

2368
01:24:12,833 --> 01:24:14,233
YOU ARE MY FATHER?

2369
01:24:14,300 --> 01:24:15,933
I AM.

2370
01:24:16,000 --> 01:24:18,400
I HAVE WATCHED YOUR PROGRESS
SINCE YOU WERE BORN.

2371
01:24:18,467 --> 01:24:20,667
YOU HAVE EXCELLED
IN ALL THINGS.

2372
01:24:20,733 --> 01:24:22,067
GIVE ME THAT BEARD!

2373
01:24:22,133 --> 01:24:23,767
I WAS MOST DISAPPOINTED TO LEARN
THAT YOU HAD DESERTED.

2374
01:24:23,833 --> 01:24:26,900
I CAME THIS TRIP HOPING
I WOULD FIND YOU HAD RETURNED.

2375
01:24:26,967 --> 01:24:28,133
GOT ANY COUGH DROPS, DAD?

2376
01:24:28,200 --> 01:24:31,067
HAS WHAT I HAVE DONE NOT
DISQUALIFIED ME?

2377
01:24:31,133 --> 01:24:32,433
AM I STILL TO--

2378
01:24:32,500 --> 01:24:34,533
YOU ARE BACK.
THAT IS ALL THAT MATTERS.

2379
01:24:34,600 --> 01:24:35,767
WE'LL KILL
THE FATTED CALF NOW.

2380
01:24:35,833 --> 01:24:37,533
YOUR MISTAKES WERE MADE
BECAUSE OF THAT BOOK.

2381
01:24:37,600 --> 01:24:40,267
IT BLURRED YOUR MIND,
BUT ONLY TEMPORARILY.

2382
01:24:40,333 --> 01:24:41,700
WHAT? OH!

2383
01:24:41,767 --> 01:24:43,767
HOW IS IT YOU ARE ABLE
TO LEAVE THE PLANET?

2384
01:24:43,833 --> 01:24:45,200
IT'S A SPACESHIP
AND YOU JUST SORT OF--

2385
01:24:45,267 --> 01:24:47,333
WILL NOT THE GOVERNMENT
STRUCTURE COLLAPSE
IN YOUR ABSENCE?

2386
01:24:47,400 --> 01:24:49,167
WE WILL RETURN IMMEDIATELY,

2387
01:24:49,233 --> 01:24:51,967
AS SOON AS THE GARGONS
ARE UNLOADED FROM
THE FLEET OF SHIPS.

2388
01:24:52,033 --> 01:24:54,367
THE PEOPLE ARE UNAWARE
THAT I AM GONE.

2389
01:24:54,433 --> 01:24:56,567
YES, WE MUST LEAVE QUICKLY.

2390
01:24:56,633 --> 01:24:58,467
IF YOUR ABSENCE
WERE DISCOVERED,

2391
01:24:58,533 --> 01:25:01,533
IT WOULD LIKELY SPARK THE
BEGINNING OF A REVOLUTION.

2392
01:25:01,600 --> 01:25:04,100
I AM NOT THE ONLY ONE
WHO HAD THAT BOOK, FATHER.

2393
01:25:04,167 --> 01:25:09,400
YES, I KNOW, AND YOU WILL
HELP IN TRACKING DOWN OTHERS
WHO MAY HAVE SUCH BOOKS.

2394
01:25:09,467 --> 01:25:11,333
YES, I-- I SEE THE FLEET IS
APPROACHING.

2395
01:25:11,400 --> 01:25:13,067
MADE YOU LOOK.

2396
01:25:13,133 --> 01:25:15,767
THEY ARE FLYING FROM RADIO
SIGNALS FROM THE GUIDE SHIP,
ARE THEY NOT?

2397
01:25:15,833 --> 01:25:17,167
JUST A LITTLE TORTURE!

2398
01:25:17,233 --> 01:25:19,733
LET ME BE THE ONE TO
DIRECT THEM IN FOR LANDING.

2399
01:25:19,800 --> 01:25:23,067
CAPTAIN, ARE THE SHIPS
CLOSE ENOUGH TO RECEIVE
THEIR LANDING SIGNALS?

2400
01:25:23,133 --> 01:25:24,233
MOMENTARILY, BUT--

2401
01:25:24,300 --> 01:25:25,600
THEN GO BELOW, DEREK.

2402
01:25:25,667 --> 01:25:27,467
YOU WILL BRING THEM IN.

2403
01:25:27,533 --> 01:25:30,500
I'M CONVINCED
HE'S TURNED BAD.

2404
01:25:30,567 --> 01:25:33,467
YEAH, BUT--
BUT WHAT ABOUT TORTURE?

2405
01:25:33,533 --> 01:25:37,567
SAFELY, I'LL JUST BE
GUIDING THEM IN. HA!
NO CRASHING. HA!

2406
01:25:37,633 --> 01:25:38,900
OH.

2407
01:25:38,967 --> 01:25:42,833
SUCKERS.
SO LONG, SCREW YA,
SEE YOU IN ST. LOUYA.

2408
01:25:42,900 --> 01:25:46,333
DEREK, WHAT ARE YOU DOING?
UNBOLT THE HATCH!

2409
01:25:46,400 --> 01:25:47,367
[ELECTRONIC BEEPING]

2410
01:25:47,433 --> 01:25:49,967
MOM, IS THAT YOU
MAKING THAT NOISE?

2411
01:25:50,033 --> 01:25:52,633
LOOKS LIKE DEREK
WENT IN FIRST AND CLOSED
THE ENTRANCE WAY.

2412
01:25:52,700 --> 01:25:54,367
ARE WE STILL IN THIS MOVIE?

2413
01:25:54,433 --> 01:25:57,400
WHATEVER'S IN THE SKY,
THEY'RE GETTING MIGHTY CLOSE.

2414
01:25:57,467 --> 01:25:59,267
DEREK HAS SOME PLAN.

2415
01:25:59,333 --> 01:26:02,033
HE'S NOT DOING WHAT
THEY WANT HIM TO, I'M SURE.

2416
01:26:02,100 --> 01:26:03,233
[ELECTRONIC BEEPING]

2417
01:26:03,300 --> 01:26:05,000
OH, KARAOKE. I'D LIKE TO
SING RHINESTONE COWBOY.

2418
01:26:05,067 --> 01:26:07,500
MASTER CONTROL TO FLEET,
MASTER CONTROL TO FLEET.

2419
01:26:07,567 --> 01:26:12,100
INCREASE SPEED.
SET FLIGHT PATTERN
TO MINUS .08.

2420
01:26:12,167 --> 01:26:13,333
[LEADER]
DEREK, I COMMAND YOU!
DO NOT DO THIS!

2421
01:26:13,400 --> 01:26:15,467
- INCREASE SPEED.
- OPEN THIS HATCH AT ONCE!

2422
01:26:15,533 --> 01:26:18,267
THE SHIPS SEEM TO BE CONVERGING
AND INCREASING THEIR SPEED.

2423
01:26:18,333 --> 01:26:19,500
THEY CANNOT LAND!

2424
01:26:19,567 --> 01:26:21,300
HE DOES NOT PLAN TO HAVE
THEM LAND, BUT CRASH!

2425
01:26:21,367 --> 01:26:22,567
THEY'RE COMING RIGHT AT US!

2426
01:26:22,633 --> 01:26:25,100
DEREK'S DOING IT.
THAT'S WHAT HE PLANNED!

2427
01:26:25,167 --> 01:26:27,967
BUT HE'S INSIDE THERE!
HE'LL BE KILLED TOO!

2428
01:26:28,033 --> 01:26:29,800
GET DOWN,
INSIDE THE CAVE!

2429
01:26:29,867 --> 01:26:31,433
OH, LORD,
LET IT BE QUICK.

2430
01:26:31,500 --> 01:26:34,033
[LEADER]
DEREK, MY SON! THINK,
THINK OF WHAT YOU ARE DOING!

2431
01:26:34,100 --> 01:26:36,033
TURN THE SHIPS AROUND
BEFORE IT IS TOO LATE!

2432
01:26:36,100 --> 01:26:37,600
OH, BITE ME, DAD,
YOU'RE SO EMBARRASSING!

2433
01:26:37,667 --> 01:26:39,367
HOLD COURSE STEADY.

2434
01:26:39,433 --> 01:26:41,800
[HIGH-PITCHED PINGING]

2435
01:26:41,867 --> 01:26:46,833
[RUMBLING AND WHOOSHING]

2436
01:26:46,900 --> 01:26:50,167
THEY TURNED IT
INTO MOUNT VESUVIUS.

2437
01:26:50,233 --> 01:26:52,367
[RUMBLING DIES DOWN]

2438
01:26:52,433 --> 01:26:53,567
KINGSFORD TONIGHT.

2439
01:26:53,633 --> 01:26:55,300
[FIRE CRACKLING]

2440
01:26:55,367 --> 01:26:59,000
AH, THE FOLEY MAN'S
FRYING UP A BURGER.

2441
01:26:59,067 --> 01:27:02,300
OH, CRIMINY, THERE'S LITTLE
CHUNKS OF DEREK EVERYWHERE.

2442
01:27:02,367 --> 01:27:04,367
YECCH.

2443
01:27:04,433 --> 01:27:07,133
EH, TOSS SPARKY INTO A BAG.
LET'S GET OUT OF HERE.

2444
01:27:07,200 --> 01:27:10,767
IT'S BEAUTIFUL UP HERE,
ISN'T IT?

2445
01:27:10,833 --> 01:27:12,700
♪♪

2446
01:27:12,767 --> 01:27:15,233
JOE, DO YOU WANT TO
GET BACK TOGETHER?

2447
01:27:15,300 --> 01:27:18,733
♪♪

2448
01:27:18,800 --> 01:27:22,167
♪ SOMEWHERE ♪

2449
01:27:22,233 --> 01:27:25,000
♪♪

2450
01:27:25,067 --> 01:27:26,833
- IT'S HIS GRADUATION PHOTO.
- WOW.

2451
01:27:26,900 --> 01:27:32,433
I SHALL MAKE THE EARTH
MY HOME, AND I SHALL
NEVER, NEVER LEAVE IT.

2452
01:27:32,500 --> 01:27:33,700
YOU KNOW, HE FIRST
HAD ONE TAKEN WITH
HIS HOCKEY UNIFORM,

2453
01:27:33,767 --> 01:27:35,700
BUT HE OPTED FOR THAT ONE.

2454
01:27:35,767 --> 01:27:38,233
SING US OUT OF HERE,
DEREK!

2455
01:27:38,300 --> 01:27:41,133
♪ DOO DOO DOO DOO DOO ♪

2456
01:27:41,200 --> 01:27:44,300
MANY OF THE MERCURY PLAYERS
HAVE NEVER BEEN IN FILMS BEFORE.

2457
01:27:44,367 --> 01:27:46,900
HERE ARE SOME OF THEM.

2458
01:27:46,967 --> 01:27:49,633
OH, LET'S GO HOME.
I'VE GOT A ROOM TO RENT OUT.

2459
01:27:49,700 --> 01:27:52,633
LOOK TO THIS DAY,
YOUNG GRADUATE,

2460
01:27:52,700 --> 01:27:56,033
AS YOU MOVE ON
INTO YOUR NEW LIFE.

2461
01:27:56,100 --> 01:28:02,967
♪♪

2462
01:28:03,033 --> 01:28:10,967
MECHANICAL WHIRRING]

2463
01:28:11,033 --> 01:28:13,000
IN TODAY'S EXPERIMENT,

2464
01:28:13,067 --> 01:28:16,867
OUR ALIEN TEENAGER'S
SLENDERIZING ATTRACTIVE
SPACE GARB

2465
01:28:16,933 --> 01:28:22,800
IS OBVIOUSLY A CLEVER
COMBINATION OF $30 OFF-THE-RACK
FLEET FARM COVERALLS

2466
01:28:22,867 --> 01:28:24,867
AND JUST THE RIGHT AMOUNT
OF DUCT TAPE.

2467
01:28:24,933 --> 01:28:29,867
WELL, OUR FALL LINE IS OUT,
AND WEREN'T WE JUST THE
TEENSIEST BIT INSPIRED

2468
01:28:29,933 --> 01:28:31,100
BY TODAY'S EXPERIMENT?

2469
01:28:31,167 --> 01:28:32,267
- MM-HMM.
- YOU BET.

2470
01:28:32,333 --> 01:28:33,433
[LAUGHS]

2471
01:28:33,500 --> 01:28:35,067
SO, CAMBOT,
OUR FIRST MODEL, PLEASE?

2472
01:28:35,133 --> 01:28:36,533
[CLEARS THROAT]

2473
01:28:36,600 --> 01:28:39,800
INSPIRED BY
THE PRACTICAL FRIVOLITY
OF A DONNA KARAN,

2474
01:28:39,867 --> 01:28:42,033
HERE'S JOEL, CAVORTING
IN A PEPPY JUMPER

2475
01:28:42,100 --> 01:28:44,100
ACCENTED WITH
RED DUCT TAPE PIPING

2476
01:28:44,167 --> 01:28:46,333
FOR THE RIGHT AMOUNT OF
COME HITHER SENSUALITY.

2477
01:28:46,400 --> 01:28:50,300
I'VE TAKEN A DARING APPROACH
FOR OUR FETCHING LAD,
EH, MR. CROW?

2478
01:28:50,367 --> 01:28:52,233
OUI, OUI, MONSIEUR.

2479
01:28:52,300 --> 01:28:55,933
BUT WAIT, ISN'T THAT GADABOUT
GADFLY TOM SERVO

2480
01:28:56,000 --> 01:28:58,533
IN MY CALF-LENGTH TUNIC
WITH OPAQUE LEGGINGS

2481
01:28:58,600 --> 01:29:02,667
STRIPED WITH A TEASING
SMACK OF BRIGHT BUT SERIOUS
PERMA-SEAL GAFFER TAPE?

2482
01:29:02,733 --> 01:29:03,933
[LAUGHS]

2483
01:29:04,000 --> 01:29:06,133
WELL, NOW,
I WANTED TO SEE CROW

2484
01:29:06,200 --> 01:29:09,633
IN SOMETHING A LITTLE CO-ED
THAT ABSOLUTELY SCREAMS FALL,

2485
01:29:09,700 --> 01:29:11,733
AND BY GOLLY,
DIDN'T I GET IT?

2486
01:29:11,800 --> 01:29:15,800
COVERALL MEETS POLO IN THIS
RUGGED TAPE-STRIPED
RUGGER JERSEY,

2487
01:29:15,867 --> 01:29:18,267
WITH A KHAKI PANT AND
A TOUCH OF MERRY OLD ENGLAND.

2488
01:29:18,333 --> 01:29:19,467
EH, WHAT?

2489
01:29:19,533 --> 01:29:21,667
WHAT? WHAT?
OH! OH! MY TURN.
[CLEARS THROAT]

2490
01:29:21,733 --> 01:29:23,767
AND JUST IN TIME
FOR THE CRUISE SEASON,

2491
01:29:23,833 --> 01:29:26,900
AND OUR LITTLE CRUISER
SPORTS MY SASSY NAUTICAL THEME

2492
01:29:26,967 --> 01:29:29,633
IN A NAVY COVERALL
WITH WHITE GAFFER PIPING.

2493
01:29:29,700 --> 01:29:32,267
IT'S GUSSETED FOR AN EASY FEEL,
AND GUESS WHAT?

2494
01:29:32,333 --> 01:29:34,900
BELLBOTTOMS ARE BACK,
AND JUST IN TIME.

2495
01:29:34,967 --> 01:29:37,533
WELL, YOU CAN SWAB MY DECK
ANYTIME, SAILOR.

2496
01:29:37,600 --> 01:29:39,500
BY THE BY, YOU WERE A DREAM
AT THE SHOOT SESSION.

2497
01:29:39,567 --> 01:29:41,467
I'LL WORK WITH YOU
ANY OLD TIME.

2498
01:29:41,533 --> 01:29:43,400
WELL, FROM SHIP TO SHORE,
TOMMY.

2499
01:29:43,467 --> 01:29:46,200
NOW, HOW MANY TIMES
HAS THIS HAPPENED TO YOU?

2500
01:29:46,267 --> 01:29:49,133
DINNER, MR. PRESIDENT?
TONIGHT?

2501
01:29:49,200 --> 01:29:50,600
WHY, SURE!

2502
01:29:50,667 --> 01:29:51,800
NOW, WHAT DO YOU DO?

2503
01:29:51,867 --> 01:29:53,367
MY VERSATILE BLACK COTTON
BROADCLOTH

2504
01:29:53,433 --> 01:29:56,033
WITH SHINY GLOSS
DUCT-TAPE LAPELS AND ACCENTS

2505
01:29:56,100 --> 01:29:58,667
COMES TO THE RESCUE
WITH OUR LITTLE INGENUE.

2506
01:29:58,733 --> 01:30:01,500
FROM CHAOS TO KENNEBUNKPORT
IN MINUTES.

2507
01:30:01,567 --> 01:30:03,233
AND JUST IN TIME.

2508
01:30:03,300 --> 01:30:07,700
EVENING MAY BE TOM'S,
BUT THE NIGHT BELONGS TO CROW.

2509
01:30:07,767 --> 01:30:09,800
WOW, MY EYES
CAN'T HELP BUT TURN

2510
01:30:09,867 --> 01:30:12,567
AT THE SIGHT OF THIS
MAGNIFICENT LITTLE NOTHING.

2511
01:30:12,633 --> 01:30:15,667
YES, IT'S THE CLASSIC
JOE NAMATH NETTED
SLINGSHOT HOOP.

2512
01:30:15,733 --> 01:30:18,467
JOEL, JOEL, JOEL,
JOEL-- CAMBOT! YEAH,
THAT'S ENOUGH, THAT'S ENOUGH!

2513
01:30:18,533 --> 01:30:19,467
UH, JOEL, COME ON.

2514
01:30:19,533 --> 01:30:20,667
WHAT? WHAT?

2515
01:30:20,733 --> 01:30:22,500
I THOUGHT WE AGREED
NOT TO SHOW THAT ONE.

2516
01:30:22,567 --> 01:30:25,233
UH, THINGS GOT A LITTLE CARRIED
AWAY AT THE PHOTO SESSION.

2517
01:30:25,300 --> 01:30:30,667
WE WERE DISCUSSING JFK
THE FILM, AND ONE THING LED
TO ANOTHER AND--HA HA! WELL!

2518
01:30:30,733 --> 01:30:33,733
HONEY, IF YOU'VE GOT IT,
FLAUNT IT, YOU KNOW?

2519
01:30:33,800 --> 01:30:35,400
WELL, LET'S DO A LETTER,
OKAY?

2520
01:30:35,467 --> 01:30:36,867
YEAH, LET'S READ A LETTER,
SHALL WE?

2521
01:30:36,933 --> 01:30:37,900
I THOUGHT YOU
LOOKED VERY, VERY--

2522
01:30:37,967 --> 01:30:40,600
WELL, THIS ONE SAYS,
"DEAR JOE..."

2523
01:30:40,667 --> 01:30:43,100
UH, LET'S PUT THIS UP
ON STILL STORY, CAMBOT.

2524
01:30:43,167 --> 01:30:47,767
IT SAYS, "MY 'WHO'
FAMILY LIKES YOUR SHOWS,
'EXEPT' MY MOM.

2525
01:30:47,833 --> 01:30:49,933
"SHE HATES THE JOKES
YOU MAKE.

2526
01:30:50,000 --> 01:30:53,767
"WE ALL ARE FANS
'EXEPT' FOR HER.

2527
01:30:53,833 --> 01:30:55,100
"WHAT SHOULD WE DO.

2528
01:30:55,167 --> 01:30:58,167
THE AHMADI'S,
SAN JOSE, CA."

2529
01:30:58,233 --> 01:31:00,700
AND IT SHOWS
AN UNHAPPY MOM.

2530
01:31:00,767 --> 01:31:02,867
JUST TELL MOM TO WAIT FOR
LAWRENCE WELK TO COME BACK.

2531
01:31:02,933 --> 01:31:04,867
OOH, WHAT A BURN.

2532
01:31:04,933 --> 01:31:05,867
THAT'S SOMEBODY'S MOTHER.

2533
01:31:05,933 --> 01:31:06,900
SCORCH.

2534
01:31:06,967 --> 01:31:08,033
THIS NEXT ONE COMES FROM--

2535
01:31:08,100 --> 01:31:09,567
I'LL PUT IT UP
ON THE STILL STORY--

2536
01:31:09,633 --> 01:31:13,433
THE GAMERA TEAM,
UNIVERSITY OF KENTUCKY
COLLEGE OF MEDICINE.

2537
01:31:13,500 --> 01:31:16,367
"DEAR JOEL, 'CROWE,'
TOM SERVO, AND GYPSY:

2538
01:31:16,433 --> 01:31:19,567
"A NUMBER OF US HERE ON EARTH
AT THE UNIVERSITY OF KENTUCKY
COLLEGE OF MEDI--"

2539
01:31:19,633 --> 01:31:23,933
STOP IT. "WERE GREATLY
INSPIRED BY THE GAMERA MOVIES
SHOWN LAST YEAR ON MST.

2540
01:31:24,000 --> 01:31:28,300
"SO INSPIRED, IN FACT, THAT WE
NAMED OUR PEDIATRICS WARD TEAM
AFTER GAMERA HIMSELF

2541
01:31:28,367 --> 01:31:31,100
AND BECAME
'THE GAMERA TEAM.'"

2542
01:31:31,167 --> 01:31:32,600
AND LET'S SHOW
A PICTURE OF THEM.

2543
01:31:32,667 --> 01:31:34,300
AND THAT'S SOME
OF THE YOUNG--

2544
01:31:34,367 --> 01:31:35,467
NOT VERY GOOD.

2545
01:31:35,533 --> 01:31:37,533
- THEY'LL BE DOCTORS SOMEDAY.
- NO, IT'S FINE.

2546
01:31:37,600 --> 01:31:39,033
I FEEL SECURE AND SAFE,
KNOWING THAT THEY'RE GONNA BE

2547
01:31:39,100 --> 01:31:40,600
PRACTICING MEDICINE
ON HUMAN BEINGS.

2548
01:31:40,667 --> 01:31:41,833
WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIRS?

2549
01:31:41,900 --> 01:31:44,333
[LAUGHS]
AND THEN THE--
AND THEN THE CLAM SAYS,

2550
01:31:44,400 --> 01:31:46,233
"I THOUGHT
I WAS A BIVALVE."

2551
01:31:46,300 --> 01:31:48,067
[LAUGHS]

2552
01:31:48,133 --> 01:31:50,667
OH, I SEE
YOU'VE HEARD THAT ONE.

2553
01:31:50,733 --> 01:31:52,467
OH.
EXCUSE ME, DEAR.

2554
01:31:52,533 --> 01:31:55,833
JOEL, I WAS
JUST ENTERTAINING.

2555
01:31:55,900 --> 01:31:59,300
UNTIL NEXT TIME, UH...

2556
01:31:59,367 --> 01:32:01,633
POUR THE WINE AND THEN
PUSH THE BUTTON, LOUIE.

2557
01:32:01,700 --> 01:32:04,200
OUI, OUI, MONSIEUR.

2558
01:32:04,267 --> 01:32:06,700
[LAUGHS]

2559
01:32:06,767 --> 01:32:08,967
HELP ME.

2560
01:32:09,033 --> 01:32:11,767
SO, HAVE I TOLD YOU
I HAVE A MAN UP IN SPACE?

2561
01:32:11,833 --> 01:32:15,767
NO, LITERALLY, I HAVE
A MAN UP IN SPACE.

2562
01:32:15,833 --> 01:32:23,767
♪♪

2563
01:33:18,933 --> 01:33:20,633
WHEN WE RETURN
TO OUR PLANET,

2564
01:33:20,700 --> 01:33:23,433
THE HIGH COURT MAY WELL
SENTENCE YOU TO TORTURE!
